{"level":30,"time":1776978853703,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01NFfVgDTqBD7r4hJs7iHVnX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a comprehensive grouping file about overhead electric line clearances. Let me understand what this covers:\n\n**Grouping Focus**: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n\n**Key Points**:\n- 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement\n- 15-foot radial clearance from distribution conductors\n- 16-18 feet vertical clearance for driveways\n- Various clearances for different facilities (buildings, fences, trees, etc.)\n- Must measure from outside conductor, not pole\n- 48-hour notification requirement\n\n**Checklist Items**: There are 47 checklist items (EL-1.1 through EL-1.47) covering various clearance requirements.\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Read the project README to identify document IDs and what sheets are available\n2. Check facts.md to understand applicability\n3. Review relevant sheets and their guides/blocks\n4. Evaluate each checklist item\n5. Return only fail and not-verifiable findings\n\nLet me start by reading the project README to understand what's available.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8111,"cache_read_input_tokens":23654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8111,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11ce902f-86c5-4003-b16c-9143da511761","uuid":"322f7a6a-0d9d-4a2b-8426-0c5d37f64b62"}
