{"level":30,"time":1776978854093,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Qmhgkwc3d8exfjJWZsuWcZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Okay, so I have the grouping file. This is about tree clearances from overhead electric lines. There are 15 checklist items (EL-2.1 through EL-2.15) that cover:\n\n1. Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 ft of distribution\n2. Non-utility-compatible trees within 50 ft of transmission\n3. Large trees (40+ ft) within 25 ft of distribution\n4. Large trees (40+ ft) within 50 ft of transmission\n5. Trees in transmission easement boundaries\n6. Trees within 10 ft of utility poles\n7. Trees within 10 ft of pad-mounted equipment\n8. Trees within 5 ft of underground equipment\n9. Trees within 20 ft of underground equipment without root barriers\n10. Plant legend doesn't identify species\n11. Large trees not differentiated\n12. Tree clearances measured from pole centerline instead of conductor\n13. Tree clearances measured from canopy instead of trunk\n14. Trees not shown on landscape plan relative to overhead facilities\n15. Trees in prohibited zones without Austin Energy approval\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Check if this grouping applies to the project (is there overhead electric infrastructure?)\n2. Find and review the relevant documents (landscape plan, site plan, plant schedule, utility plan, grading plan)\n3. Evaluate each checklist item\n\nLet me start by reading the README.md to understand the project and find the document IDs.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3569,"cache_read_input_tokens":23654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3569,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_man