{"level":30,"time":1776978855230,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01SPsNmTRsSYoRQqQASZTM8H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I've read the grouping file. This is a comprehensive review of clearances from overhead electric lines. Let me understand the key points:\n\n**Grouping Overview:**\n- ID: 1 (from filename \"1.md\")\n- Subject: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n- Contains 47 checklist items (EL-1.1 through EL-1.47)\n\n**Key Requirements:**\n1. 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead conductors\n2. 15-foot radial clearance from distribution primary and neutral conductors\n3. 16-18 feet vertical clearance for driveways/parking depending on truck traffic\n4. 10 lateral feet from overhead distribution conductors for tree placement\n5. 50 lateral feet from transmission conductors for tree placement\n6. Various specific requirements for fences, retaining walls, etc.\n\n**Documents to Review:**\n- Site Plan Sheets\n- Building Elevation Sheets\n- Section/Profile Exhibits\n- Survey Data\n- Landscape Plans\n- Utility Plans\n- Cover Sheet\n\nNow I need to:\n1. Check the project README to understand what site plan documents are available\n2. Check facts.md to see what infrastructure exists\n3. Review relevant sheets from the site plan\n4. Evaluate each checklist item\n\nLet me start by reading the project README and facts.md.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8142,"cache_read_input_tokens":23654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8142,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8920d43-e944-47ba-ad17-2e6340f