{"level":30,"time":1776978858150,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01MG7Ark8z8vicNCbEuf3zFY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a good understanding of the grouping. Let me understand what I need to do:\n\n**Grouping 1: Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines**\n\nThis grouping covers clearance requirements between overhead electric distribution/transmission facilities and proposed site features (buildings, fences, retaining walls, driveways, parking, etc.).\n\nKey regulatory thresholds:\n- 7.5 feet horizontal sky-to-ground clearance from overhead primary, neutral, and secondary conductors\n- 15-foot radius clearance from overhead distribution primary and neutral conductors\n- 16 feet minimum vertical clearance for driveways/parking without truck traffic\n- 18 feet minimum vertical clearance for roads/streets/areas with truck traffic\n- 10 lateral feet from overhead distribution conductors for tree placement\n- 30-40 lateral feet (50 ft per UCM § 1.10.10.4) from overhead transmission conductors for tree placement\n- 10-foot radial clearance for construction working clearances from energized overhead lines\n\n**Project Context:**\n- Valley View Townhomes - 39 multi-family townhome units, 8 buildings\n- Site area: ~2.16 acres (with discrepancies noted)\n- Address: 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, TX 78704\n- Zoning: MF-2 (Multi-Family Residence — Medium Density)\n\n**Applicability Check:**\nFrom facts.md, I need to determine if there are overhead electric facilities on or adjacent to the site. Looking at the Documents to Review section and the checklist items, I need to review:\n- Sheet 21: Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n- Site plan sheets for overhead pole/conductor locations\n- Building elevation sheets for clearances\n- Utility plans for electric facility locations\n- Landscape plans for tree placement near electric facilities\n\nLet me now read the electrical design plan sheet guide to see what's documented.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":7955,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8310,"cache_read_input_tokens":23654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8310,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eda7f2a1-6294-41b6-8e72-831ed9038702","uuid":"6f7d0e3b-bde5-43e7-8035-9e143a9a5ae9"}
