{"level":30,"time":1776978859754,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016tGeNaL36RuV9nLUKs2TVL","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 21 — Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n     2→\n     3→Layout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Scale: 1\" = 20'\n    11→*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88\n    12→*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88\n    13→*   Bldg. 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n    14→*   Bldg. 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    15→*   Bldg. 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    16→*   Bldg. 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    17→*   Bldg. 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n    18→*   Bldg. 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n    19→*   Bldg. 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n    20→*   Bldg. 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    21→*   Private Domestic Water Branches: 2\" HDPE\n    22→*   Private Wastewater Branches: 6\" PVC\n    23→*   Geologist inspection trench depth threshold: > 5 feet\n    24→\n    25→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 3: drawing — Main Electrical Site Plan**\n    28→    The central site plan detailing the layout of Buildings 1 through 8, including their individual units, square footages, and Finished Floor Elevations (FFEs). The drawing illustrates the routing of underground electric lines, and the specific placement of electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meters. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, routing of electrical lines, and proximity of utility boxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    31→    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    34→    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    37→    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    40→    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    43→    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    46→    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    49→    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    52→    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n    53→\n    54→---\n    55→\n    56→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    57→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eda7f2a1-6294-41b6-8e72-831ed9038702","uuid":"f6fc5658-f54a-485f-a19f-8dc484d44573","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 21 — Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n\nLayout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Scale: 1\" = 20'\n*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   Bldg. 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n*   Bldg. 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n*   Bldg. 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Private Domestic Water Branches: 2\" HDPE\n*   Private Wastewater Branches: 6\" PVC\n*   Geologist inspection trench depth threshold: > 5 feet\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 3: drawing — Main Electrical Site Plan**\n    The central site plan detailing the layout of Buildings 1 through 8, including their individual units, square footages, and Finished Floor Elevations (FFEs). The drawing illustrates the routing of underground electric lines, and the specific placement of electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meters. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, routing of electrical lines, and proximity of utility boxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n\n*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n\n*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n\n*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n\n*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":57,"startLine":1,"totalLines":57}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776978859756,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TCJPJNqbWtFgkhbyBY3zii","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 21 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 2: diagram — A graphic scale bar showing distances of 0, 20, and 40 feet, along with the text 'Scale 1\" = 20''. A north arrow is also present above the scale bar.\n     4→\n     5→[Graphic scale bar showing distances 0, 20, 40]\n     6→Scale 1\" = 20'\n     7→[North arrow pointing upwards and slightly to the right]\n     8→\n     9→## Block 3: drawing — This block contains a detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n    10→\n    11→A detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n    12→\n    13→## Block 4: notes — This block contains 'Utility Notes' detailing contractor responsibilities regarding existing utilities and specific requirements for private domestic water and wastewater branches. Below the notes are disclaimers about the application not verifying all data and the reliance on record information for existing utilities.\n    14→\n    15→**Utility Notes**\n    16→1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n    17→2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n    18→3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n    19→4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n    20→\n    21→Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n    22→\n    23→The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n    24→\n    25→## Block 5: notes — A small block containing text that references another sheet for profile information.\n    26→\n    27→See Sht. 19\n    28→for Profile\n    29→\n    30→## Block 6: notes — A block containing a 'Tree List' reference stating 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.' Below it is a 'Note' regarding a Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule that requires trenching over 5 feet deep to be inspected by a geologist.\n    31→\n    32→**Tree List**\n    33→Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n    34→\n    35→**Note**\n    36→This project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n    37→\n    38→## Block 7: notes — A block listing two benchmarks (B.M. #1 and B.M. #2) with descriptions indicating they are mag nails set in asphalt, along with their respective elevations in NAVD 88 (GEOID 18).\n    39→\n    40→**Benchmarks**\n    41→B.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    42→Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    43→\n    44→B.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\n    45→Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n    46→\n    47→## Block 12: text_block — A block providing the legal description of the property, identifying it as Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision.\n    48→\n    49→**Legal Description**\n    50→Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n    51→\n    52→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eda7f2a1-6294-41b6-8e72-831ed9038702","uuid":"705e2d30-7917-4175-aedc-994741a70bde","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 21 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 2: diagram — A graphic scale bar showing distances of 0, 20, and 40 feet, along with the text 'Scale 1\" = 20''. A north arrow is also present above the scale bar.\n\n[Graphic scale bar showing distances 0, 20, 40]\nScale 1\" = 20'\n[North arrow pointing upwards and slightly to the right]\n\n## Block 3: drawing — This block contains a detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n\nA detailed site plan showing multiple buildings (Bldg. 1 to Bldg. 8) and their respective units, with FFE (Finished Floor Elevation) and square footage information. The plan includes electrical elements such as transformers, pull boxes, underground electric lines, and electrical meters. Additionally, the plan shows topography lines, property boundaries, and various easements like drainage, public utility, and wastewater. Information on adjoining properties is provided, detailing acreage, zoning, and use.\n\n## Block 4: notes — This block contains 'Utility Notes' detailing contractor responsibilities regarding existing utilities and specific requirements for private domestic water and wastewater branches. Below the notes are disclaimers about the application not verifying all data and the reliance on record information for existing utilities.\n\n**Utility Notes**\n1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n\nRelease of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n\nThe location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.\n\n## Block 5: notes — A small block containing text that references another sheet for profile information.\n\nSee Sht. 19\nfor Profile\n\n## Block 6: notes — A block containing a 'Tree List' reference stating 'Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.' Below it is a 'Note' regarding a Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule that requires trenching over 5 feet deep to be inspected by a geologist.\n\n**Tree List**\nRefer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\n\n**Note**\nThis project is subject to the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule (COA ECM 1.12.0 and COA Item No. 658S of the SSM) provision that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist (Texas P.G.) or a geologist's representative.\n\n## Block 7: notes — A block listing two benchmarks (B.M. #1 and B.M. #2) with descriptions indicating they are mag nails set in asphalt, along with their respective elevations in NAVD 88 (GEOID 18).\n\n**Benchmarks**\nB.M. #1 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 678.52' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\nB.M. #2 - Mag Nail Set in Asphalt\nElevation = 681.08' NAVD 88 (GEOID 18)\n\n## Block 12: text_block — A block providing the legal description of the property, identifying it as Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision.\n\n**Legal Description**\nLot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\n","numLines":52,"startLine":1,"totalLines":52}}}
