{"level":30,"time":1776978860971,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JpFLvQ2ZHoxYZN2DYJ1uQN","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 2 — Plat\n     2→\n     3→Subdivision plat map showing legal boundaries, easements, and signatures.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet displays the historical recorded plat for the Mecey Subdivision (Travis County, 1975), which serves as the base property boundary framework for the current Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to establish the legal boundary dimensions, right-of-way dedications, existing easements, and historical surveyor certifications for Lots 1 and 2 between Valley View Road and Clawson Road.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Property Recording:** Book 73, Page 76 (Filed December 11, 1975, at 2:10 PM)\n    11→*   **Original Survey Date:** August 20, 1975\n    12→*   **Base Property Reference:** Lot A, Trico Subdivision (Book 69, Page 14) / Volume 4916, Page 2385\n    13→*   **Scale:** 1\" = 100 Feet\n    14→*   **Curve Data:** Delta (Δ) = 31°25', Tangent (T) = 20.84', Radius (R) = 74.10', Long Chord (L.C.) = 39.12', Arc = 40.63'\n    15→*   **Surveyor:** Forrest B. Scott, Reg. Public Surveyor #399 (Austin, Texas)\n    16→*   **Current Project Address:** 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704\n    17→\n    18→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    19→\n    20→*   **Block 1: drawing — Mecey Subdivision Plat**\n    21→    The main drawing area containing the historical plat map, legal descriptions, owner's dedication, surveyor's certification, and approval signatures. \n    22→    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of Lot 1 and Lot 2, their orientation between Valley View Road and Clawson Road, and the location of drainage easements. \n    23→    *READ the block content for* precise boundary bearings/dimensions, curve data details, historical recording information, and standard legal declarations.\n    24→\n    25→*   **Blocks 7, 18: text_block — Project Title**\n    26→    Identifies the current project name, site address, and the specific title of this sheet.\n    27→    *READ the block content for* the project address (3759 Valley View Road) and sheet title (\"Plat\").\n    28→\n    29→*   **Blocks 9, 11: table/text_block — Project Details**\n    30→    Contains the project tracking details.\n    31→    *READ the block content for* the Project No. (RJ3 70496) and the initials for Design (CS, JR), CAD (JW, CS), and Review (JKR).\n    32→\n    33→*   **Blocks 2, 13: text_block — Sheet Indexing**\n    34→    *READ the block content for* the sheet number (Sheet 2 of 39) and tracking number (SP-2025-0126C).\n    35→\n    36→*   **Blocks 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    37→    Contains standard engineering firm contact info (Bleyl Engineering), office locations, the empty revision schedule, original layout size (24x36), and CAD file path plots. These can generally be skipped during technical review unless confirming the engineer of record's contact information.\n    38→\n    39→---\n    40→\n    41→- `block-1.md` — drawing: The main content area showing the plat for the Mecey Subdivision. This includes the legal descriptio\n    42→\n    43→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    44→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ccf6950-9428-47a1-a0e1-f1b6954e2e70","uuid":"09a780ec-914e-4b25-92c1-cf1068fdb1f3","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-02/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 2 — Plat\n\nSubdivision plat map showing legal boundaries, easements, and signatures.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet displays the historical recorded plat for the Mecey Subdivision (Travis County, 1975), which serves as the base property boundary framework for the current Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to establish the legal boundary dimensions, right-of-way dedications, existing easements, and historical surveyor certifications for Lots 1 and 2 between Valley View Road and Clawson Road.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Property Recording:** Book 73, Page 76 (Filed December 11, 1975, at 2:10 PM)\n*   **Original Survey Date:** August 20, 1975\n*   **Base Property Reference:** Lot A, Trico Subdivision (Book 69, Page 14) / Volume 4916, Page 2385\n*   **Scale:** 1\" = 100 Feet\n*   **Curve Data:** Delta (Δ) = 31°25', Tangent (T) = 20.84', Radius (R) = 74.10', Long Chord (L.C.) = 39.12', Arc = 40.63'\n*   **Surveyor:** Forrest B. Scott, Reg. Public Surveyor #399 (Austin, Texas)\n*   **Current Project Address:** 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas 78704\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: drawing — Mecey Subdivision Plat**\n    The main drawing area containing the historical plat map, legal descriptions, owner's dedication, surveyor's certification, and approval signatures. \n    *Use VISION to examine* the spatial layout of Lot 1 and Lot 2, their orientation between Valley View Road and Clawson Road, and the location of drainage easements. \n    *READ the block content for* precise boundary bearings/dimensions, curve data details, historical recording information, and standard legal declarations.\n\n*   **Blocks 7, 18: text_block — Project Title**\n    Identifies the current project name, site address, and the specific title of this sheet.\n    *READ the block content for* the project address (3759 Valley View Road) and sheet title (\"Plat\").\n\n*   **Blocks 9, 11: table/text_block — Project Details**\n    Contains the project tracking details.\n    *READ the block content for* the Project No. (RJ3 70496) and the initials for Design (CS, JR), CAD (JW, CS), and Review (JKR).\n\n*   **Blocks 2, 13: text_block — Sheet Indexing**\n    *READ the block content for* the sheet number (Sheet 2 of 39) and tracking number (SP-2025-0126C).\n\n*   **Blocks 3, 4, 5, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 15, 16, 17: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains standard engineering firm contact info (Bleyl Engineering), office locations, the empty revision schedule, original layout size (24x36), and CAD file path plots. These can generally be skipped during technical review unless confirming the engineer of record's contact information.\n\n---\n\n- `block-1.md` — drawing: The main content area showing the plat for the Mecey Subdivision. This includes the legal descriptio\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":44,"startLine":1,"totalLines":44}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776978860973,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018hESWa8qRaqpPmtGkx8Sz9","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 21 — Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n     2→\n     3→Layout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Scale: 1\" = 20'\n    11→*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88\n    12→*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88\n    13→*   Bldg. 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n    14→*   Bldg. 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    15→*   Bldg. 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    16→*   Bldg. 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    17→*   Bldg. 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n    18→*   Bldg. 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n    19→*   Bldg. 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n    20→*   Bldg. 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\n    21→*   Private Domestic Water Branches: 2\" HDPE\n    22→*   Private Wastewater Branches: 6\" PVC\n    23→*   Geologist inspection trench depth threshold: > 5 feet\n    24→\n    25→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 3: drawing — Main Electrical Site Plan**\n    28→    The central site plan detailing the layout of Buildings 1 through 8, including their individual units, square footages, and Finished Floor Elevations (FFEs). The drawing illustrates the routing of underground electric lines, and the specific placement of electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meters. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, routing of electrical lines, and proximity of utility boxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    31→    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    34→    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    37→    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    40→    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    43→    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    46→    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    49→    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    52→    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n    53→\n    54→---\n    55→\n    56→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    57→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ccf6950-9428-47a1-a0e1-f1b6954e2e70","uuid":"8d5097fb-4da1-4918-9e03-4fd14c5de414","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-21/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 21 — Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\n\nLayout of preliminary electrical design, routing, transformers, and meters.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the proposed electrical infrastructure, mapping the layout of underground electric lines, electrical meters, transformers, and pull boxes across the eight proposed buildings on the site.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Scale: 1\" = 20'\n*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   Bldg. 1: 3,290 sf, FFE = 687.50\n*   Bldg. 2: 4,830 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 3: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 4: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Bldg. 5: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 6: 3,290 sf, FFE = 683.0\n*   Bldg. 7: 4,144 sf, FFE = 685.0\n*   Bldg. 8: 4,997 sf, FFE = 685.50\n*   Private Domestic Water Branches: 2\" HDPE\n*   Private Wastewater Branches: 6\" PVC\n*   Geologist inspection trench depth threshold: > 5 feet\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 3: drawing — Main Electrical Site Plan**\n    The central site plan detailing the layout of Buildings 1 through 8, including their individual units, square footages, and Finished Floor Elevations (FFEs). The drawing illustrates the routing of underground electric lines, and the specific placement of electrical transformer pads, pull boxes, and meters. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, routing of electrical lines, and proximity of utility boxes to the building units; READ for specific unit numbers and adjacent easement dimensions.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Benchmarks**\n    Details for two survey control points (mag nails set in asphalt) used for elevation reference. READ the block content for exact benchmark descriptions and elevations (678.52' and 681.08').\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Utility Notes**\n    Provides contractor directives regarding the verification of existing utilities and specific material sizing for private domestic water (2\" HDPE) and wastewater (6\" PVC) branches. READ the block content for these specifications and liability disclaimers.\n\n*   **Block 7: notes — Tree List & Geologist Mitigation Rule**\n    Contains a cross-reference to landscape sheet 32 for the tree list, and a critical construction constraint regarding the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule. READ for the specific requirement that all trenching greater than 5 feet deep must be inspected by a geologist.\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Cross Reference**\n    A small note directing the reader to another sheet for profile information. READ to note the reference to Sheet 19.\n\n*   **Block 11: text_block — Legal Description**\n    Identifies the legal plat details of the subject property. READ for the subdivision name and recording details (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision Volume 73, Page 76).\n\n*   **Block 12: text_block — Title Block**\n    Specifies the sheet name and project location. READ to confirm the sheet is the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan for Valley View Townhomes.\n\n*   **Block 2: diagram — Scale and North Arrow**\n    Provides the graphic scale and orientation for the main drawing. VISION to understand the page orientation (North arrow pointing up-right) and confirm the 1\" = 20' scale.\n\n*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 10: various — Boilerplate & Administrative**\n    Contains standard project tracking and professional compliance elements, including the Texas 811 \"Call Before You Dig\" logo (Block 1), Bleyl Engineering firm contact info (Block 8), Jason K. Rodgers' professional engineer seal (Block 9), and sheet tracking information (Block 10). READ Block 10 for the specific sheet number (21 of 39).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":57,"startLine":1,"totalLines":57}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776978860974,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GLXd3jnfnnM3HfEDRXBzzV","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n     2→\n     3→Detailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n    11→*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n    12→*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n    13→*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n    14→*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n    15→*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n    16→*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n    17→*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n    18→*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n    19→*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n    20→*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n    21→\n    22→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    23→\n    24→*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    25→    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n    26→\n    27→*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    28→    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n    29→\n    30→*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    31→    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    34→    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n    35→\n    36→*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    37→    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n    38→\n    39→*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    40→    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n    41→\n    42→*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    43→    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n    44→\n    45→*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    46→    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n    47→\n    48→*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    49→    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n    50→\n    51→*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    52→    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n    53→\n    54→*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    55→    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n    56→\n    57→*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    58→    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n    59→\n    60→---\n    61→\n    62→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    63→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ccf6950-9428-47a1-a0e1-f1b6954e2e70","uuid":"e5b98733-c43c-4e1f-ba01-63a689eaa49b","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-09/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 9 — Site Plan\n\nDetailed site plan layout with associated building and parking data.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the primary Site Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project (Sheet 9 of 39). It illustrates the overall site layout, including the arrangement of eight multi-family residential buildings, internal driveways, parking, a detention pond, pedestrian walkways, and retaining walls, while providing comprehensive tabular data to verify compliance with zoning, area, coverage, height, and parking requirements.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   **Site Area:** 94,192 sf (2.162 acres)\n*   **Zoning:** MF-2/Multi-Family Low Density\n*   **Total Units:** 39 units (16 Two Bedroom, 23 Three Bedroom) across 8 buildings\n*   **Maximum Building Height:** 40' allowed; 36' - 1\" is the highest proposed (Building 3)\n*   **Impervious Cover:** 59% proposed (55,502 sf) vs 60% allowable\n*   **Building Coverage:** 34% proposed (32,296 sf) vs 50% allowable\n*   **Gross Floor Area:** 83,986 sf\n*   **Vehicle Parking:** 88 total spaces provided (10 surface, 78 garage)\n*   **Bicycle Parking:** 5 required; 41 provided (39 long term, 2 short term)\n*   **Accessibility Slopes:** Max parking slope 1:50; Max cross-slope 1:50; Max ramp slope 1:12\n*   **Benchmarks (NAVD 88):** BM #1 = 678.52'; BM #2 = 681.08'\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 1: drawing — Main Site Plan**\n    A comprehensive layout drawing of the property. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout of Buildings 1-8, the routing of internal driveways and concrete/decomposed granite walkways, the location of the biofiltration/detention pond in the northeast corner, and the placement of retaining walls around the site perimeter.\n\n*   **Block 16: table — Site Data Table**\n    A summary table of overall site metrics. READ the block content for exact values verifying zoning compliance, including site area, existing vs. proposed impervious cover percentages, allowable vs. proposed building coverage, and gross floor area.\n\n*   **Block 14: table — Building Data Table**\n    A breakdown of metrics per building. READ the block content for individual building types (4-, 5-, or 6-plexes), gross floor areas, building footprints, bedroom configurations, and total unit counts (39 total, maximum 3 stories).\n\n*   **Block 15: table — Building Height Table**\n    A summary of building heights for compliance checking. READ the block content for the average MSL, physical building heights (ranging from 33'-4.75\" to 36'-1\"), and verification that all buildings fall under the 40' allowable height limit.\n\n*   **Block 17: table — Site Area Calculation (MF-2)**\n    A calculation of required area based on unit types. READ the block content to verify that the 94,192 sf provided site area satisfies the 93,600 sf required for the 39 2+ bedroom units.\n\n*   **Block 8: notes — Parking Data**\n    A tabular summary of parking requirements. READ the block content for the breakdown of vehicle parking (surface vs. garage) and the exact counts for short-term and long-term bicycle parking spaces.\n\n*   **Block 10: notes — Site Plan Release Notes**\n    A list of administrative conditions for the site plan. READ the block content for compliance requirements regarding standard building codes, signage, utility providers, demolition, and right-of-way excavation permits.\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Accessibility Notes**\n    Design constraints for ADA compliance. READ the block content for specific, mandated slope tolerances for accessible parking spaces, cross-slopes, and ramps (e.g., max ramp slope of 1:12).\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Lighting Note & Figure 34**\n    Requirements for exterior lighting. READ for the requirement that all exterior lighting must be full cut-off and fully shielded per Subchapter E 2.5. Use VISION to review the four acceptable fixture profiles illustrated in Figure 34.\n\n*   **Block 6: notes — Fence Note**\n    Tree protection requirements. READ the block content for instructions mandating hand-digging of post holes within Critical Root Zones (CRZ) and the required application of 3-inch hardwood mulch.\n\n*   **Block 9: notes — Trash Collection Notes**\n    Rules for waste management. READ the block content for curbside unattended container restrictions and necessary enforcement signage requirements.\n\n*   **Blocks 3, 5, 7, 11, 12, 13: various — Administrative & Boilerplate Data**\n    Standard site plan identifiers and administrative data. READ for the legal description (Block 3), the specific benchmark elevations (Block 5), and general utility liability notes (Block 7). Use VISION to locate the graphic scale showing 1\" = 20' (Block 11), the Texas 811 call-before-you-dig logo (Block 12), and the engineer's seal dated 2/27/26 (Block 13).\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":63,"startLine":1,"totalLines":63}}}
