{"level":30,"time":1776978876528,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_012g5gynrG2dGJEB1oWWUmQi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have a complete picture of the landscape design. Let me summarize what I've learned:\n\n**Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations) Plant List:**\n- Shade Trees:\n  - 2 Live Oak (100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' HT minimum)\n  - 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal., 4\" cal., 16' HT minimum)\n  \n- Ornamental Trees:\n  - 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal., 2.5\" cal., 8' HT minimum)\n  - 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal., 2.5\" cal., 10' HT minimum)\n\n- Shrubs: Various (Dwarf Palmetto, Big Muhly, Gulf Muhly, Texas Sage, Dwarf Wax Myrtle)\n- Groundcovers: Obedient Plant, Frogfruit\n\nThese are all the NEW PROPOSED trees. The existing trees being preserved are listed in the Tree List (Sheet 32).\n\n**Key Finding About Overhead Electric:**\nSheet 31 mentions \"Overhead Electric (OHE)\" in the site plan drawing. Sheet 21 references that tree list is on Sheet 32.\n\nNow I need to examine the actual landscape plan (Sheet 31, Block 2) to see:\n1. Where overhead electric utilities are located\n2. Where proposed new trees are placed relative to the OHE\n3. Whether any trees are placed within restricted clearance zones\n\nLet me use the vision tool to examine the landscape plan more carefully.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4346,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8077,"cache_read_input_tokens":43168,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8077,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f27eabf-4e7e-4d33-b3eb-83a00ab44689","uuid":"8a0bc65f-0dcd-451b-bdc9-1ade88581af6"}
