{"level":30,"time":1776978888041,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan and identify: 1) All overhead electric lines (OHE) shown on the plan - trace their paths and note their locations across the site; 2) All tree symbols shown on the plan (circles and other symbols indicating tree locations) - note their specific locations and proximity to overhead electric lines; 3) The scale and dimensions; 4) Any transmission lines, poles, or major utility infrastructure. Focus on identifying where trees are positioned relative to overhead electric utilities.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776978899555,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan (Sheet 21) and provide detailed information about:\n\n1. **Transformer Pad Locations:** Identify and describe the exact location of each transformer pad shown on the plan (note building proximity, coordinates if available, or relative position). Note how many transformer pads are shown.\n\n2. **Transformer Pad Details:** For each transformer pad, identify:\n   - Dimensions (if shown)\n   - Equipment specifications (service type: single-phase or three-phase; oil-filled or dry-type)\n   - Access door orientation if visible\n   - Any dimension lines or distance callouts showing clearances to buildings, structures, or other features\n\n3. **Clearances Shown:** List any clearances explicitly dimensioned on the plan:\n   - Horizontal clearances from buildings, structures, parking areas, etc.\n   - Vertical clearances or niche configurations\n   - Separation from utilities (water, wastewater, storm drain, gas lines)\n   - Clearances from landscaping, fences, or other site features\n\n4. **Property Location:** Confirm whether transformer pad(s) are located entirely on private property or if they are close to property lines or easements. Note any easement boundaries shown.\n\n5. **Underground Utilities:** Identify the routing of underground electric lines to/from the transformer pads and any interactions with other utilities (water, wastewater, storm drain).\n\n6. **Parking and Circulation:** Note the proximity of transformer pad(s) to parking areas, vehicle circulation routes, or drive aisles. Identify if bollards are shown in the detail sheets or electrical plan.\n\n7. **Cross-References:** Note any references to detail sheets, electrical specifications, or Austin Energy Design approvals on the electrical plan sheet.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21 of 39), here is the information regarding your requested points:\n\n**1. Transformer Pad Locations**\nThere are exactly five (5) transformer pads identified on this plan, denoted by rectangular outlines along the blue electrical line routing, each with a leader line pointing to the label \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n*   **Pad 1:** Located in the northwest quadrant of the site, situated west of Building 1 and immediately south of the northernmost entrance drive aisle.\n*   **Pad 2:** Located on the western edge of the site, situated west of Building 2, between the building and the western property line / \"Sidewalk Easement\".\n*   **Pad 3:** Located in the southwest quadrant of the site, situated west of Building 8, between the building and the western property boundary.\n*   **Pad 4:** Located in the central portion of the site, situated east of Building 4 and west of Building 5, adjacent to an internal parking area.\n*   **Pad 5:** Located in the south-central portion of the site, situated east of Building 7 and west of Building 6, adjacent to an internal parking area.\n\n**2. Transformer Pad Details**\nThe plan provides only a schematic representation of the transformer pads.\n*   **Dimensions:** No specific dimensions (length x width) are shown for any of the pads on this sheet.\n*   **Equipment Specifications:** There are no notes or labels indicating service type (single-phase or three-phase) or equipment type (oil-filled or dry-type).\n*   **Access Door Orientation:** The graphical symbols are simple rectangles; no access door orientations are visible or indicated.\n*   **Dimension Lines/Clearances:** There are no dimension lines or distance callouts shown on or immediately adjacent to the transformer pad symbols to indicate size or clearances.\n\n**3. Clearances Shown**\nThere are **no explicit clearances dimensioned** on this plan sheet for the transformer pads.\n*   **Horizontal clearances:** While the pads are drawn physically separated from buildings and parking areas, no specific distances (e.g., \"10'\") are called out.\n*   **Vertical clearances:** None shown (this is a 2D plan view).\n*   **Separation from utilities:** The electrical lines cross other utilities, but specific clearance dimensions between the lines or pads and other utilities are not labeled.\n*   **Clearances from landscaping/fences:** No explicit dimension lines are provided for these features relative to the transformer pads.\n\n**4. Property Location**\nAll five transformer pads appear to be located entirely on private property within the main property boundary (indicated by the heavy dashed line with bearing/distance callouts, e.g., `S 62° 02' 28\" E 419.06'`).\n*   Pads 1, 2, and 3 are located relatively close to the western property line.\n*   A \"Sidewalk Easement\" runs along the outside of the western property line near Pads 2 and 3.\n*   Various \"P.U.E.\" (Public Utility Easement) areas are shown near the property boundaries, but the transformer pads are located inward from the main boundary lines.\n\n**5. Underground Utilities**\nThe underground electrical routing is prominently shown using a solid blue line.\n*   **Routing:** The primary connection point enters the site from the west (bottom left quadrant), labeled with a note pointing to the line: \"Underground Electric Line\". The line routes throughout the site connecting \"Electrical Pull Box\" locations to the \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations, and subsequently to banks of \"Electrical Meters\" located on or near the buildings.\n*   **Interactions:** The blue underground electric line crosses or runs in close proximity to several other utilities. For example, it crosses lines labeled \"W\" (Water), \"WW\" or \"S\" (Wastewater/Sewer), and \"SD\" (Storm Drain) at multiple points throughout the site to reach the various transformer pads and buildings.\n\n**6. Parking and Circulation**\n*   **Proximity:**\n    *   **Pad 1** is immediately adjacent to the main entrance/exit drive aisle.\n    *   **Pads 4 and 5** are located adjacent to head-in parking spaces within the internal circulation areas of the complex.\n    *   **Pads 2 and 3** are located behind buildings, separated from the main vehicular circulation areas.\n*   **Bollards:** There are no bollards explicitly shown or labeled near any of the transformer pads on this specific plan sheet.\n\n**7. Cross-References**\n*   **Detail Sheets:** The \"Utility Notes\" box in the bottom right corner references \"Detail 520-AW-01B\" and \"Detail 520-AW-01C\" regarding Private Domestic Water Branches and Private Wastewater Branches. However, there are **no cross-references to electrical detail sheets** for the transformer pads on this page.\n*   **Approvals:** There are no stamps or notes indicating Austin Energy Design approvals. The sheet is labeled \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\".","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1665,"outputTokens":1101,"totalTokens":4805,"reasoningTokens":2039},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertai