rosses or runs in close proximity to several other utilities. For example, it crosses lines labeled \"W\" (Water), \"WW\" or \"S\" (Wastewater/Sewer), and \"SD\" (Storm Drain) at multiple points throughout the site to reach the various transformer pads and buildings.\n\n**6. Parking and Circulation**\n*   **Proximity:**\n    *   **Pad 1** is immediately adjacent to the main entrance/exit drive aisle.\n    *   **Pads 4 and 5** are located adjacent to head-in parking spaces within the internal circulation areas of the complex.\n    *   **Pads 2 and 3** are located behind buildings, separated from the main vehicular circulation areas.\n*   **Bollards:** There are no bollards explicitly shown or labeled near any of the transformer pads on this specific plan sheet.\n\n**7. Cross-References**\n*   **Detail Sheets:** The \"Utility Notes\" box in the bottom right corner references \"Detail 520-AW-01B\" and \"Detail 520-AW-01C\" regarding Private Domestic Water Branches and Private Wastewater Branches. However, there are **no cross-references to electrical detail sheets** for the transformer pads on this page.\n*   **Approvals:** There are no stamps or notes indicating Austin Energy Design approvals. The sheet is labeled \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\"."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ccf6950-9428-47a1-a0e1-f1b6954e2e70","uuid":"d2b2e64f-b054-41e3-9cf5-b6a3c6710c86","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" (Sheet 21 of 39), here is the information regarding your requested points:\n\n**1. Transformer Pad Locations**\nThere are exactly five (5) transformer pads identified on this plan, denoted by rectangular outlines along the blue electrical line routing, each with a leader line pointing to the label \"Electrical Transformer Pad\".\n*   **Pad 1:** Located in the northwest quadrant of the site, situated west of Building 1 and immediately south of the northernmost e