REE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   **PL**: \"PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   **P**: \"PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n*   **M**: \"MITIGATION TREE\"\n\n*Approximate Locations of Proposed Trees:*\n*   **Western Edge (Left side, along Valley View Road)**: Several large proposed trees are located in the street yard buffer area (shaded region H-1). Labels visible include **SY/M** and **M**.\n*   **Northern Edge (Top)**: A row of proposed trees runs along the upper property boundary. Labels visible include **M** and **P/M**.\n*   **Eastern Edge (Right side)**: A row of proposed trees is located along the right boundary. Labels visible include **M** and **P/M**.\n*   **Southern Edge (Bottom)**: A row of approximately five to six proposed trees is planted along the bottom boundary. Most of these are labeled **M**.\n*   **Interior / Parking Areas**: There are a few trees located within the interior parking islands/peninsulas. One clearly visible label near the center top of the parking area is **PL/M**.\n\n**3. Proximity to Utilities**\n*   **Southern Boundary**: There is a significant proximity issue visible along the southern (bottom) boundary. A row of approximately five proposed trees (labeled **M**) is positioned directly along the \"-OHE-\" line. \n*   **Distance Estimate**: The center planting points (trunks) of these trees appear to be situated immediately adjacent to, or directly underneath, the overhead electric line. The large circles representing their proposed mature canopies heavily overlap the OHE line.\n\n**4. Electric Infrastructure Details**\n*   **Utility Poles**: There are small \"x\" marks located on the \"-OHE-\" line itself, which typically indicate utility pole locations in standard site plan symbology. There is also a distinct symbol consisting of a small circle with a cross/X through it near the bottom right corner of the OHE run, which may represent a primary pole.\n*   **Tra