{"level":30,"time":1776978910759,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":4,"prompt":"Are there any overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) marked on this existing conditions survey? If so, where are they located on the site? Check the entire drawing carefully for any overhead electric poles, conductors, or utility lines. Also note if there are any utility poles marked on the property or adjacent areas.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided site plan, yes, there are overhead utility lines and utility poles marked on the survey. \n\nAccording to the \"LEGEND\" located in the top left corner of the document, the linetype \"---O.H.U.L.---\" denotes an \"OVERHEAD UTILITY LINE.\"\n\nThese lines and associated poles are located in two primary areas on the drawing:\n\n1.  **Along Valley View Road (Left side of the drawing):**\n    *   An overhead utility line, indicated by a dashed line with the text **\"O.H.U.L.\"**, runs roughly parallel to the front property line along **\"VALLEY VIEW ROAD\"**.\n    *   There are utility poles indicated along this line. Near the bottom-left property corner (relative to the drawing orientation), there is a symbol labeled **\"UTILITY POLE\"**. Another pole is indicated near the top-left property corner along this same line, along with a line labeled **\"GUY WIRE\"**.\n\n2.  **Along the Northern/Eastern Boundary (Top side of the drawing):**\n    *   A second overhead utility line, also marked with the dashed **\"O.H.U.L.\"** linetype, runs parallel to the property boundary labeled **\"S63°03'28\"E 419.86'\"**.\n    *   This line appears to be located just outside the subject property boundary, situated on the adjacent property labeled **\"LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS\"**.\n    *   Multiple utility poles are marked along this line. Moving from left to right along that top boundary, there is a symbol labeled **\"UTILITY POLE\"** with an attached line labeled **\"GUY WIRE\"**, and further to the right, another symbol labeled **\"UTILITY POLE\"**.\n\nThere do not appear to be any O.H.U.L. lines crossing the interior of the lot over the proposed building slab area.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1377,"outputTokens":417,"totalTokens":3797,"reasoningTokens":2003},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1695804]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Are there any overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) marked on this existing conditions survey? If so, where are they located on the site? Check th