{"level":30,"time":1776978911106,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan and identify the following:\n\n1. Where are overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this plan? Describe their location(s) and routing across the site.\n2. What tree symbols are shown on the plan? Identify the locations of all proposed trees (indicated by circles or other tree symbols).\n3. Describe the proximity/spatial relationship between any proposed trees and the overhead electric lines. Are there trees near or under the OHE lines?\n4. Are there any dimension lines or distance callouts showing clearances between trees and overhead electric facilities?\n5. What is the overall distribution of trees across the site (north, south, east, west sections)?\n\nProvide specific location references such as \"southwest corner,\" \"along property line,\" \"near Building X,\" etc.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan, here are the detailed observations addressing your questions:\n\n**1. Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines Locations:**\nAn overhead electric line is explicitly identified on the plan. It is labeled as **\"---- OHE ----\"**.\n*   **Location/Routing:** This line is located exclusively along the southern edge of the site plan. It runs generally east-to-west, roughly parallel to the southern property line and the limits of construction (labeled \"LOC\"). It extends from the southwest portion of the site towards the southeast corner.\n\n**2. Proposed Tree Locations:**\nTrees are represented on the plan by circular symbols of varying diameters, many of which contain a central cross (\"+\") or specific hatch patterns. The key notes at the bottom right identify specific tree types like \"SY - STREET YARD TREE,\" \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE,\" \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE,\" and \"M - MITIGATION TREE.\"\nProposed trees are located in the following areas:\n*   **Northern Boundary:** A continuous row of large proposed trees (several labeled \"M\" and \"H-7\") spans the northern property line.\n*   **Western Boundary (Valley View Road):** A grouping of street yard trees (labeled \"SY\") is located along the curved western frontage.\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** A continuous row of trees runs north-to-south along the eastern property line.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** A row of trees is proposed along the southern property line.\n*   **Interior:** Several individual trees are located within parking lot islands (often near areas shaded and labeled \"H-4\" for Parking Lot Landscaping).\n\n**3. Proximity/Spatial Relationship Between Trees and OHE Lines:**\nThere is a close spatial relationship and apparent conflict between the proposed trees and the overhead electric lines along the southern boundary.\n*   Multiple tree symbols (specifically the circular symbols with a central \"+\", some associated with the \"M\" label) are placed directly in the path of the \"---- OHE ----\" line.\n*   Particularly in the southeast section of the property line, at least three tree symbols directly intersect or are positioned immediately underneath the indicated OHE line routing.\n\n**4. Dimension Lines and Clearances:**\n*   There are **no** dimension lines, distance callouts, or specific textual notes visible on this plan sheet that indicate horizontal or vertical clearances between the proposed trees and the overhead electric (\"OHE\") lines.\n\n**5. Overall Distribution of Trees:**\nThe overall distribution of trees is highly **perimeter-focused**. The landscaping strategy appears primarily dedicated to buffering and screening the edges of the property:\n*   Dense rows of trees outline the north, east, and south property boundaries.\n*   The west section features significant street yard landscaping along the public right-of-way.\n*   The interior distribution is sparse by comparison, limited to a few specific parking lot landscape islands situated between the buildings and parking areas.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1476,"outputTokens":617,"totalTokens":4029,"reasoningTokens":1936},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Landscape Plan and identify the following:\n\n1. Where are overhead electric (OHE) lines shown on this plan? Describe their location(s) and routing across the site.\n2. What tree symbols are shown on the plan? Identify the locations of all proposed trees (indicated by circles or other tree symbols).\n3. Describe the proximity/spatial relationship between any proposed trees and the overhead electric lines. Are there trees near or under the OHE lines?\n4. Are there any dimension lines or distance callouts showing clearances between trees and overhead electric facilities?\n5. What is the overall distribution of trees across the site (north, south, east, west sections)?\n\nProvide specific location references such as \"southwest corner,\" \"along property line,\" \"near Building X,\" etc."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-J3vn19MJE3jnKSOoGQiU5aWV","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 21:15:11 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::8vrwx-1776978886059-56f9238a826b"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan, here are the detailed observations addressing your questions:\n\n**1. Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines Locations:**\nAn overhead electric line is explicitly identified on the plan. It is labeled as **\"---- OHE ----\"**.\n*   **Location/Routing:** This line is loc