and **\"Bldg. 1\"**.\n*   **Location 2 (Southwest):** Located in the interior courtyard space, positioned south of **\"Bldg. 2\"** and west of **\"Bldg. 8\"**.\n*   **Location 3 (Northeast):** Located in the interior courtyard space, positioned east of **\"Bldg. 4\"** and south of **\"Bldg. 5\"**.\n*   **Location 4 (Southeast):** Located in the interior courtyard space, positioned east of **\"Bldg. 7\"** and south of **\"Bldg. 6\"**.\n\n**2. Transformer specifications:**\n*   **Pad dimensions:** No dimensions (e.g., 5'x5' or 10'x10') are labeled on or next to any of the transformer pad symbols.\n*   **Service type:** The plan does not specify the service type (e.g., single-phase, three-phase, kVA rating) for any of the transformers. The only text provided is the label **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**.\n\n**3. Clearances shown:**\n*   There are no dimension lines or textual notes indicating required clearance distances from the transformer pads to buildings, sidewalks, underground utilities, trees, or property lines on this drawing.\n\n**4. Access door orientation:**\n*   The transformer access door orientation is not indicated on the plan. The symbol used is a uniform square with an 'X' through it, with no directional markings indicating the front, back, or door swing.\n\n**5. Property location:**\n*   All four transformer pads appear to be located entirely on private property within the development site.\n*   While there are labeled easements on the perimeter (e.g., \"Sidewalk Easement\", \"5' P.U.E.\", \"15' Easement\"), the transformer pads themselves do not appear to be located directly on the property lines or within these designated perimeter utility easements.\n\n**6. Underground utilities:**\nThere are multiple other utility lines shown in proximity to the transformer locations, primarily indicated by dashed lines with letter abbreviations.\n*   **Water (\"W\"):** Water lines are shown running near all four transformer pad locations. The solid blue lines (representing proposed electrical routing) frequently cross these \"W\" lines.\n*   **Storm Drain (\"SD\"):** Storm drain lines and associated rectangular boxes (inlets) are located in the courtyards near Locations 2, 3, and 4. The electrical routing lines cross these \"SD\" lines in multiple places.\n*   **Wastewater/Sewer:** Near Location 1 (Northwest), there is an **\"Existing #13466 Wastewater MH\"** and an associated line.\n*   **Conflicts:** While the plan view (top-down) shows blue electrical lines crossing \"W\" and \"SD\" lines in numerous locations near the transformers, there are no specific profile views, callouts, or notes on this page indicating how vertical conflicts between these utilities will be resolved.\n\n**7. Parking and vehicle areas:**\n*   **Location 1 (Northwest):** This pad is located just south of a line labeled **\"Concrete Curb\"**, which appears to define the main entry drive from the street. It is situated in the landscaping space behind the curb.\n*   **Locations 2, 3, and 4:** These pads are located in the interior pedestrian/landscaped courtyards between the buildings and do not appear to be immediately adjacent to vehicular driveways or parking areas based on the visible linework.\n*   **Bollards:** There are no symbols, details, or notes indicating the placement of protective bollards around any of the transformer pads.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1560,"outputTokens":889,"totalTokens":4401,"reasoningTokens":1952},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCR