{"level":30,"time":1776978934393,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013EXutsPkxTdMfJrvV3YMpf","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 19 — Utility Tap Plan\n     2→\n     3→Utility tap plan showing proposed water and wastewater connections.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Utility Tap Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout and connection points for proposed water, wastewater, and storm drain lines across eight multi-family buildings. Its primary purpose is to define utility routing, drainage fixture unit (DFU) loads, pipe material specifications, and regulatory compliance notes for the site's wet utilities.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Private domestic water branches: 2\" HDPE service tubing\n    11→*   Private wastewater branches: 6\" PVC at a minimum 2.0% slope\n    12→*   Pressure reducing valve (PRV) set pressure threshold: 65 psi\n    13→*   Number of private fire hydrants on site: 1\n    14→*   Trench depth requiring geologist inspection: Greater than 5 feet\n    15→*   Drainage Fixture Units (DFUs): 4Plex = 136 DFUs, 5Plex = 170 DFUs, 6Plex = 204 DFUs\n    16→*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' (NAVD 88)\n    17→*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n    18→\n    19→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    20→\n    21→*   **Block 2**: The main site plan diagram showing buildings (Bldg. 1-8), utility routing (water, wastewater, storm drain), lift stations, cleanouts, and site topography. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, pipe routing, line lengths, and specific component locations.\n    22→*   **Block 1**: Legend defining the symbols and line types used for existing and proposed utilities (W, WW, RW, E, SD) in the main diagram. Use VISION to cross-reference symbols while reviewing Block 2.\n    23→*   **Block 13**: Utility notes specifying pipe materials and slopes for private domestic water and wastewater branches. READ for exact material sizes and installation standards.\n    24→*   **Block 7**: Drainage Fixture Unit Table breaking down the total DFU loads by building number and type (e.g., 4Plex, 5Plex, 6Plex). READ for specific sanitary load calculations.\n    25→*   **Block 17**: Benchmark data providing precise elevations and descriptions of vertical control points. READ for exact elevation values used for site grading and utility slopes.\n    26→*   **Block 10**: Water tap note outlining requirements for replacing existing Asbestos Cement (AC) pipe with Ductile Iron (DI) pipe and required hazardous disposal protocols. READ for regulatory compliance regarding existing AC lines.\n    27→*   **Block 11**: Special Services Division note mandating compliance with the Austin Fire Code for the site's private fire hydrant. READ for maintenance obligations and the exact private hydrant count.\n    28→*   **Block 5**: Technical note dictating the use of factory restrained joint pipes or mechanical joint restraint devices for all water line bends, tees, and valves. READ for specific structural requirements on water mains.\n    29→*   **Block 9**: PRV Note stipulating that any structure with water pressure at or above 65 psi must install a pressure reducing valve. READ for pressure management requirements.\n    30→*   **Block 19**: Geologist inspection requirement note triggered by the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule for deep trenching. READ for the specific trench depth threshold (5 feet).\n    31→*   **Blocks 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 14, 15, 16, 18, 20**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the project title block, engineering firm details, Texas 811 logo, legal description, disclaimers regarding utility locations, and a cross-reference to the landscape plan for trees. READ for general project administration and liability disclaimers if required.\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    36→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f2d0cbc-d0ea-481e-8f7b-51f5d8083c45","uuid":"22b774db-9607-4ee0-a8f5-8bd57378f49d","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-19/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 19 — Utility Tap Plan\n\nUtility tap plan showing proposed water and wastewater connections.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Utility Tap Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout and connection points for proposed water, wastewater, and storm drain lines across eight multi-family buildings. Its primary purpose is to define utility routing, drainage fixture unit (DFU) loads, pipe material specifications, and regulatory compliance notes for the site's wet utilities.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Private domestic water branches: 2\" HDPE service tubing\n*   Private wastewater branches: 6\" PVC at a minimum 2.0% slope\n*   Pressure reducing valve (PRV) set pressure threshold: 65 psi\n*   Number of private fire hydrants on site: 1\n*   Trench depth requiring geologist inspection: Greater than 5 feet\n*   Drainage Fixture Units (DFUs): 4Plex = 136 DFUs, 5Plex = 170 DFUs, 6Plex = 204 DFUs\n*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' (NAVD 88)\n*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2**: The main site plan diagram showing buildings (Bldg. 1-8), utility routing (water, wastewater, storm drain), lift stations, cleanouts, and site topography. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, pipe routing, line lengths, and specific component locations.\n*   **Block 1**: Legend defining the symbols and line types used for existing and proposed utilities (W, WW, RW, E, SD) in the main diagram. Use VISION to cross-reference symbols while reviewing Block 2.\n*   **Block 13**: Utility notes specifying pipe materials and slopes for private domestic water and wastewater branches. READ for exact material sizes and installation standards.\n*   **Block 7**: Drainage Fixture Unit Table breaking down the total DFU loads by building number and type (e.g., 4Plex, 5Plex, 6Plex). READ for specific sanitary load calculations.\n*   **Block 17**: Benchmark data providing precise elevations and descriptions of vertical control points. READ for exact elevation values used for site grading and utility slopes.\n*   **Block 10**: Water tap note outlining requirements for replacing existing Asbestos Cement (AC) pipe with Ductile Iron (DI) pipe and required hazardous disposal protocols. READ for regulatory compliance regarding existing AC lines.\n*   **Block 11**: Special Services Division note mandating compliance with the Austin Fire Code for the site's private fire hydrant. READ for maintenance obligations and the exact private hydrant count.\n*   **Block 5**: Technical note dictating the use of factory restrained joint pipes or mechanical joint restraint devices for all water line bends, tees, and valves. READ for specific structural requirements on water mains.\n*   **Block 9**: PRV Note stipulating that any structure with water pressure at or above 65 psi must install a pressure reducing valve. READ for pressure management requirements.\n*   **Block 19**: Geologist inspection requirement note triggered by the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule for deep trenching. READ for the specific trench depth threshold (5 feet).\n*   **Blocks 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 14, 15, 16, 18, 20**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the project title block, engineering firm details, Texas 811 logo, legal description, disclaimers regarding utility locations, and a cross-reference to the landscape plan for trees. READ for general project administration and liability disclaimers if required.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776978934395,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0117gFkxjEYx4b4GCqS3rf7o","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 12 — Storm Sewer Plan\n     2→\n     3→Displays the proposed storm sewer layout and drainage infrastructure details.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the proposed Storm Sewer Plan (Sheet 12 of 39) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's surface and subsurface drainage infrastructure, including the layout of storm sewer pipes, grate inlets, manholes, and junction boxes overlaid on the site grading and building footprints. \n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→*   **Scale**: 1\" = 20'\n    11→*   **Benchmarks**: BM #1 Elevation = 678.52' (NAVD 88), BM #2 Elevation = 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n    12→*   **ADA Specifications**: ADA Ramp maximum slope = 8.33%; Level Landing maximum slope = 2.00%\n    13→*   **Storm Sewer Pipes**: Drawing indicates extensive use of 12\", 18\", and 24\" HDPE pipe. Examples include:\n    14→    *   24\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 1.35% (e.g., lengths of 53.28 lf, 47.98 lf, 26.71 lf, 20.98 lf)\n    15→    *   18\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 0.50% (e.g., lengths of 71.10 lf, 63.17 lf, 61.27 lf)\n    16→    *   18\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 4.00% (e.g., lengths of 49.02 lf, 25.60 lf, 19.84 lf)\n    17→*   **Key Structures**:\n    18→    *   4'x4' Junction Box: Rim = 684.80, FL 24\" = 673.90\n    19→    *   SD Manhole (near Bldg 2): Rim = 684.71, FL 24\" = 675.47, FL 18\" = 675.57\n    20→    *   Multiple 18\" and 2'x2' Grate Inlets throughout the site (e.g., 2'x2' Grate Inlet Rim = 684.34, FL 24\" = 675.19)\n    21→*   **Building Sizes**: Examples include Bldg 2 (4,830 sf, FFE=685.50), Bldg 7 (4,144 sf, FFE=685.0), Bldg 8 (4,997 sf, FFE=685.50)\n    22→\n    23→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    24→\n    25→*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan Drawing**\n    26→    Contains the detailed layout of the storm sewer system, including pipe alignments, structure locations, existing/proposed contours, building footprints (Buildings 1-8), and property boundaries.\n    27→    *Use VISION to trace drainage flow paths, examine the spatial relationship between infrastructure and building footprints, and READ for specific pipe dimensions, slopes, and structure elevations.*\n    28→\n    29→*   **Block 10: seal — Title Block**\n    30→    Provides primary project identification (Valley View Townhomes, Austin, TX) and the engineering firm's information (Bleyl Engineering).\n    31→    *READ for project context and location.*\n    32→\n    33→*   **Block 3: notes — Benchmarks**\n    34→    Details the vertical control points used for the site plan, specifying the elevations of BM #1 and BM #2.\n    35→    *READ for exact survey elevation references.*\n    36→\n    37→*   **Block 4: notes — Legend**\n    38→    Defines the line types and symbols used on the drawing, such as existing/proposed contours, spot elevations, and limits of construction. It also notes maximum slopes for ADA ramps and landings.\n    39→    *READ for ADA constraints and symbol definitions, VISION to map these symbols onto the main drawing.*\n    40→\n    41→*   **Block 5: notes — Drainage & Curb Notes**\n    42→    Provides construction directions for curbs (catch vs. spill curbs) and administrative requirements for detention/filtration facility certification prior to obtaining a Certificate of Occupancy.\n    43→    *READ for compliance and curb grading requirements.*\n    44→\n    45→*   **Blocks 6, 7: notes — References & Legal Description**\n    46→    Provides the legal plat description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision) and points to Sheet 32 for the site's tree list.\n    47→    *READ to cross-reference property bounds or tree data.*\n    48→\n    49→*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 11, 12, 13, 14: various — Boilerplate, Scale & Administrative**\n    50→    Contains the engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), Texas 811 utility contact information, standard utility verification disclaimers, city review disclaimers, the drawing scale (1\" = 20'), project tracking numbers, and the sheet index (Sheet 12 of 39).\n    51→    *READ Block 12 to confirm the drawing scale; skip the rest unless auditing standard design metadata or disclaimers.*\n    52→\n    53→---\n    54→\n    55→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    56→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f2d0cbc-d0ea-481e-8f7b-51f5d8083c45","uuid":"11d0745f-7a0e-4d3b-859b-25839f556eb4","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-12/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 12 — Storm Sewer Plan\n\nDisplays the proposed storm sewer layout and drainage infrastructure details.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the proposed Storm Sewer Plan (Sheet 12 of 39) for the Valley View Townhomes project. Its primary purpose is to detail the site's surface and subsurface drainage infrastructure, including the layout of storm sewer pipes, grate inlets, manholes, and junction boxes overlaid on the site grading and building footprints. \n\n**Key values**:\n*   **Scale**: 1\" = 20'\n*   **Benchmarks**: BM #1 Elevation = 678.52' (NAVD 88), BM #2 Elevation = 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n*   **ADA Specifications**: ADA Ramp maximum slope = 8.33%; Level Landing maximum slope = 2.00%\n*   **Storm Sewer Pipes**: Drawing indicates extensive use of 12\", 18\", and 24\" HDPE pipe. Examples include:\n    *   24\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 1.35% (e.g., lengths of 53.28 lf, 47.98 lf, 26.71 lf, 20.98 lf)\n    *   18\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 0.50% (e.g., lengths of 71.10 lf, 63.17 lf, 61.27 lf)\n    *   18\" HDPE pipe runs sloped at 4.00% (e.g., lengths of 49.02 lf, 25.60 lf, 19.84 lf)\n*   **Key Structures**:\n    *   4'x4' Junction Box: Rim = 684.80, FL 24\" = 673.90\n    *   SD Manhole (near Bldg 2): Rim = 684.71, FL 24\" = 675.47, FL 18\" = 675.57\n    *   Multiple 18\" and 2'x2' Grate Inlets throughout the site (e.g., 2'x2' Grate Inlet Rim = 684.34, FL 24\" = 675.19)\n*   **Building Sizes**: Examples include Bldg 2 (4,830 sf, FFE=685.50), Bldg 7 (4,144 sf, FFE=685.0), Bldg 8 (4,997 sf, FFE=685.50)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 2: drawing — Main Site Plan Drawing**\n    Contains the detailed layout of the storm sewer system, including pipe alignments, structure locations, existing/proposed contours, building footprints (Buildings 1-8), and property boundaries.\n    *Use VISION to trace drainage flow paths, examine the spatial relationship between infrastructure and building footprints, and READ for specific pipe dimensions, slopes, and structure elevations.*\n\n*   **Block 10: seal — Title Block**\n    Provides primary project identification (Valley View Townhomes, Austin, TX) and the engineering firm's information (Bleyl Engineering).\n    *READ for project context and location.*\n\n*   **Block 3: notes — Benchmarks**\n    Details the vertical control points used for the site plan, specifying the elevations of BM #1 and BM #2.\n    *READ for exact survey elevation references.*\n\n*   **Block 4: notes — Legend**\n    Defines the line types and symbols used on the drawing, such as existing/proposed contours, spot elevations, and limits of construction. It also notes maximum slopes for ADA ramps and landings.\n    *READ for ADA constraints and symbol definitions, VISION to map these symbols onto the main drawing.*\n\n*   **Block 5: notes — Drainage & Curb Notes**\n    Provides construction directions for curbs (catch vs. spill curbs) and administrative requirements for detention/filtration facility certification prior to obtaining a Certificate of Occupancy.\n    *READ for compliance and curb grading requirements.*\n\n*   **Blocks 6, 7: notes — References & Legal Description**\n    Provides the legal plat description (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision) and points to Sheet 32 for the site's tree list.\n    *READ to cross-reference property bounds or tree data.*\n\n*   **Blocks 1, 8, 9, 11, 12, 13, 14: various — Boilerplate, Scale & Administrative**\n    Contains the engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), Texas 811 utility contact information, standard utility verification disclaimers, city review disclaimers, the drawing scale (1\" = 20'), project tracking numbers, and the sheet index (Sheet 12 of 39).\n    *READ Block 12 to confirm the drawing scale; skip the rest unless auditing standard design metadata or disclaimers.*\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":56,"startLine":1,"totalLines":56}}}
