etween Buildings 4 and 6.\n\n*(Note: There are also several locations labeled \"Electrical Meters\" distributed near the individual buildings).*\n\n**Relation to Overhead Utility Lines**\n*   **Valley View Road (Western Boundary):** An existing overhead utility line is indicated by a dashed line labeled \"OHE\" running north-south along Valley View Road. A proposed \"Underground Electric Line\" is shown connecting directly to a utility pole on this line (situated roughly midway along the western property frontage, south of the main entrance). This appears to be the primary feed for the site's proposed underground system.\n*   **Northern Boundary:** There is an existing overhead utility line indicated by a dashed line labeled \"OHE\" running east-west along the northern boundary. The proposed underground electrical infrastructure (blue line) runs roughly parallel to this boundary behind Buildings 1, 2, and 3, but the plan does not depict a direct connection point between the proposed underground system and the northern overhead line."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8920d43-e944-47ba-ad17-2e6340f56c7c","uuid":"49000e57-df55-4c67-8610-1644f20aded4","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided site plan document, here is the spatial layout of the proposed electrical infrastructure:\n\n**Scale**\nThe scale of the drawing is specified in the top right corner as **Scale 1\" = 20'**.\n\n**Spatial Layout of Proposed Electrical Infrastructure**\nThe proposed electrical infrastructure is denoted by solid blue lines and blue symbols (squares and rectangles) with accompanying callout labels. \n\n**1. Underground Electrical Lines**\n*   The primary routing of the proposed \"Underground Electric Line\" forms a continuous loop around the perimeter of the internal building clusters (Buildings 1 through 8).\n*   The line branches off to serve individual buildings, transformers, pull boxes, and meter banks throughout the site. \n\n**2. Electrical Transformers**\nThere are three identified \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" locations shown on the plan:\n*   **West side of Building 2:** Located near the northwest corner of Building 2, adjacent to the entrance drive.\n*   **West side of Building 8:** Located near the southwest corner of Building 8.\n*   **Between Buildings 4 and 6:** Located on the east side of the site, east of Building 4 (Unit 404) and north of Building 6 (Unit 601).\n\n**3. Electrical Pull Boxes**\nThere are multiple \"Electrical Pull Box\" locations placed along the underground routing. They are specifically labeled at the following locations:\n*   Northwest of Building 1 (near Unit 102).\n*   Northeast of Building 3 (near Unit 303).\n*   Southwest of Building 8 (near Unit 801).\n*   South of Building 7, near the southern boundary.\n*   Southeast of Building 6 (near Unit 603).\n*   Adjacent to the Electrical Transformer Pad located between Buildings 4 and 6.\n\n*(Note: There are also several locations labeled \"Electrical Meters\" distributed near the individual buildings).*\n\n**Relation to Overhead Utility Lines**\n*   **Valley View Road (Western Boundary):** An existing overhead utility line is indicated by a dashed line labeled \"OHE\" running north-south along Valley View Road. A proposed \"Underground Electric Line\" is shown connecting directly to a utility pole on this line (situated roughly midway along the western property frontage, south of the main entrance). This appears to be the primary feed for the site's proposed underground system.\n*   **Northern Boundary:** There is an existing overhead utility line indicated by a dashed line labeled \"OHE\" running east-west along the northern boundary. The proposed underground electrical infrastructure (blue line) runs roughly parallel to this boundary behind Buildings 1, 2, and 3, but the plan does not depict a direct connection point between the proposed underground system and the northern overhead line."}]}
