 are positioned immediately adjacent to or directly underneath the path of the overhead electric line. Specific labels located near the tree symbols along this overlapping path include **\"M\"** (identified in the Key Notes as \"MITIGATION TREE\") and **\"SY\"** (identified as \"STREET YARD TREE\").\n\n**3) Scale and Dimensions**\n*   The scale is explicitly stated in the bottom right corner of the drawing area.\n*   It reads exactly: **\"SCALE IN FEET (1\"=20'-0\")\"**\n*   Directly below this text is a graphic scale bar marked with intervals of **0, 10, 20,** and **50**.\n\n**4) Transmission Lines, Poles, or Major Utility Infrastructure**\n*   **Poles:** There are small symbols (circles/crosses) at the far left and right ends of the \"- OHE -\" line that likely represent utility poles, though they are not explicitly labeled with text like \"UP\" (Utility Pole) or \"PP\" (Power Pole).\n*   **Other Infrastructure:** \n    *   Underground storm drain lines are visible running horizontally through the central drive aisles/parking areas, labeled **\"- SD -\"**.\n    *   Major stormwater management infrastructure is detailed in the top right quadrant (northeast corner) of the site. Two shaded areas are explicitly labeled **\"SEDIMENTATION BASIN\"** and **\"FILTRATION BASIN\"**. \n*   No large-scale transmission towers or major substation infrastructure are depicted on this landscape plan sheet. The primary electrical utility concern shown regarding trees is the standard **\"- OHE -\"** distribution line along the southern boundary.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1412,"outputTokens":623,"totalTokens":4444,"reasoningTokens":2409},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission doc