{"level":30,"time":1776979215258,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the electrical design plan to identify overhead electric infrastructure. Please provide:\n\n1. **Overhead Electric Facilities**: Are there any overhead electric lines, conductors, poles, or transmission facilities shown on this electrical design plan? If yes, describe their location and any voltage/classification labels.\n\n2. **Voltage Classification**: Is the overhead electric infrastructure labeled with voltage (e.g., 12.47 kV for distribution, 69 kV+ for transmission)?\n\n3. **Underground Electric Infrastructure**: Show the location of underground electric lines, transformer pads, pull boxes, vaults, and any other electric equipment. Are they distribution or transmission equipment?\n\n4. **Proximity to Site Boundary**: Note any overhead or underground electric facilities that are located near or on the southern boundary of the site (where the landscape plan shows the OHE line).\n\n5. **Utility Notes**: Are there any notes or specifications that reference clearance requirements for trees or vegetation near electric facilities?","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here is the detailed analysis addressing your specific questions:\n\n**1. Overhead Electric Facilities**\nYes, overhead electric infrastructure is shown on this plan. It is denoted by dashed lines with the text label `---OHE---` inserted periodically along the line.\n*   **Location 1 (Western Boundary):** An overhead electric line runs vertically along the left side of the drawing, outside the main property boundary, within what appears to be a Right-of-Way.\n*   **Location 2 (Southern Boundary):** An overhead electric line runs horizontally along the bottom of the drawing, closely following the property line boundary (labeled near `S67°39'57\"W 414.24'`).\n\n**2. Voltage Classification**\nNo, the overhead electric infrastructure is **not** labeled with any specific voltage classification (e.g., kV ratings for distribution or transmission) anywhere on this plan. The lines are simply designated as `OHE`.\n\n**3. Underground Electric Infrastructure**\nUnderground electric infrastructure is extensively detailed on the site, represented by solid blue lines marked periodically with an `---E---`, connecting to various blue-outlined equipment boxes.\n*   **Network Type:** Based on the configuration—tapping off an overhead line, routing to transformer pads, and then distributing directly to electrical meters on individual residential townhome buildings—this represents **distribution** equipment, not transmission.\n*   **Equipment Locations & Exact Labels:**\n    *   **\"Underground Electric Line\"**: Explicitly labeled with callouts pointing to the blue lines on the western edge (entering the site near Building 2) and in the central area between Buildings 4 and 7.\n    *   **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"**: Three are clearly labeled.\n        *   Located on the west side of the site, between Bldg 1 and Bldg 2.\n        *   Located on the north-east side of the site, near Bldg 4.\n        *   Located on the south-east side of the site, between Bldg 6 and Bldg 7.\n    *   **\"Electrical Pull Box\"**: Several are distributed along the underground routing.\n        *   Near the northwest corner by Bldg 1.\n        *   Mid-west side near Bldg 2.\n        *   North-central near Bldg 3.\n        *   East-central near Bldg 5.\n        *   Three are located along the southern routing path near Buildings 7 and 8.\n    *   **\"Electrical Meters\"**: Boxes are located on or immediately adjacent to every single building (Bldgs 1 through 8), with explicit text callouts pointing to them.\n\n**4. Proximity to Site Boundary (Southern Edge)**\nThere is significant electrical infrastructure located on and near the southern boundary (the bottom edge of the drawing).\n*   **Overhead:** A dashed line labeled `---OHE---` runs roughly parallel to and along the southern property line (near the bearing `S67°39'57\"W 414.24'`).\n*   **Underground:** A solid blue underground electric line (`---E---`) runs inside the property line, parallel to the southern boundary, servicing the southern sides of Building 8 and Building 7.\n*   **Equipment:** There are three specific boxes labeled **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** located along this southern underground line, sitting very close to the southern property boundary.\n\n**5. Utility Notes**\nI have reviewed all notes on the plan. There are **no** notes or specifications that reference clearance requirements for trees or vegetation near the electric facilities.\nFor exact reference, the complete text of the **\"Utility Notes\"** block (bottom right) is as follows:\n> 1. Contractor shall verify horizontal and vertical location of existing utilities prior to construction.\n> 2. Contractor shall verify location of existing line, point of connection and notify engineer of any conflicts/discrepancies prior to installation of improvements.\n> 3. All Private Domestic Water Branches to the buildings are to be 2\" HDPE service tube per Detail 520-AW-01B\n> 4. All Private Wastewater Branches to the building are to be 6\" PVC service connections per Detail 520-AW-01C\n>\n> Release of this application does not constitute a verification of all data, information and calculations supplied by the applicant. The engineer of record is solely responsible for the completeness, accuracy and adequacy of his/her submittal, whether or not the application is reviewed for Code compliance by City engineers.\n>\n> The location of all existing utilities shown on these plans has been based upon record information only and may not match locations as constructed. The contractor shall contact Texas 811 for assistance in determining existing utility locations prior to beginning construction. Contractor shall field verify locations of utility crossings prior to beginning construction.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1510,"outputTokens":1035,"totalTokens":4787,"reasoningTokens":2242},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the electrical design plan to identify overhead electric infrastructure. Please provide:\n\n1. **Overhead Electric Facilities**: Are there any overhead electric lines, conductors, poles, or transmission facilities shown on this electrical design plan? If yes, describe their location and any voltage/classification labels.\n\n2. **Voltage Classification**: Is the overhead electric infrastructure labeled with voltage (e.g., 12.47 kV for distribution, 69 kV+ for transmission)?\n\n3. **Underground Electric Infrastructure**: Show the location of underground electric lines, transformer pads, pull boxes, vaults, and any other electric equipment. Are they distribution or transmission equipment?\n\n4. **Proximity to Site Boundary**: Note any overhead or underground electric facilities that are located near or on the southern boundary of the site (where the landscape plan shows the OHE line).\n\n5. **Utility Notes**: Are there any notes or specifications that reference clearance requirements for trees or vegetation near electric facilities?"}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-2jqcZKJM15DwiPBwu1wxPPmM","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 21:16:07 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::sj4nb-1776978914744-f9c4dc0887bf"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here is the detailed analysis addr