REE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   **P** - \"PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n*   **M** - \"MITIGATION TREE\"\n\n*Note: Many trees on the plan feature multiple labels, such as a tree marked with both \"SY\" and \"M\", indicating it serves dual mitigation requirements.*\n\n### 3. Utility-Compatible Species\n\nThere is **no mention** of utility-compatible species, nor is there a species list or reference to \"ECM Appendix F\" anywhere on this specific sheet. The notes strictly cover irrigation requirements, finished elevations for parking lot islands, and general drought/vegetation establishment guidelines.\n\n### 4. Root Barrier Details\n\nThere are **no notes, callouts, or details** regarding root barriers anywhere on this landscape plan.\n\n### 5. Landscaping Details Sheet\n\nSheet 37 (Landscape Details) is **not referenced** anywhere on this plan. The current sheet (Sheet 28) does not contain planting details, root barrier specifications, or cross-references pointing to another sheet for those specific details."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ccf6950-9428-47a1-a0e1-f1b6954e2e70","uuid":"4dfc8dca-c251-454f-927d-410a1c6ee3e9","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan document (labeled Sheet 28 of 35, noting a discrepancy with your prompt which mentions Sheet 31), here is the detailed information requested. \n\n**Important Note:** The exact locations of transformer pads are not explicitly marked or labeled (e.g., \"TR\") on this specific landscape plan sheet. Therefore, the analysis below identifies the vegetation in the general quadrants and estimated areas you provided. Because the pads are not drawn, precise distances from trees/shrubs to the pads cannot be calculated. Specific biological tree species (e.g., Oak, Elm) are not listed on this sheet; trees are only identified by their functional category codes (SY, PL, P, M).\n\n### 1. Vegetation Near Estimated Transfor