{"level":30,"time":1776979215260,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":21,"prompt":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan and identify:\n\n1. What overhead electric (OHE) lines are shown? If OHE lines are depicted, describe their location(s) and routing across the site.\n2. Are there any pad-mounted transformers or other pad-mounted electrical equipment shown? If so, describe their locations.\n3. Are there any poles or utility structures shown on the plan?\n4. What underground utilities are shown (transformers, pull boxes, conduits, vaults)?\n5. Are there any landscape features (trees, shrubs) shown in relation to the electrical infrastructure?\n6. Provide specific locations using grid references or proximity to buildings (e.g., \"near Building 1,\" \"south of Building 5\").\n\nThis is an electrical infrastructure plan, so focus on identifying utility structures and their positions relative to the site boundaries and buildings.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan provided, here is an analysis addressing your specific questions:\n\n**1. Overhead Electric (OHE) Lines**\n*   Overhead electric lines are depicted on the plan using lines intermittently labeled with **\"OHE\"**.\n*   **Western Boundary:** An OHE line runs generally north-south along the far western edge of the site, traversing through an existing easement and crossing multiple existing tree canopies.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** An OHE line runs roughly parallel to the southern property line (near the boundary labeled N62° 39' 57\"W 414.24').\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** An OHE line runs north-south along the eastern property line (near the boundary labeled S27° 19' 20\"W), partially inside an existing utility easement.\n\n**2. Pad-Mounted Electrical Equipment**\nPad-mounted equipment is explicitly labeled in several locations on the site, indicated by square or rectangular pad symbols connected to the underground electrical network (blue lines):\n*   **Near Building 1:** An **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** is located to the west of Building 1.\n*   **Near Building 2:** An **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** is located to the west of Building 2.\n*   **Near Building 4/5:** An **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** is located east of Building 4 and west of Building 5.\n*   **Near Building 6/7:** An **\"Electrical Transformer Pad\"** is located east of Building 7 and west of Building 6.\n\n**3. Poles or Utility Structures**\n*   While explicit labels stating \"Pole\" are not prominently visible on the electrical network itself, standard small circular symbols denote vertices and utility poles along the routing of the **\"OHE\"** lines on the western, southern, and eastern perimeters. \n*   An **\"AT&T Vault\"** is labeled in the extreme northwest corner of the drawing area, outside the main building footprint zone.\n\n**4. Underground Utilities**\nThe plan heavily details proposed underground electrical infrastructure, delineated by solid blue lines:\n*   **Underground Electric Lines:** A line on the western boundary is explicitly labeled **\"Underground Electric Line\"**, showing where power transitions or routes into the site's network. The solid blue lines throughout the site represent the underground conduit routing.\n*   **Electrical Pull Boxes:** Labeled **\"Electrical Pull Box\"** in multiple locations, including:\n    *   North of Building 1\n    *   West of Building 2 / South of Building 8\n    *   North of Building 4\n    *   South of Building 7\n    *   East of Building 5\n*   **Electrical Meters:** Banks of meters are shown attached to the buildings and labeled **\"Electrical Meters\"** (e.g., on the north side of Bldg 1, north side of Bldg 3, north side of Bldg 4, south side of Bldg 7).\n*   **Vault Easement:** A **\"Vault Easement\"** is labeled west of Building 8 in conjunction with an Electrical Pull Box.\n\n**5. Landscape Features in Relation to Electrical Infrastructure**\n*   **Tree Canopies:** Large overlapping circles with varying line weights represent existing tree canopies and root zones (driplines). \n*   **Conflict Areas:** The **OHE** line on the western boundary routes directly through several large, existing tree canopies. Similarly, underground electrical lines (blue lines) on the northern side of the site (near Building 3 and Building 4) route near or through the driplines of large existing trees. \n\n**6. Specific Locations Summary**\n*   **West of Building 1 & 2:** Primary entry points for electrical infrastructure, including two \"Electrical Transformer Pads\" and multiple \"Electrical Pull Boxes\".\n*   **North/South Faces of Buildings:** Most \"Electrical Meters\" are localized on the north or south exterior walls of the respective townhome buildings (e.g., north walls of Bldgs 1, 3, 4; south walls of Bldgs 2, 7, 8).\n*   **Central Corridor:** The gap between the western buildings (1, 2, 3, 8) and eastern buildings (4, 5, 6, 7) contains routing for the underground electric lines connecting the two halves of the development.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1490,"outputTokens":945,"totalTokens":4485,"reasoningTokens":2050},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the Preliminary Electrical Design Plan and identify:\n\n1. What overhead electric (OHE) lines are shown? If OHE lines are depicted, describe their location(s) and routing across the site.\n2. Are there any pad-mounted transformers or other pad-mounted electrical equipment shown? If so, describe their locations.\n3. Are there any poles or utility structures shown on the plan?\n4. What underground utilities are shown (transformers, pull boxes, conduits, vaults)?\n5. Are there any landscape features (trees, shrubs) shown in relation to the electrical infrastructure?\n6. Provide specific locations using grid references or proximity to buildings (e.g., \"near Building 1,\" \"south of Building 5\").\n\nThis is an electrical infrastructure plan, so focus on identifying utility structures and their positions relative to the site boundaries and buildings."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-9NUp3V94QENoTQep4rZdYIM5","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-s