es of Buildings:** Most \"Electrical Meters\" are localized on the north or south exterior walls of the respective townhome buildings (e.g., north walls of Bldgs 1, 3, 4; south walls of Bldgs 2, 7, 8).\n*   **Central Corridor:** The gap between the western buildings (1, 2, 3, 8) and eastern buildings (4, 5, 6, 7) contains routing for the underground electric lines connecting the two halves of the development.","providerOptions":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}]}]},"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","fallbacksAvailable":["google"],"planningReasoning":"System credentials planned for: vertex, google. Total execution order: vertex(system) → google(system)","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","finalProvider":"vertex","modelAttemptCount":1,"modelAttempts":[{"modelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","canonicalSlug":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","success":true,"providerAttemptCount":1,"providerAttempts":[{"provider":"vertex","internalModelId":"vertex:gemini-3.1-pro-preview","providerApiModelId":"gemini-3.1-pro-preview","credentialType":"system","success":true,"startTime":2943348.317973,"endTime":2993474.102451,"statusCode":200,"providerResponseId":"6YvqaZPwFYKSl7oPmY7OmAI"}]}],"totalProviderAttemptCount":1},"cost":"0.03892","marketCost":"0.03892","inferenceCost":"0.03892","inputInferenceCost":"0.00298","outputInferenceCost":"0.03594","generationId":"gen_01KPY351NPEVZE1Y0J6HJXQ5A9"}}}]},"msg":"Vision response"}
{"level":30,"time":1776979215261,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 9 (Proposed Site Plan) and describe the relationship between the proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) and any overhead electric infrastructure visible on the plan. Specifically note:\n\n1. The location and routing of any overhead utility lines shown on this proposed site plan\n2. Proximity of proposed buildings to overhead lines (identify which building(s) are near overhead infrastructure)\n3. Proximity of proposed driveways, parking areas, and sidewalks to overhead lines\n4. Any clearance dimensions or annotations shown between proposed structures and overhead utilities\n5. Whether any buildings or site features appear to be positioned directly beneath or in conflict with overhead lines from the existing survey\n\nPlease provide spatial descriptions using building numbers and site areas (e.g., \"Building 1 is located northwest..., the overhead line runs...\").\n","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 9 (Proposed Site Plan), here is the requested information regarding the relationship between the proposed buildings and overhead electric infrastructure:\n\n**1. Location and routing of overhead utility lines**\nAn overhead electric line is visible on the plan, denoted by a dashed line interspersed with the label **\"- OHE -\"**. This line runs linearly along the entire southern property boundary of the site, extending from the western edge to the eastern edge. \n\n**2. Proximity of proposed buildings to overhead lines**\n*   **Building 8** (located in the southwest quadrant) and **Building 6** (located in the southeast quadrant) are the only proposed buildings situated near the overhead electric infrastructure. Both buildings parallel the southern property line where the \"- OHE -\" line routes.\n*   **Buildings 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, and 7** are located in the northern and central portions of the site and do not have any overhead utility lines shown near them.\n\n**3. Proximity of proposed driveways, parking areas, and sidewalks**\n*   **Sidewalks:** A proposed sidewalk routes along the southern (rear) perimeters of Building 8 and Building 6. This sidewalk runs parallel to the southern property boundary and the \"- OHE -\" line, positioned between the buildings and the utility line.\n*   **Driveways and Parking:** The primary driveways entering the site from the west, as well as the internal parking areas (surface spaces and garages), are located centrally and to the north. They are not shown in proximity to or conflicting with the southern \"- OHE -\" line on this sheet.\n\n**4. Clearance dimensions or annotations**\n*   There are **no explicit horizontal or vertical clearance dimensions** (e.g., minimum required clearance distances) drawn or annotated between the proposed buildings/structures and the overhead utility lines. \n*   However, there are annotations denoting utility easements routing precisely along this \"- OHE -\" alignment on the southern boundary:\n    *   Near the south-central boundary (south of the space between Bldgs 8 & 6): **\"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n    *   Near the southeast corner (south of Bldg 6): **\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5108, Pg. 805 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"**\n\n**5. Direct conflicts or features positioned directly beneath lines**\n*   **Buildings:** Based on the 2D layout, none of the proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) appear to be positioned directly beneath the overhead lines; they appear adequately set back from the southern boundary and the associated 5' electrical easements.\n*   **Site Features:** There is a proposed **\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"** designed to run exactly along the southern property line (with labels pointing to it such as \"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"). Because the \"- OHE -\" line is also routed directly along this boundary, the overhead electric lines appear to run directly over the alignment of this proposed retaining wall.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1479,"outputTokens":663,"totalTokens":5451,"reasoningTokens":3309},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2702484]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Please examine Sheet 9 (Proposed Site Plan) and describe the relationship between the proposed buildings (Buildings 1-8) and any overhead electric infrastructure visible on the plan. Specifically note:\n\n1. The location and routing of any overhead utility lines shown on this proposed site plan\n2. Proximity of proposed buildings to overhead lines (identify which building(s) are near overhead infrastructure)\n3. Proximity of proposed driveways, parking areas, and sidewalks to overhead lines\n4. Any clearance dimensions or annotations shown between proposed structures and overhead utilities\n5. Whether any buildings or site features appear to be positioned directly beneath or in conflict with overhead lines from the existing survey\n\nPlease provide spatial descriptions using building numbers and site areas (e.g., \"Building 1 is located northwest..., the overhead line runs...\").\n"}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-47Obx8NgFNzsk4OgEKTMtuyC","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 21:16:18 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::8ch4m-1776978940380-bc7c01467cbb"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of Sheet 9 (Proposed Site Plan), here is the requested information regarding the relationship between the proposed buildings and overhead electric infrastructure:\n\n**1. Location and routing