tility Lines\n**Yes**, overhead utility lines are explicitly marked on the plan. \n*   They are indicated by dashed lines containing the text label **\"- OHE -\"**. \n*   These lines run continuously along the **left property boundary**, directly parallel to Valley View Road. \n*   Another segment of **\"- OHE -\"** lines runs continuously along the **bottom (southern) property boundary**.\n\n### Layout of Parking, Sidewalks, Driveways, and Structures (Relative to Valley View Road and Overhead Lines)\n\n**Driveways:**\n*   There are two main entrances connecting the site to Valley View Road. Both driveways cross directly beneath/adjacent to the \"- OHE -\" lines running along the left boundary.\n*   The top (north) entrance is labeled **\"Construct Type II Driveway See Detail 4/323-2\"**.\n*   The bottom (south) entrance is labeled **\"Construct Type II Driveway See Detail 1/323-2\"**.\n*   These driveways lead into a continuous internal **\"Concrete Drive\"** that loops through the center of the property, granting access to all buildings.\n\n**Sidewalks:**\n*   A public sidewalk labeled **\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk\"** runs vertically along the entire left boundary of the property. This sidewalk is located directly parallel to Valley View Road and is situated in the same corridor as the overhead utility (\"- OHE -\") lines.\n*   Internally, pedestrian routing uses a network of paths labeled **\"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway\"** and **\"Construct 4' Concrete Sidewalk\"** that connect the buildings away from the main road.\n\n**Parking Areas:**\n*   There is no parking located directly on Valley View Road or immediately under the primary overhead utility lines on the left boundary. \n*   All parking is internalized, consisting of marked surface spaces and individual garage driveways branching off the main internal \"Concrete Drive\".\n\n**Other Structures:**\n*   A **\"Detention Pond\"** is located in the top right (northeast) corner, far from Valley View 