{"level":30,"time":1776979220465,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_019PvwAwsChJFUSUKpBAesCA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Great! Now I have a much clearer picture:\n\n**Key findings from Site Plan (Sheet 9):**\n1. **Overhead utility lines (OHE) marked** along Valley View Road (western/left boundary) and southern boundary\n2. **Two main driveway entrances** that connect to Valley View Road beneath/adjacent to the overhead lines\n3. **Public sidewalk** runs along Valley View Road in the same corridor as the overhead lines\n4. **Transformer pad** near Bldg. 2, close to the Valley View Road boundary and overhead lines\n5. **Internal parking and driveways** away from the overhead lines\n\nNow I need to verify:\n1. **Clearance dimensions** - Are clearances marked from the overhead conductors to the buildings, driveways, sidewalks, and transformer pads?\n2. **Profile views** - Are there cross-sections showing vertical clearances to the driveways?\n3. **Building elevations** - Do the building elevation sheets show surveyed overhead conductor locations?\n4. **Landscape plan** - Are trees near the overhead lines from the utility-compatible list?\n5. **Cover sheet notes** - Is there a 48-hour notification requirement noted?\n6. **Retaining walls** - Do they maintain required clearance from overhead lines?\n\nLet me check:\n1. The grading plan (Sheet 11) to see if there are driveway clearance dimensions\n2. Building elevation sheets to see if they show overhead conductor locations\n3. The landscape plan (Sheet 31) to see tree species and proximity to overhead lines\n4. The cover sheet (Sheet 1) for project notes\n5. The construction details to see if clearances are noted","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_