{"level":30,"time":1776979436962,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TxsGvRL1ueNcUC6QFYfMBt","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 38 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: diagram — Elevation view drawings of a typical step in a footing, showing dimensions and requirements for the bottom of strip footing to be level, stepping bottom of footing as required.\n     4→\n     5→2'-0\"\n     6→AS REQUIRED\n     7→#4 @ 12\" O.C.E.W.\n     8→BOTTOM OF STRIP FOOTING TO BE LEVEL, STEP BOTTOM OF FOOTING AS REQ'D.\n     9→2'-0\"\n    10→12\"\n    11→SEE \"RETAINING WALL\" DETAILS FOR FOOTING REINFORCING\n    12→ELEVATION VIEW\n    13→TYPICAL STEP IN FOOTING\n    14→\n    15→## Block 2: diagram — A cross-section detail showing how to install a new slab adjacent to an existing slab using a #6 rebar dowel. It includes instructions for cleaning the surface, drilling holes, and inserting the rebar with epoxy.\n    16→\n    17→EXISTING SLAB\n    18→CLEAN EXISTING SURFACE PRIOR TO SETTING \"NEW\" CONCRETE\n    19→NEW SLAB\n    20→#6 REBAR (NOT SMOOTH DOWEL)\n    21→DRILL HOLE WITH 7/8\" BIT WHEN USING #4 REBAR\n    22→CLEAR HOLE WITH COMPRESSED AIR PRIOR TO INSERTING EPOXY.\n    23→6\" EMBED\n    24→DRILLED HOLE IN EXISTING CONCRETE SHOULD BE SIZED TO ALLOW REBAR INSTALLATION BY HAND. ONLY LIGHT \"TAPPING\" WITH HAMMER SHOULD BE REQUIRED.\n    25→DOWEL DETAIL\n    26→\n    27→## Block 3: diagram — A cross-section detail of a retaining wall with a maximum height of 14'-0\". It includes specifications for rebar placement, gravel backfill, geotextile fabric, weep pipes, and dimensions for the wall and footing.\n    28→\n    29→CHAMFER EXPOSED EDGES (TYPICAL)\n    30→EXISTING WALL\n    31→GRAVEL BACK FILL\n    32→#7 @ 10\" O.C. VERT.\n    33→14'-0\" MAX.\n    34→MIRAFI 140N GEOTEXTILE OR APPROVED EQUAL\n    35→#4 @ 12\" O.C. VERT.\n    36→#3 @ 12\" O.C. HORIZ. EACH FACE\n    37→ADD 2\" DIA. PVC WEEP PIPE @ 5' O.C. 8\" ABOVE WALL FOOTING \"TOE\"\n    38→TOP OF GRADE\n    39→#7 @ 10\" O.C. TOP AND BOTTOM\n    40→ADD (2)#6 DOWELS @ 18\" O.C. TOP AND BOTTOM SEE DETAIL THIS PAGE.\n    41→#4 @ 12\" O.C. CONT. AS SHOWN\n    42→14'-0\" MAX. RETAINING WALL\n    43→\n    44→## Block 4: drawing — A plan view drawing of retaining walls, pond walls, and existing walls. It includes callouts for a new retaining wall to be in place prior to demo for pond walls, an existing buttress with instructions to drill and epoxy #6 x 12\" dowels 6\" into the buttress 12\" O.C. tie to wall steel, and a callout to start on the south side of existing wall.\n    45→\n    46→POND WALL REF PG 2\n    47→POND WALL REF PG 2\n    48→POND WALL REF PG 2\n    49→POND WALL REF PG 2\n    50→NEW WALL TO BE IN PLACE PRIOR TO DEMO FOR POND WALLS.\n    51→NEW RETAINING WALL REF DETAIL THIS PAGE\n    52→EXISTING WALL\n    53→EXISTING BUTTRESS DRILL AND EPOXY #6 X 12\" DOWELS 6\" INTO BUTTRESS 12\" O.C. TIE TO WALL STEEL\n    54→NEW RETAINING WALL REF DETAIL THIS PAGE\n    55→PLAN VIEW\n    56→ONE 20' SECTION OF NEW FOOTING TO BE INSTALLED AT A TIME. START AT THE SOUTH SIDE OF EXISTING WALL.\n    57→\n    58→## Block 5: notes — A list of notes covering general contractor responsibilities, concrete specifications, and reinforcement requirements.\n    59→\n    60→NOTES:\n    61→1. THE CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR OBTAINING ALL PERMITS NECESSARY TO LEGALLY COMMENCE WITH THIS WORK.\n    62→2. OBTAIN LOCATION AND DEPTH OF EXISTING UTILITY LINES PRIOR TO BEGINNING CONSTRUCTION.\n    63→3. CONTRACTOR SHALL DISPOSE OF ALL SPOILS LEGALLY AT AN OFFSITE LOCATION OR AS DIRECTED BY OWNER.\n    64→4. SHOULD CONDITIONS ARISE THAT ARE NOT COVERED BY DETAILS ON THIS PLAN, CONTACT ENGINEER AT ONCE FOR ADDITIONAL INSTRUCTIONS.\n    65→CONCRETE:\n    66→1. CONCRETE TO HAVE A MINIMUM 28 DAY COMPRESSIVE STRENGTH OF 3000 PSI.\n    67→2. CONCRETE SHALL BE WELL CONSOLIDATED USING PROPER MECHANICAL VIBRATION.\n    68→3. MINIMUM CONCRETE CLEAR COVER SHALL BE\n    69→IN SLABS:\n    70→3/4\" ADJACENT TO INTERIOR SLAB SURFACES\n    71→1 1/2\" ABOVE SUB-GRADE\n    72→IN STIFFENING BEAMS, WALLS AND FOOTINGS:\n    73→1 1/2\" ADJACENT TO EXTERIOR OR INTERIOR SURFACES\n    74→3\" FROM SURFACES IN CONTACT WITH EARTH\n    75→AT PIPE PENETRATION IN BEAM OR SLAB:\n    76→2\" FOR REBAR\n    77→REINFORCEMENT:\n    78→1. REINFORCING STEEL TO BE GRADE 60 FOR #4 AND LARGER AND GRADE 40 FOR #3.\n    79→2. ADD 24\"x24\" CORNER BARS EQUAL TO SIZE AND SPACING OF DISCONTINUOUS HORIZ. STEEL.\n    80→\n    81→## Block 6: notes — A general note regarding the purpose of the schematic plan, confirming it is for locating and identifying foundation reinforcing elements only, and emphasizing the architect's responsibility for dimensional control.\n    82→\n    83→NOTE:\n    84→THIS IS A SCHEMATIC PLAN FOR THE PURPOSE OF LOCATING AND IDENTIFYING FOUNDATION REINFORCING ELEMENTS ONLY. VERIFY ALL DIMENSIONS, DROPS, OFFSETS AND FEATURES WITH THE ARCHITECTURAL PLANS BEFORE FORMING THE FOUNDATION. MLAW CANNOT BE HELD LIABLE FOR ANY CONTRACTOR OVERSIGHT IN THIS REGARD. DO NOT FORM FOUNDATION USING THESE PLANS. DIMENSIONAL CONTROL IS THE RESPONSIBILITY OF THE ARCHITECT. USE THESE PLANS FOR THE PLACEMENT OF THE GRADE BEAMS AND REINFORCEMENT.\n    85→\n    86→## Block 9: table — A table outlining the design criteria for the project, including allowable soil bearing, lateral pressure method, active soil pressure for the heel, passive pressure, and soil weight.\n    87→\n    88→DESIGN CRITERIA:\n    89→REQUIREMENTS OF IBC 2015\n    90→| *ALLOWABLE SOIL BEARING | : 4,000 PSF |\n    91→|---|---|\n    92→| *LATERAL PRESSURE METHOD | : E.F.P. |\n    93→| *ACTIVE SOIL PRESSURE - HEEL | : 45.5 PSF |\n    94→| *PASSIVE PRESSURE | : 290 PSF |\n    95→| *SOIL WEIGHT | : 130 PSF |\n    96→\n    97→## Block 10: table — A list of required inspections prior to specific construction phases.\n    98→\n    99→REQUIRED INSPECTIONS:\n   100→1. PRIOR TO CONCRETE PLACEMENT OF FOOTINGS.\n   101→2. PRIOR TO CONCRETE PLACEMENT OF WALLS.\n   102→3. PRIOR TO BACKFILL PLACEMENT TO VERIFY FILTER FABRIC AND DRAINAGE GRAVEL.\n   103→\n   104→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11ce902f-86c5-4003-b16c-9143da511761","uuid":"43f59648-20ec-44c6-92b3-ff66f613fc26","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-38/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 38 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: diagram — Elevation view drawings of a typical step in a footing, showing dimensions and requirements for the bottom of strip footing to be level, stepping bottom of footing as required.\n\n2'-0\"\nAS REQUIRED\n#4 @ 12\" O.C.E.W.\nBOTTOM OF STRIP FOOTING TO BE LEVEL, STEP BOTTOM OF FOOTING AS REQ'D.\n2'-0\"\n12\"\nSEE \"RETAINING WALL\" DETAILS FOR FOOTING REINFORCING\nELEVATION VIEW\nTYPICAL STEP IN FOOTING\n\n## Block 2: diagram — A cross-section detail showing how to install a new slab adjacent to an existing slab using a #6 rebar dowel. It includes instructions for cleaning the surface, drilling holes, and inserting the rebar with epoxy.\n\nEXISTING SLAB\nCLEAN EXISTING SURFACE PRIOR TO SETTING \"NEW\" CONCRETE\nNEW SLAB\n#6 REBAR (NOT SMOOTH DOWEL)\nDRILL HOLE WITH 7/8\" BIT WHEN USING #4 REBAR\nCLEAR HOLE WITH COMPRESSED AIR PRIOR TO INSERTING EPOXY.\n6\" EMBED\nDRILLED HOLE IN EXISTING CONCRETE SHOULD BE SIZED TO ALLOW REBAR INSTALLATION BY HAND. ONLY LIGHT \"TAPPING\" WITH HAMMER SHOULD BE REQUIRED.\nDOWEL DETAIL\n\n## Block 3: diagram — A cross-section detail of a retaining wall with a maximum height of 14'-0\". It includes specifications for rebar placement, gravel backfill, geotextile fabric, weep pipes, and dimensions for the wall and footing.\n\nCHAMFER EXPOSED EDGES (TYPICAL)\nEXISTING WALL\nGRAVEL BACK FILL\n#7 @ 10\" O.C. VERT.\n14'-0\" MAX.\nMIRAFI 140N GEOTEXTILE OR APPROVED EQUAL\n#4 @ 12\" O.C. VERT.\n#3 @ 12\" O.C. HORIZ. EACH FACE\nADD 2\" DIA. PVC WEEP PIPE @ 5' O.C. 8\" ABOVE WALL FOOTING \"TOE\"\nTOP OF GRADE\n#7 @ 10\" O.C. TOP AND BOTTOM\nADD (2)#6 DOWELS @ 18\" O.C. TOP AND BOTTOM SEE DETAIL THIS PAGE.\n#4 @ 12\" O.C. CONT. AS SHOWN\n14'-0\" MAX. RETAINING WALL\n\n## Block 4: drawing — A plan view drawing of retaining walls, pond walls, and existing walls. It includes callouts for a new retaining wall to be in place prior to demo for pond walls, an existing buttress with instructions to drill and epoxy #6 x 12\" dowels 6\" into the buttress 12\" O.C. tie to wall steel, and a callout to start on the south side of existing wall.\n\nPOND WALL REF PG 2\nPOND WALL REF PG 2\nPOND WALL REF PG 2\nPOND WALL REF PG 2\nNEW WALL TO BE IN PLACE PRIOR TO DEMO FOR POND WALLS.\nNEW RETAINING WALL REF DETAIL THIS PAGE\nEXISTING WALL\nEXISTING BUTTRESS DRILL AND EPOXY #6 X 12\" DOWELS 6\" INTO BUTTRESS 12\" O.C. TIE TO WALL STEEL\nNEW RETAINING WALL REF DETAIL THIS PAGE\nPLAN VIEW\nONE 20' SECTION OF NEW FOOTING TO BE INSTALLED AT A TIME. START AT THE SOUTH SIDE OF EXISTING WALL.\n\n## Block 5: notes — A list of notes covering general contractor responsibilities, concrete specifications, and reinforcement requirements.\n\nNOTES:\n1. THE CONTRACTOR IS RESPONSIBLE FOR OBTAINING ALL PERMITS NECESSARY TO LEGALLY COMMENCE WITH THIS WORK.\n2. OBTAIN LOCATION AND DEPTH OF EXISTING UTILITY LINES PRIOR TO BEGINNING CONSTRUCTION.\n3. CONTRACTOR SHALL DISPOSE OF ALL SPOILS LEGALLY AT AN OFFSITE LOCATION OR AS DIRECTED BY OWNER.\n4. SHOULD CONDITIONS ARISE THAT ARE NOT COVERED BY DETAILS ON THIS PLAN, CONTACT ENGINEER AT ONCE FOR ADDITIONAL INSTRUCTIONS.\nCONCRETE:\n1. CONCRETE TO HAVE A MINIMUM 28 DAY COMPRESSIVE STRENGTH OF 3000 PSI.\n2. CONCRETE SHALL BE WELL CONSOLIDATED USING PROPER MECHANICAL VIBRATION.\n3. MINIMUM CONCRETE CLEAR COVER SHALL BE\nIN SLABS:\n3/4\" ADJACENT TO INTERIOR SLAB SURFACES\n1 1/2\" ABOVE SUB-GRADE\nIN STIFFENING BEAMS, WALLS AND FOOTINGS:\n1 1/2\" ADJACENT TO EXTERIOR OR INTERIOR SURFACES\n3\" FROM SURFACES IN CONTACT WITH EARTH\nAT PIPE PENETRATION IN BEAM OR SLAB:\n2\" FOR REBAR\nREINFORCEMENT:\n1. REINFORCING STEEL TO BE GRADE 60 FOR #4 AND LARGER AND GRADE 40 FOR #3.\n2. ADD 24\"x24\" CORNER BARS EQUAL TO SIZE AND SPACING OF DISCONTINUOUS HORIZ. STEEL.\n\n## Block 6: notes — A general note regarding the purpose of the schematic plan, confirming it is for locating and identifying foundation reinforcing elements only, and emphasizing the architect's responsibility for dimensional control.\n\nNOTE:\nTHIS IS A SCHEMATIC PLAN FOR THE PURPOSE OF LOCATING AND IDENTIFYING FOUNDATION REINFORCING ELEMENTS ONLY. VERIFY ALL DIMENSIONS, DROPS, OFFSETS AND FEATURES WITH THE ARCHITECTURAL PLANS BEFORE FORMING THE FOUNDATION. MLAW CANNOT BE HELD LIABLE FOR ANY CONTRACTOR OVERSIGHT IN THIS REGARD. DO NOT FORM FOUNDATION USING THESE PLANS. DIMENSIONAL CONTROL IS THE RESPONSIBILITY OF THE ARCHITECT. USE THESE PLANS FOR THE PLACEMENT OF THE GRADE BEAMS AND REINFORCEMENT.\n\n## Block 9: table — A table outlining the design criteria for the project, including allowable soil bearing, lateral pressure method, active soil pressure for the heel, passive pressure, and soil weight.\n\nDESIGN CRITERIA:\nREQUIREMENTS OF IBC 2015\n| *ALLOWABLE SOIL BEARING | : 4,000 PSF |\n|---|---|\n| *LATERAL PRESSURE METHOD | : E.F.P. |\n| *ACTIVE SOIL PRESSURE - HEEL | : 45.5 PSF |\n| *PASSIVE PRESSURE | : 290 PSF |\n| *SOIL WEIGHT | : 130 PSF |\n\n## Block 10: table — A list of required inspections prior to specific construction phases.\n\nREQUIRED INSPECTIONS:\n1. PRIOR TO CONCRETE PLACEMENT OF FOOTINGS.\n2. PRIOR TO CONCRETE PLACEMENT OF WALLS.\n3. PRIOR TO BACKFILL PLACEMENT TO VERIFY FILTER FABRIC AND DRAINAGE GRAVEL.\n\n","numLines":104,"startLine":1,"totalLines":104}}}
