{"level":30,"time":1776979436963,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015wSM3rq2Z4kG1iH9yGrmYJ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 1 — Content Blocks\n     2→\n     3→## Block 1: drawing — This block shows a map of the project location, highlighting the surrounding streets and intersection. A pointer indicates the specific project location.\n     4→\n     5→[Map showing the project location and surrounding streets.]\n     6→\n     7→N\n     8→\n     9→PROJECT\n    10→LOCATION\n    11→\n    12→## Block 5: table — This block contains data related to the Austin Fire Department's requirements for the project. It includes information such as fire design codes, fire flow demand, occupancy classification, construction classification, building fire area, automatic fire sprinkler system type, reduced fire flow demand, applies to project status, AFD fire hydrant flow test dates and locations, city of Austin pipeline ordinance compliance, high-rise status, international wildland-urban interface code compliance, and alternative method of compliance AMOC.\n    13→\n    14→Austin Fire Department\n    15→\n    16→| Fire Design Codes | 2021 International Fire Code Edition\n    17→with City of Austin Local Amendments |\n    18→|---|---|\n    19→| Fire Flow Demand @ 20 psi\n    20→(gpm) | 3000 GPM |\n    21→| Occupancy Classification | R3 |\n    22→| Construction Classification | Type V-B |\n    23→| Building Fire Area (s.f.) | 13,344 |\n    24→| Automatic Fire Sprinkler System\n    25→Type (If applicable) | NFPA 13D |\n    26→| Reduced Fire Flow Demand @ 20\n    27→psi for having a sprinkler system\n    28→(gpm) | 1500 GPM |\n    29→| AFD Fire Hydrant Flow Test Date | 3/21/2025 |\n    30→| AFD Fire Hydrant Flow Test\n    31→Location | 3700 Valley View Rd. |\n    32→| City of Austin Pipeline Ordinance\n    33→Applies to Project | No |\n    34→| High-Rise | No |\n    35→| International Wildland-Urban\n    36→Interface Code | N/A |\n    37→| Alternative Method of\n    38→Compliance AMOC (If applicable) | N/A |\n    39→\n    40→## Block 6: table — This block contains the site development data for the Valley View Townhomes project. It includes contact information for the owner, engineer, architect, and landscape architect, as well as the legal description, subdivision file number, zoning case number, and limits of construction.\n    41→\n    42→Site Development Data Valley View Townhomes\n    43→Owner: WM 41 Austin RE, LLC.\n    44→Contact Person: Richard D. Agnew\n    45→500 West 5th Street, Ste. 1010\n    46→Austin, Texas 78701\n    47→Phone: 512-565-6159\n    48→Email: Richard.Agnew@slpops.com\n    49→\n    50→Engineer: Bleyl Engineering\n    51→Contact Person: Jason Rodgers\n    52→7701 San Felipe, Suite 200\n    53→Austin, Texas 78729\n    54→Phone: (512) 454-2400\n    55→Email: jrodgers@bleylengineering.com\n    56→\n    57→Architect: Danze & Davis Architects, Inc.\n    58→Contact Person: Harrison Davis\n    59→4701 Spicewood Springs Rd, Ste 200\n    60→Austin, Texas 78759\n    61→Phone: (512) 343-0714\n    62→\n    63→Landscape Architect: Blu Fish Collaborative, Inc.\n    64→Contact Person: Mike Fishbaugh\n    65→3607 S. Lamar Blvd., Suite 104\n    66→Austin, Texas 78704\n    67→Phone: (512) 338-4115\n    68→\n    69→Legal Description: Lot 1 Mecey Subdivision, Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County,\n    70→Texas\n    71→2.16 Acres\n    72→Subdivision File No. C8S-75-160\n    73→Zoning Case No. C14-2011-0093\n    74→Limits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n    75→\n    76→## Block 8: text_block — This block is the title and primary identification information for the site plan. It states the project name, address, jurisdiction, SP number, and submittal date.\n    77→\n    78→Site Plan\n    79→Valley View Townhomes\n    80→3759 Valley View Road\n    81→Austin, Texas 78704\n    82→Jurisdiction: Austin Full Purpose\n    83→\n    84→SP-2025-0126C\n    85→Submittal Date: May 20, 2025\n    86→\n    87→## Block 9: text_block — This block is a disclaimer from Bleyl Engineering stating that they are not responsible for the accuracy of the survey or design errors resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n    88→\n    89→Bleyl Engineering and its associates will not be held responsible for the accuracy of the survey or for design errors or\n    90→omissions resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n    91→\n    92→## Block 10: text_block — This block is a note stating that all detention basins, water quality ponds, and appurtenances must be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the Drainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n    93→\n    94→All detention basins, water quality ponds and appurtenances which receive stormwater runoff from commercial or\n    95→multi-family development shall be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the maintenance standards in the\n    96→Drainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n    97→\n    98→## Block 11: text_block — This block is a note stating that compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory.\n    99→\n   100→Compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory for multi-family complexes,\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8920d43-e944-47ba-ad17-2e6340f56c7c","uuid":"1b9d3a66-74cc-493c-bb0b-0db787385162","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-01/blocks.md","content":"# Sheet 1 — Content Blocks\n\n## Block 1: drawing — This block shows a map of the project location, highlighting the surrounding streets and intersection. A pointer indicates the specific project location.\n\n[Map showing the project location and surrounding streets.]\n\nN\n\nPROJECT\nLOCATION\n\n## Block 5: table — This block contains data related to the Austin Fire Department's requirements for the project. It includes information such as fire design codes, fire flow demand, occupancy classification, construction classification, building fire area, automatic fire sprinkler system type, reduced fire flow demand, applies to project status, AFD fire hydrant flow test dates and locations, city of Austin pipeline ordinance compliance, high-rise status, international wildland-urban interface code compliance, and alternative method of compliance AMOC.\n\nAustin Fire Department\n\n| Fire Design Codes | 2021 International Fire Code Edition\nwith City of Austin Local Amendments |\n|---|---|\n| Fire Flow Demand @ 20 psi\n(gpm) | 3000 GPM |\n| Occupancy Classification | R3 |\n| Construction Classification | Type V-B |\n| Building Fire Area (s.f.) | 13,344 |\n| Automatic Fire Sprinkler System\nType (If applicable) | NFPA 13D |\n| Reduced Fire Flow Demand @ 20\npsi for having a sprinkler system\n(gpm) | 1500 GPM |\n| AFD Fire Hydrant Flow Test Date | 3/21/2025 |\n| AFD Fire Hydrant Flow Test\nLocation | 3700 Valley View Rd. |\n| City of Austin Pipeline Ordinance\nApplies to Project | No |\n| High-Rise | No |\n| International Wildland-Urban\nInterface Code | N/A |\n| Alternative Method of\nCompliance AMOC (If applicable) | N/A |\n\n## Block 6: table — This block contains the site development data for the Valley View Townhomes project. It includes contact information for the owner, engineer, architect, and landscape architect, as well as the legal description, subdivision file number, zoning case number, and limits of construction.\n\nSite Development Data Valley View Townhomes\nOwner: WM 41 Austin RE, LLC.\nContact Person: Richard D. Agnew\n500 West 5th Street, Ste. 1010\nAustin, Texas 78701\nPhone: 512-565-6159\nEmail: Richard.Agnew@slpops.com\n\nEngineer: Bleyl Engineering\nContact Person: Jason Rodgers\n7701 San Felipe, Suite 200\nAustin, Texas 78729\nPhone: (512) 454-2400\nEmail: jrodgers@bleylengineering.com\n\nArchitect: Danze & Davis Architects, Inc.\nContact Person: Harrison Davis\n4701 Spicewood Springs Rd, Ste 200\nAustin, Texas 78759\nPhone: (512) 343-0714\n\nLandscape Architect: Blu Fish Collaborative, Inc.\nContact Person: Mike Fishbaugh\n3607 S. Lamar Blvd., Suite 104\nAustin, Texas 78704\nPhone: (512) 338-4115\n\nLegal Description: Lot 1 Mecey Subdivision, Volume 73, Page 76, Plat Records of Travis County,\nTexas\n2.16 Acres\nSubdivision File No. C8S-75-160\nZoning Case No. C14-2011-0093\nLimits of Construction: 2.26 Acres\n\n## Block 8: text_block — This block is the title and primary identification information for the site plan. It states the project name, address, jurisdiction, SP number, and submittal date.\n\nSite Plan\nValley View Townhomes\n3759 Valley View Road\nAustin, Texas 78704\nJurisdiction: Austin Full Purpose\n\nSP-2025-0126C\nSubmittal Date: May 20, 2025\n\n## Block 9: text_block — This block is a disclaimer from Bleyl Engineering stating that they are not responsible for the accuracy of the survey or design errors resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n\nBleyl Engineering and its associates will not be held responsible for the accuracy of the survey or for design errors or\nomissions resulting from survey inaccuracies.\n\n## Block 10: text_block — This block is a note stating that all detention basins, water quality ponds, and appurtenances must be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the Drainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n\nAll detention basins, water quality ponds and appurtenances which receive stormwater runoff from commercial or\nmulti-family development shall be maintained by the record owner in accordance with the maintenance standards in the\nDrainage and Environmental Criteria Manual.\n\n## Block 11: text_block — This block is a note stating that compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory.\n\nCompliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory for multi-family complexes,","numLines":100,"startLine":1,"totalLines":277}}}
