{"level":30,"time":1776979436963,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017iARvCyfsuae5UiqjxDb7L","type":"tool_result","content":"   100→Compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory for multi-family complexes,\n   101→businesses and office buildings.\n   102→\n   103→## Block 12: text_block — This block is a note indicating where the Integrated Pest Management Plan can be found in the Official Public Records of Travis County, Texas.\n   104→\n   105→For Integrated Pest Management Plan, see agreement filed in document No.____________, Official Public Records,\n   106→Travis County, Texas.\n   107→\n   108→## Block 13: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project is located within the West Bouldin Creek Watershed and that no portion of the tract is within the 100-year flood plain.\n   109→\n   110→This project is located within the West Bouldin Creek Watershed (Urban). All storm flows from this site will be directed\n   111→to the West Bouldin Creek Watershed. No portion of this tract is within the boundaries of the 100 year flood plain of\n   112→any waterway that is within the limits of study of the Federal Flood Insurance Administration FIRM panel\n   113→#48453C0585H, dated September 26, 2008 for Travis County.\n   114→\n   115→## Block 14: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project is not located within the Edwards Aquifer Recharge Zone or the Edwards Aquifer Contributing Zone.\n   116→\n   117→Edwards Aquifer Note This project is not located within the Edwards Aquifer Recharge Zone or the Edwards Aquifer\n   118→Contributing Zone.\n   119→\n   120→## Block 15: text_block — This block contains the scale, mapsco number, and city of Austin grid number for the project location map.\n   121→\n   122→Project Location Map\n   123→Scale: 1\" = 400'\n   124→Mapsco #614S\n   125→City of Austin Grid #G19\n   126→\n   127→## Block 16: text_block — This block contains a table for recording the dates that various City departments reviewed the plans.\n   128→\n   129→Reviewed By:\n   130→\n   131→Development Services Department Date\n   132→SP-2025-0126C\n   133→Development Permit No.\n   134→\n   135→City of Austin Fire Department Date\n   136→\n   137→Austin Water Date\n   138→\n   139→## Block 17: text_block — This block is a note indicating that the contractor is responsible for filing all necessary forms with the Environmental Protection Agency for projects involving 5 acres or more of disturbed area.\n   140→\n   141→Contractor is responsible for filing all necessary forms with the Environmental Protection Agency for all projects\n   142→involving 5 acres or more of disturbed area or part of a larger development which will eventually disturb 5 acres or more.\n   143→Note The contractor and the owner both must file a Notice of Intent.\n   144→\n   145→## Block 18: text_block — This block is a note requiring all potable water system components installed after January 4, 2014, to be \"lead free\" according to the US Safe Drinking Water Act. It lists examples of exempt and non-exempt components.\n   146→\n   147→All potable water system components installed after January 4, 2014, shall be essentially \"lead free\" according to the\n   148→US Safe Drinking Water Act. Examples are valves (corporation stop, curb stop, and pressure reducing), nipples,\n   149→bushings, pipe, fittings and backflow preventers. Fire hydrants, tapping saddles and 2 inch and larger gate valves are\n   150→the only components exempt from this requirement. Components that are not clearly identified by the manufacturer as\n   151→meeting this requirement either by markings on the component or on the packaging shall not be installed.\n   152→\n   153→## Block 19: text_block — This block is a note regarding the project's private hydrants and the owner's responsibility to comply with the Austin Fire Code. It states that private hydrants must be serviced, maintained, and flowed annually.\n   154→\n   155→City of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060\n   156→This project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin\n   157→Fire Code. Failure to comply may result in civil and/or criminal remedies available to the City. The performance of\n   158→this obligation shall always rest with the owner or record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced,\n   159→maintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project\n   160→includes __1__ private hydrants.\n   161→\n   162→## Block 20: text_block — This block states that a civil engineer registered in Texas must certify the plan as complete, accurate, and in compliance with the Land Development Code, unless waived by the director.\n   163→\n   164→A civil engineer registered in Texas must certify a plan or plat as complete, accurate, and in compliance with Chapter\n   165→25-8 Subchapter A of the Land Development Code. The director may waive this requirement after making a\n   166→determination that the plan or plat includes only minor alterations or improvement that do not require the services of an\n   167→engineer.\n   168→\n   169→## Block 21: text_block — This block is a note regarding the placement of silt fences and additional erosion/sedimentation controls as required by the City's Environmental and Conservation Services Department. It also specifies that only approved construction entrances should be used.\n   170→\n   171→All temporary spoils and equipment storage areas shall have silt fence placed along the perimeter of the downslope\n   172→side. Additional erosion/sedimentation controls may be required at the direction of the City's Environmental and\n   173→Conservation Services Department Officer/Inspector. The contractor shall work closely with all City Personnel to insure\n   174→adequacy of placement and maintenance of all erosion/sedimentation control devices. Only those construction\n   175→entrances shown on the approved site plan shall be used for ingress and egress to and from site. In the event that\n   176→additional entrance locations are required to facilitate placement of materials, the contractor shall construct a stabilized\n   177→construction entrance in accordance with City of Austin Standard Details in order to comply with all provisions of the\n   178→City's Land Development Code and Environmental Protection Ordinances.\n   179→\n   180→## Block 22: text_block — This block is a note stating that approval by the City of Austin indicates compliance with applicable City regulations only and that approval by other governmental entities may be required.\n   181→\n   182→Approval of these plans by the City of Austin indicates compliance with applicable City regulations only. Approval by\n   183→other governmental entities may be required prior to the start of construction. The applicant is responsible for\n   184→determining what additional approvals may be necessary.\n   185→\n   186→## Block 23: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project received approval from the Watershed Protection Department for a waiver to a specific section of the COA Drainage Criteria Manual.\n   187→\n   188→DCM Waiver Note: On 01/21/2026 this project received approval from the Watershed Protection Department of a\n   189→waiver to Section 1.2.4.E.1.e.i of the COA Drainage Criteria Manual.\n   190→\n   191→## Block 24: text_block — This block contains a stamp for the City of Austin to officially approve the site plan. It includes fields for the file number, application date, approval date, whether it was approved administratively or by commission, the expiration date, case manager, and zoning.\n   192→\n   193→SITE PLAN APPROVAL SHEET ____1____ of ____39____\n   194→FILE NUMBER ____SP-2025-0126C____ APPLICATION DATE ____05/20/2025____\n   195→APPROVED ON _________________ \n   196→□ADMINISTRATIVELY \n   197→□BY COMMISSION\n   198→UNDER SECTION 112 OF CHAPTER 25-5 OF THE CITY OF AUSTIN CODE.\n   199→EXPIRATION DATE (25-5-81,LDC) ___________________ CASE MANAGER ___Jim Gobel_______\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8920d43-e944-47ba-ad17-2e6340f56c7c","uuid":"3d3e11de-9f2d-44cc-84ec-a57fd067f1d0","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-01/blocks.md","content":"Compliance with the Commercial and Multi-Family Recycling Ordinance is mandatory for multi-family complexes,\nbusinesses and office buildings.\n\n## Block 12: text_block — This block is a note indicating where the Integrated Pest Management Plan can be found in the Official Public Records of Travis County, Texas.\n\nFor Integrated Pest Management Plan, see agreement filed in document No.____________, Official Public Records,\nTravis County, Texas.\n\n## Block 13: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project is located within the West Bouldin Creek Watershed and that no portion of the tract is within the 100-year flood plain.\n\nThis project is located within the West Bouldin Creek Watershed (Urban). All storm flows from this site will be directed\nto the West Bouldin Creek Watershed. No portion of this tract is within the boundaries of the 100 year flood plain of\nany waterway that is within the limits of study of the Federal Flood Insurance Administration FIRM panel\n#48453C0585H, dated September 26, 2008 for Travis County.\n\n## Block 14: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project is not located within the Edwards Aquifer Recharge Zone or the Edwards Aquifer Contributing Zone.\n\nEdwards Aquifer Note This project is not located within the Edwards Aquifer Recharge Zone or the Edwards Aquifer\nContributing Zone.\n\n## Block 15: text_block — This block contains the scale, mapsco number, and city of Austin grid number for the project location map.\n\nProject Location Map\nScale: 1\" = 400'\nMapsco #614S\nCity of Austin Grid #G19\n\n## Block 16: text_block — This block contains a table for recording the dates that various City departments reviewed the plans.\n\nReviewed By:\n\nDevelopment Services Department Date\nSP-2025-0126C\nDevelopment Permit No.\n\nCity of Austin Fire Department Date\n\nAustin Water Date\n\n## Block 17: text_block — This block is a note indicating that the contractor is responsible for filing all necessary forms with the Environmental Protection Agency for projects involving 5 acres or more of disturbed area.\n\nContractor is responsible for filing all necessary forms with the Environmental Protection Agency for all projects\ninvolving 5 acres or more of disturbed area or part of a larger development which will eventually disturb 5 acres or more.\nNote The contractor and the owner both must file a Notice of Intent.\n\n## Block 18: text_block — This block is a note requiring all potable water system components installed after January 4, 2014, to be \"lead free\" according to the US Safe Drinking Water Act. It lists examples of exempt and non-exempt components.\n\nAll potable water system components installed after January 4, 2014, shall be essentially \"lead free\" according to the\nUS Safe Drinking Water Act. Examples are valves (corporation stop, curb stop, and pressure reducing), nipples,\nbushings, pipe, fittings and backflow preventers. Fire hydrants, tapping saddles and 2 inch and larger gate valves are\nthe only components exempt from this requirement. Components that are not clearly identified by the manufacturer as\nmeeting this requirement either by markings on the component or on the packaging shall not be installed.\n\n## Block 19: text_block — This block is a note regarding the project's private hydrants and the owner's responsibility to comply with the Austin Fire Code. It states that private hydrants must be serviced, maintained, and flowed annually.\n\nCity of Austin - Water and Wastewater Utility - Special Services Division (512) 972-1060\nThis project has private hydrants located within the property. The property owner is required to comply with Austin\nFire Code. Failure to comply may result in civil and/or criminal remedies available to the City. The performance of\nthis obligation shall always rest with the owner or record. Fire hydrants on private property are required to serviced,\nmaintained and flowed annually, using a contractor registered with the City to provide this service. This project\nincludes __1__ private hydrants.\n\n## Block 20: text_block — This block states that a civil engineer registered in Texas must certify the plan as complete, accurate, and in compliance with the Land Development Code, unless waived by the director.\n\nA civil engineer registered in Texas must certify a plan or plat as complete, accurate, and in compliance with Chapter\n25-8 Subchapter A of the Land Development Code. The director may waive this requirement after making a\ndetermination that the plan or plat includes only minor alterations or improvement that do not require the services of an\nengineer.\n\n## Block 21: text_block — This block is a note regarding the placement of silt fences and additional erosion/sedimentation controls as required by the City's Environmental and Conservation Services Department. It also specifies that only approved construction entrances should be used.\n\nAll temporary spoils and equipment storage areas shall have silt fence placed along the perimeter of the downslope\nside. Additional erosion/sedimentation controls may be required at the direction of the City's Environmental and\nConservation Services Department Officer/Inspector. The contractor shall work closely with all City Personnel to insure\nadequacy of placement and maintenance of all erosion/sedimentation control devices. Only those construction\nentrances shown on the approved site plan shall be used for ingress and egress to and from site. In the event that\nadditional entrance locations are required to facilitate placement of materials, the contractor shall construct a stabilized\nconstruction entrance in accordance with City of Austin Standard Details in order to comply with all provisions of the\nCity's Land Development Code and Environmental Protection Ordinances.\n\n## Block 22: text_block — This block is a note stating that approval by the City of Austin indicates compliance with applicable City regulations only and that approval by other governmental entities may be required.\n\nApproval of these plans by the City of Austin indicates compliance with applicable City regulations only. Approval by\nother governmental entities may be required prior to the start of construction. The applicant is responsible for\ndetermining what additional approvals may be necessary.\n\n## Block 23: text_block — This block is a note stating that the project received approval from the Watershed Protection Department for a waiver to a specific section of the COA Drainage Criteria Manual.\n\nDCM Waiver Note: On 01/21/2026 this project received approval from the Watershed Protection Department of a\nwaiver to Section 1.2.4.E.1.e.i of the COA Drainage Criteria Manual.\n\n## Block 24: text_block — This block contains a stamp for the City of Austin to officially approve the site plan. It includes fields for the file number, application date, approval date, whether it was approved administratively or by commission, the expiration date, case manager, and zoning.\n\nSITE PLAN APPROVAL SHEET ____1____ of ____39____\nFILE NUMBER ____SP-2025-0126C____ APPLICATION DATE ____05/20/2025____\nAPPROVED ON _________________ \n□ADMINISTRATIVELY \n□BY COMMISSION\nUNDER SECTION 112 OF CHAPTER 25-5 OF THE CITY OF AUSTIN CODE.\nEXPIRATION DATE (25-5-81,LDC) ___________________ CASE MANAGER ___Jim Gobel_______","numLines":100,"startLine":100,"totalLines":277}}}
