{"level":30,"time":1776979988776,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Vez7CSfraNxC1199mKVsks","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rm7GfHG2FRGHu9VFcvMxqa","name":"mcp__conductor_tools__vision","input":{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and identify:\n\n1. Location of the overhead electric line shown on this sheet\n2. Any trees or landscaping elements planted near the overhead electric line (identify which trees or plantings are within 10 feet, 15 feet, 25 feet, or 50 feet of the overhead line)\n3. Species of trees near the overhead electric line (if labeled)\n4. Any utility clearance notes or annotations on the landscape plan\n5. Whether any trees appear to be incompatible with utility clearance requirements\n\nProvide spatial descriptions using the building locations and site areas (e.g., \"south of Buildings 6 and 8, along the southern boundary where the overhead line runs\").\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1433,"cache_read_input_tokens":66529,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1433,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11ce902f-86c5-4003-b16c-9143da511761","uuid":"c4aae053-d420-408e-b2bd-67d6cad0432c"}
{"level":30,"time":1776979988776,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and identify:\n\n1. Location of the overhead electric line shown on this sheet\n2. Any trees or landscaping elements planted near the overhead electric line (identify which trees or plantings are within 10 feet, 15 feet, 25 feet, or 50 feet of the overhead line)\n3. Species of trees near the overhead electric line (if labeled)\n4. Any utility clearance notes or annotations on the landscape plan\n5. Whether any trees appear to be incompatible with utility clearance requirements\n\nProvide spatial descriptions using the building locations and site areas (e.g., \"south of Buildings 6 and 8, along the southern boundary where the overhead line runs\").\n","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (31)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776979988777,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011aMKmSgUXReaG8h2rP4iec","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 3 — Block 19\n     2→\n     3→## text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements for tree pruning, easements, clearances, and relocation costs.\n     4→\n     5→Electric Notes\n     6→1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n     7→2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n     8→3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n     9→4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless require clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n    10→5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\n    11→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8920d43-e944-47ba-ad17-2e6340f56c7c","uuid":"710c37d0-8eeb-4d88-ba34-52fa5e5d592c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-03/block-19.md","content":"# Sheet 3 — Block 19\n\n## text_block: List of 5 notes regarding electric utilities, specifically referencing Austin Energy's requirements for tree pruning, easements, clearances, and relocation costs.\n\nElectric Notes\n1. Austin Energy has the right to prune and/or remove trees, shrubbery and other obstructions to the extent necessary to keep the easements clear. Austin Energy will perform all tree work in compliance with Chapter 25-8, Subchapter B of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n2. The owner/developer of this subdivision/lot shall provide Austin Energy with any easement and/or access required, in addition to those indicated, for the installation and ongoing maintenance of overhead and underground electric facilities. These easements and/or access are required to provide electric service to the building and will not be located so as to cause the site to be out of compliance with Chapter 25-8 of the City of Austin Land Development Code.\n3. The owner shall be responsible for installation of temporary erosion control, revegetation and tree protection. In addition, the owner shall be responsible for any initial tree pruning and tree removal that is within ten feet of the center line of the proposed overhead electric facilities designed to provide electric service to this project. The owner shall include Austin Energy's work within the limits of construction for this project.\n4. The owner of the property is responsible for maintaining clearances required by the National Electric Safety Code, Occupational Safety and Health Administration (OSHA) regulations, City of Austin rules and regulations and Texas state laws pertaining to clearances when working in close proximity to overhead power lines and equipment. Austin Energy will not render electric service unless require clearances are maintained. All costs incurred because of failure to comply with the required clearances will be charged to the owner.\n5. Any relocation of electric facilities shall be at the landowner's/developer's expense.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776979988777,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015aBgyndXKVXPwYVRhkaePH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have the complete picture. The site plan includes:\n\n**Sheet 3 - Block 13: Electric Transmission Notes** (16 notes)\n- No trees within 25 feet of transmission structures\n- No digging/grading within 25 feet of transmission structures\n- **Pre-construction safety meeting REQUIRED with Austin Energy 48 hours before construction**\n- Barricades 10 feet from transmission structures\n- Various other requirements for safety, access, fences, sprinklers, fire hydrants, pavement, etc.\n\n**Sheet 3 - Block 17 & 19: Electric Notes** (5 notes)\n- Austin Energy tree pruning rights\n- Owner responsible for temporary erosion control and tree protection\n- **Owner responsible for maintaining clearances required by NESC, OSHA, COA rules, and Texas law**\n- Relocation costs at owner's expense\n\nSo there IS a 48-hour notification requirement noted, but it's for Austin Energy's transmission staff, not a general \"high-voltage overhead lines\" notification. The grouping requirement EL-1.46 specifies \"48-hour notification requirement per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003\" which is a general requirement when work is near ANY high-voltage overhead lines.\n\nLet me now systematically evaluate each checklist item. I need to:\n\n1. Check if buildings maintain clearances from overhead lines (EL-1.1 through EL-1.3, EL-1.6, EL-1.7, EL-1.8)\n2. Check if there are profile views showing vertical clearances\n3. Check if building elevations show surveyed conductor locations\n4. Check parking, sidewalks, driveways, fences for clearances (EL-1.9 through EL-1.22, EL-1.28, EL-1.29)\n5. Check landscape plan for tree proximity and species (EL-1.37)\n\n\n6. Verify guy wire clearances and transformer placement (EL-1.40 through EL-1.43)\n7. Confirm measurement reference points—whether dimensions originate from conductor or pole (EL-1.23)\n\nI should review the grading plan, building elevations, landscape details, and utility coordination sheets to verify all clearance requirements are met.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2670,"cache_read_input_tokens":61121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2670,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8920d43-e944-47ba-ad17-2e6340f56c7c","uuid":"fa431b51-bfd4-4aa7-924d-d6737d75d5de"}
