{"level":30,"time":1776979988786,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the Landscape Plan and identify:\n\n1. **Proposed trees and vegetation:** Where are trees and shrubs located on this plan? How close are they to transformer pad locations (approximately)?\n\n2. **Species identification:** Are tree species listed or identified by symbols? Can you see any legend or key showing utility-compatible trees vs. others?\n\n3. **Root barrier details:** Are any root barrier details shown or referenced for trees near underground utilities?\n\n4. **Tree setbacks:** Are there any dimension lines or notes showing minimum setbacks for trees from utility infrastructure?\n\nPlease note any trees located within 10 feet of the transformer pad areas visible on the site.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (Sheet 28 of 35 for the \"VALLEY VIEW TOWNHOMES\" project), here is the information regarding your questions:\n\n**1. Proposed trees and vegetation:**\n*   **Locations:** Trees and vegetation are distributed throughout the site, primarily along the property boundaries (top, bottom, right), within the street yard along the left side (Valley View Road), and integrated into the parking areas and courtyard spaces. They are represented by circular symbols of varying sizes.\n*   **Proximity to Transformer Pads:** Transformer pads are **not explicitly labeled or clearly identifiable** on this specific landscape plan sheet. Therefore, their proximity to proposed trees cannot be determined from this document alone. (Note: There is an underground storm drain line labeled \"-SD-\" and an overhead electric line labeled \"-OHE-\" at the bottom property boundary, with trees planted adjacent to the -OHE- line).\n\n**2. Species identification:**\n*   **Species listed/symbols:** Specific biological tree species (e.g., Live Oak, Elm) are **not listed** on this sheet. Instead, trees are categorized by their landscape function or regulatory purpose using symbols (letters) placed near or inside the tree circles.\n*   **Key/Legend:** The \"KEY NOTES\" section identifies these symbols exactly as follows:\n    *   \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n    *   \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n    *   \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n    *   \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"\n*   **Utility-compatible legend:** There is **no legend or key** indicating which trees are utility-compatible versus others.\n\n**3. Root barrier details:**\n*   There are **no root barrier details** shown, noted, or referenced anywhere on this page for trees near underground utilities.\n\n**4. Tree setbacks:**\n*   There are **no dimension lines or specific notes** detailing minimum setbacks for trees from utility infrastructure on this plan.\n\n**Trees within 10 feet of transformer pad areas:**\nBecause transformer pads are not marked or identifiable on this Landscape Plan sheet, it is not possible to determine if any trees are located within 10 feet of them. You will likely need to reference the site's Utility Plan or a combined Site Plan sheet to verify these clearances.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1447,"outputTokens":523,"totalTokens":3702,"reasoningTokens":1732},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do no