{"level":30,"time":1776979988789,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":9,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 9 (Site Plan) and identify:\n1. The location and boundaries of any transmission easements or electric easements shown on the plan\n2. The location of all buildings (Buildings 1-8) relative to any easements\n3. The location of the detention pond/stacked biofiltration pond\n4. The location of the private fire hydrant\n5. The location and routing of internal driveways and parking areas\n6. Any visual indication of transmission structures, poles, conductors, or overhead electric facilities\n7. Any areas marked as \"no-build zones\" or restricted areas\n\nPlease also note if easement boundaries, transmission facilities, or restricted areas are clearly labeled and dimensioned on the plan, or if they appear to be missing or unclear.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 9 (Site Plan) for the Valley View Townhomes, here are the findings corresponding to your requested points:\n\n**1. Location and boundaries of transmission or electric easements**\nThe plan does not explicitly label any \"transmission\" easements, but it does clearly denote several distribution-level electric and utility easements near the property boundaries, delineated by dashed lines:\n*   **East Boundary (middle):** Labeled exactly as `\"5' Electric Easement Vol. 69, Pg. 14 Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"`. The boundary is shown with a dashed line 5 feet inside the property line.\n*   **Southeast Corner:** Labeled exactly as `\"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 5468, Pg. 883 D.R.T.C.Tx.\"`.\n*   **Northeast Corner:** Labeled exactly as `\"5' P.U.E. & 10' D.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"` (Public Utility Easement & Drainage Easement).\n\n**2. Location of all buildings (1-8) relative to easements**\nThe plan features 8 buildings. All buildings appear to be positioned outside of the explicitly labeled utility, drainage, and electric easement boundaries. \n*   **Bldg. 1, Bldg. 2, Bldg. 3:** Located along the northern half of the site. They are situated south of a `\"25'\"` building setback line and away from the northeastern easements.\n*   **Bldg. 4:** Located in the center of the site, fully surrounded by internal driveways, well away from boundary easements.\n*   **Bldg. 5 & Bldg. 6:** Located along the eastern boundary. Bldg. 6 is positioned adjacent to but outside the dashed line marking the `\"5' Electric Easement\"`. \n*   **Bldg. 7 & Bldg. 8:** Located along the southern boundary. They are positioned north of the southern setback line and property line, avoiding boundary easements.\n\n**3. Location of the detention pond/stacked biofiltration pond**\nThe pond is located in the far northeast corner of the site plan. It is exactly labeled `\"Biofiltration / Detention Pond\"` and is enclosed by a `\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"` and bounded to the north and east by a `\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"`.\n\n**4. Location of the private fire hydrant**\nA fire hydrant symbol exactly labeled `\"FH\"` is located in the northeastern quadrant of the site, situated between \"Bldg. 3\" and the \"Biofiltration / Detention Pond\", adjacent to the `\"20' Fire Access Gates\"`. (There is also an off-site existing hydrant labeled `\"FH(Out) 682.03\"` and `\"FH(In) 682.33\"` near the existing water manhole outside the northwest property line).\n\n**5. Location and routing of internal driveways and parking areas**\n*   **Routing:** The main entrance enters from the west property line, labeled `\"Construct Type II Driveway\"`. The driveway proceeds east into the property and splits to form a continuous loop completely encircling the center building (`\"Bldg. 4\"`), providing direct driveway access to the front of all units in Buildings 1 through 8.\n*   **Parking:** Parking consists of garage spaces for the units and select surface spots. As requested, here is the exact transcription of the relevant parking table found on the sheet:\n\n```text\nParking Data\nLand Use                                Residential\nParking Spaces Provided                 10 Surface/ 78 Garage\nCompact Spaces Provided                 0\nADA Spaces Required                     0\nADA Spaces Provided                     0\nTotal Bicycle Spaces Required           5\nLong Term Bicycle Spaces Required       3\nLong Term Bicycle Spaces Provided       39 (1 per Garage)\nShort Term Bicycle Spaces Required      2\nShort Term Bicycle Spaces Provided      2\n```\n\n**6. Visual indication of transmission structures, poles, conductors, or overhead electric facilities**\nThere are no visual indications or labels for major \"transmission\" structures or towers. However, standard overhead distribution lines and poles are present:\n*   A pole labeled `\"Power Pole\"` is located near the northwest corner of the property lines, adjacent to an `\"AT&T Post\"`.\n*   Overhead electric lines are clearly delineated by line types containing `\"---OHE---\"`. These lines run along the western property boundary and extend continuously along the entire southern property boundary.\n\n**7. \"No-build zones\" or restricted areas**\nThe plan does not explicitly use the term \"no-build zone.\" The restricted areas are indicated via property setbacks (such as the `\"25'\"` dashed setback lines shown parallel to the property boundaries) and the specific easements mentioned in Point 1 (e.g., `\"25' Drainage Easement\"`, `\"5' Electric Easement\"`). \n\n**Summary Note on Clarity and Dimensions:**\nThe easement boundaries present on the plan (Drainage, Electric, P.U.E.) are clearly drawn with distinct dashed lines and are explicitly dimensioned in their text labels (e.g., 5', 10', 25'). There is no indication of high-voltage transmission facilities; only standard distribution elements (\"OHE\" and \"Power Pole\") are mapped.","providerM