{"level":30,"time":1776980013600,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Examine the landscape plan drawing and legend closely to identify the specific tree species being planted along the southern boundary where the overhead electric (OHE) line runs. Please:\n\n1. **Identify Tree Species**: For each proposed mitigation tree (marked 'M') along the southern boundary (bottom edge of the drawing), identify what tree species is shown. Look for symbols or callouts that reference the plant list or schedule.\n\n2. **Cross-Reference Legend**: Review the key notes section to find the plant symbols and species list. If a legend is shown relating symbols to species, provide that mapping.\n\n3. **Tree Symbols on Southern Boundary**: List each mitigation tree from west to east along the southern boundary and note:\n   - Its symbol designation (M, M/P, etc.)\n   - The species (if identifiable from the legend or plant schedule)\n   - Any callout numbers or references to the plant list\n\n4. **Plant Schedule Reference**: Are there any callout numbers or references on the landscape plan that direct to a plant schedule table? If so, which plant list items correspond to the southern boundary trees?\n\n5. **Clarify Species**: If the legend uses symbols (circles with patterns) to denote species, explain the symbol meanings.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 28 of 35), here are the specific details regarding the tree species along the southern boundary (bottom edge of the drawing, indicated by the upward-pointing North arrow):\n\n**1. Identify Tree Species**\nThe specific botanical species of the proposed mitigation trees along the southern boundary cannot be identified from this single document. While the trees are clearly marked with labels designating their purpose, there are no plant tags (e.g., alphanumeric abbreviations like \"Qv\" or \"Ul\") attached to these specific trees on this sheet to indicate their species.\n\n**2. Cross-Reference Legend**\nThe \"KEY NOTES\" section on the right side of the page provides legends for hatching and specific functional tree designations, but it **does not contain a plant species list or map graphical tree symbols to specific plant species.**\n\nThe relevant section under the keyed circles lists the following exact text:\n*   \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n*   \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"\n\n**3. Tree Symbols on Southern Boundary**\nScanning the southern boundary (the bottom edge of the site plan above the property line and \"OHE\" designation) from west (left) to east (right), there are six proposed trees inside the limits of construction:\n\n*   **Tree 1 (West-most):**\n    *   Symbol Designation: Labeled with a small circle containing the letter \"M\".\n    *   Species: Unidentifiable.\n    *   Callouts: None present.\n*   **Tree 2:**\n    *   Symbol Designation: Labeled with a small circle containing the letter \"M\".\n    *   Species: Unidentifiable.\n    *   Callouts: None present.\n*   **Tree 3:**\n    *   Symbol Designation: Labeled with a small circle containing the letter \"M\".\n    *   Species: Unidentifiable.\n    *   Callouts: None present.\n*   **Tree 4:**\n    *   Symbol Designation: Labeled with a small circle containing the letter \"M\".\n    *   Species: Unidentifiable.\n    *   Callouts: None present.\n*   **Tree 5:**\n    *   Symbol Designation: Labeled with a small circle containing the letter \"M\".\n    *   Species: Unidentifiable.\n    *   Callouts: None present.\n*   **Tree 6 (East-most):**\n    *   Symbol Designation: Labeled with a small circle containing the letter \"M\".\n    *   Species: Unidentifiable.\n    *   Callouts: None present.\n\n*Note: As defined in the Key Notes, the \"M\" indicates these are \"MITIGATION TREE\"s.*\n\n**4. Plant Schedule Reference**\nThere is **no Plant Schedule, Plant List, or planting table** present anywhere on this specific sheet (Sheet 28). Because there is no schedule on this page, and no callout codes attached to the trees along the southern boundary, it is impossible to correspond these specific trees to list items without referencing other sheets from the full plan set.\n\n**5. Clarify Species Symbols**\nThe plan utilizes different graphical symbols (circles with varying internal line patterns, such as a cross pattern or a branching/starburst pattern) to illustrate the proposed trees. While standard landscape architectural practice dictates that different graphical symbols represent different tree species, the specific meanings of these graphical patterns are **not defined** on this page. The only defined tree symbols on this sheet are the functional text labels (M, SY, P, PL) listed beneath the Key Notes.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1569,"outputTokens":825,"totalTokens":4401,"reasoningTokens":2007},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Examine the landscape plan drawing and legend closely to identify the specific tree species being planted along the southern boundary where the overhead electric (OHE) line runs. Please:\n\n1. **Identify Tree Species**: For each proposed mitigation tree (marked 'M') along the southern boundary (bottom edge of the drawing), identify what tree species is shown. Look for symbols or callouts that reference the plant list or schedule.\n\n2. **Cross-Reference Legend**: Review the key notes section to find the plant symbols and species list. If a legend is shown relating symbols to species, provide that mapping.\n\n3. **Tree Symbols on Southern Boundary**: List each mitigation tree from west to east along the southern boundary and note:\n   - Its symbol designation (M, M/P, etc.)\n   - The species (if identifiable from the legend or plant schedule)\n   - Any callout numbers or references to the plant list\n\n4. **Plant Schedule Reference**: Are there any callout numbers or references on the landscape plan that direct to a plant schedule table? If so, which plant list items correspond to the southern boundary trees?\n\n5. **Clarify Species**: If the legend uses symbols (circles with patterns) to denote species, explain the symbol meanings."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-hdKdWTeGU03YuwEoLbwZMxYo","timestamp":{},