{"level":30,"time":1776980214076,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":1,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01KvdfAgoLMB85cdeFWkYBTY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! I have completed the review of the grouping \"EL-2 — Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\". \n\nMy findings identified:\n- **3 FAIL items**: EL-2.1, EL-2.3, EL-2.15\n  - EL-2.1: Non-utility-compatible trees within 15 feet of distribution conductor (measured at 0.5-4 feet)\n  - EL-2.3: Large trees within 25 feet of distribution conductor (Cedar Elm and Live Oak at 0.5-4 feet)\n  - EL-2.15: Trees in prohibited zones without Austin Energy approval\n\n- **6 NOT-VERIFIABLE items**: EL-2.6, EL-2.7, EL-2.8, EL-2.9, EL-2.11, EL-2.12, EL-2.13\n  - These items involve utilities (poles, pads, underground equipment) that are shown but without specific dimension callouts to verify distances\n  - One item (EL-2.11) involves large tree identification on plans\n  - Two items (EL-2.12, EL-2.13) involve measurement methodology not documented on plans\n  - One item (EL-2.9) involves missing root barrier details\n\n- **4 PASS items (not included in findings)**: EL-2.2 (transmission lines not confirmed as present), EL-2.4 (transmission lines not confirmed), EL-2.5 (transmission easement not present), EL-2.10 (plant legend identifies species), EL-2.14 (trees ARE shown relative to OHE facilities)\n\nThe most critical deficiencies are EL-2.1, EL-2.3, and EL-2.15, which involve trees positioned directly under or very near (0.5-4 feet) the overhead electric line when they should be 15-25 feet away.\n\n\nThe analysis is now complete with all findings documented and categorized.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4985,"cache_read_input_tokens":66543,"cache_creation":{"eph