e canopy that completely overlaps the drawn rectangular area of this transformer pad.\n*   Assuming the center point of the dashed circle represents the tree trunk, this center point is located just slightly to the west/northwest of the pad.\n*   Using the provided 1\" = 20' scale bar, the visual center of this overlapping tree canopy circle appears to be less than 5 feet from the edge of the transformer pad box.\n*   A second large tree canopy symbol is located immediately to the north, overlapping the entrance driveway curve. The southern edge of this canopy appears to touch or come within 1-2 feet of the northern edge of the transformer pad.\n\n**2. Tree symbols visible:**\n*   There are **two (2)** distinct, large dashed circular tree canopy symbols drawn in the immediate vicinity of this specific transformer pad (one overlapping the pad, one just to the north).\n*   Neither of these tree symbols has a specific numerical callout, tag, or species label attached to it on this sheet.\n*   In the bottom left corner of the drawing, there is a box labeled \"**Tree List**\" which states: \"Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\"\n\n**3. Minimum clearance verification:**\n*   Based *strictly on the visual layout* provided on this electrical plan overlay, there does **not** appear to be compliance with a 10-foot minimum lateral clearance from the transformer pad to the tree.\n*   The canopy symbol is drawn directly on top of the pad, and the geometric center of the tree symbol is located less than 10 feet (approximately half the distance of the first 20' segment on the scale bar) from the pad's edge.\n\n**4. Any vegetation details or barriers:**\n*   There are no protective barriers, root barriers, or landscaping notes called out in the area around this western transformer pad on this specific sheet.\n*   The linework shows underground utilities (e.g., a blue line labeled \"Underground Electric Line\") routing directly through the area covered by the overlapping tree canopy symbol.\n\n**5. Comparison to other pads:**\nScanning the document for other elements labeled \"Electrical Transformer Pad\":\n*   **Southwestern Pad (near Bldg 8, Unit 801):** Yes, there is a tree shown near this pad. A large dashed tree canopy symbol is located immediately to the west of this pad. Similar to Pad 1, the canopy symbol completely overlaps the transformer pad. The center of the tree circle appears to be less than 10 feet away.\n*   **Eastern Pad (near Bldg 5, Unit 504):** Yes, there is a tree shown near this pad. A large tree canopy symbol is located to the northeast. The outer edge of the canopy slightly overlaps the pad. The center of this tree circle appears to be approximately 10 to 15 feet away from the pad based on the scale.\n*   **Southeastern Pad (near Bldg 6, Unit 704):** No large tree canopy symbols are shown in close proximity to this pad.\n\n*(Note: This analysis is based solely on the visual representation of symbols on this specific \"Preliminary Electrical Design Plan\" sheet. Engineering plans often use schematic overlays, and actual physical locations may be governed by specific grading or landscaping sheets not present here.)*","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1572,"outputTokens":808,"totalTokens":4405,"reasoningTokens":2025},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2092056]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exac