{"level":30,"time":1776980472993,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"Please examine Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan) and identify:\n\n1. Location of the overhead electric line shown on this sheet\n2. Any trees or landscaping elements planted near the overhead electric line (identify which trees or plantings are within 10 feet, 15 feet, 25 feet, or 50 feet of the overhead line)\n3. Species of trees near the overhead electric line (if labeled)\n4. Any utility clearance notes or annotations on the landscape plan\n5. Whether any trees appear to be incompatible with utility clearance requirements\n\nProvide spatial descriptions using the building locations and site areas (e.g., \"south of Buildings 6 and 8, along the southern boundary where the overhead line runs\").\n","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on the visual analysis of the provided Landscape Plan (labeled Sheet 28 of 35 in the bottom right corner), here are the findings regarding your specific questions:\n\n**1. Location of the overhead electric line**\nAn overhead electric line, designated by the linetype label **-OHE-**, runs horizontally along the entire southern boundary of the site plan. It is located south of the main building footprints and the southern drive aisle/parking area.\n\n**2. Trees or landscaping elements planted near the overhead electric line**\nThere are several trees planted along the southern property boundary in close proximity to the -OHE- line. \n*   Based on the provided graphic scale (\"SCALE IN FEET 1\"=20'-0'\"), the trunks (center points) of these trees appear to be planted approximately **10 to 20 feet** away from the overhead electric line.\n*   The drawn canopies of at least five of these trees along the southern boundary completely intersect and overlap the -OHE- line.\n*   Specific trees in this area include several marked with an **\"M\"** tag, which the legend defines as a \"MITIGATION TREE\". There is a notable cluster of these \"M\" labeled trees in the southeastern corner near the -OHE- line, and at least one near the southwestern corner.\n\n**3. Species of trees near the overhead electric line**\n**No tree species are labeled on this sheet.** The plan uses functional tags (such as \"M\" for Mitigation Tree, \"ST\" for Street Yard Tree, etc.) inside the tree symbols, but there is no plant schedule or detailed annotation on this page providing botanical or common species names.\n\n**4. Utility clearance notes or annotations**\n**None found.** There are no notes, annotations, or details regarding utility clearance requirements, safe planting distances from power lines, or utility provider guidelines visible anywhere on this sheet.\n\n**5. Incompatibility with utility clearance requirements**\nDefinitive incompatibility cannot be confirmed solely from this sheet because the specific tree species (and their mature heights) and the local utility's specific clearance rules are not listed here. However, **visually, the plan shows multiple large tree canopies directly overlapping the overhead electric line**. In standard landscaping and utility practice, planting large shade or mitigation trees directly under or within 10-15 feet of an overhead electric line (where their mature canopy would intersect the wires) is typically incompatible with standard utility clearance requirements and often requires revision.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1463,"outputTokens":516,"totalTokens":4487,"reasoningTokens":2508},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary fi