a transmission easement area**\nSince no transmission easement is indicated on this sheet, there are no identifiable grading or site modifications occurring within one. Grading is shown extensively across the rest of the site (via spot elevations, contour lines, and retaining walls), but not in relation to a transmission easement.\n\n**5. Annotations or notes referencing transmission facility clearances or restrictions**\nThere are no annotations or notes referencing transmission facility clearances or restrictions on this sheet. The notes present are standard civil engineering notes (Legend, Benchmarks, Legal Description, Curb Note, and a standard \"Texas 811 - Call Before You Dig!!\" warning with general utility field verification instructions).\n\n**6. Location of the detention/biofiltration pond relative to any easements**\nIn the northeastern corner of the site (adjacent to Buildings 3 and 5), there is a structured basin area labeled **\"Sedimentation\"** surrounded by retaining wall callouts (e.g., \"TW 681.00\"). This basin is located immediately adjacent to (west of) a **\"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"** and borders a **\"7.5' P.U.E.\"** along the northern property boundary. \n\n**7. Easement boundaries and restricted areas marked with dimensions and instrument numbers**\nYes, the standard easements that *are* present on the site are clearly marked with dashed lines, dimensions, and instrument numbers. Examples transcribed exactly as they appear include:\n*   \"5' P.U.E. Vol. 99, Pg. 14 P.R.T.C.Tx\" (Northern boundary)\n*   \"7.5' P.U.E. Vol. 99, Pg. 14 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Northeastern boundary)\n*   \"25' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Eastern boundary)\n*   \"15' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Eastern boundary)\n*   \"5' Electric Easement Vol. 66, Pg. 14\" (Eastern boundary)\n*   \"5' Elec. Easement Vol. 66, Pg. 14 P.R.T.C.Tx\" (Southern boundary)\n*   \"5' Elec. & Tele. Easement Vol. 3458, Pg. 885 D.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Southeastern corner)\n*   \"25' Building Setback Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\" (Western boundary)\n\n**Discrepancies Note:**\nWhile Sheet 3 is not included in this single-image review, if Sheet 3's general notes establish requirements for showing transmission facilities, clearances, or buffers, **Sheet 11 fails to reflect them entirely**. There is a complete absence of any transmission-specific infrastructure, boundaries, or clearance zones depicted on this grading plan.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1472,"outputTokens":873,"totalTokens":4971,"reasoningTokens":2626},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2337396]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail wit