ral labels reading exactly \"Fire Lane\" are placed along this dashed route throughout the loop.\n\n**Passage near transformer pads:** Because transformer pads are not depicted or labeled on this specific sheet, it is not possible to determine if the fire lanes pass near or alongside them based on this document.\n\n**3. Fire zone clearances:**\n*   **Fire Lane Widths:** There are several dimension lines crossing the designated fire lanes that specify a width of **26'**.\n*   **Other Dimensions:** There are dimensions indicating distances between buildings across drive aisles (e.g., **28'** between Bldg. 2 and Bldg. 8; **27.3'** between Bldg. 4 and Bldg. 6) and various turning radii marked (e.g., **R30'**, **R40'**, **R10'**).\n*   **Clearance from Equipment:** I have reviewed the \"Fire Zone Notes,\" general \"Notes,\" and the drawing area. There are **no dimension lines or text notes** on this sheet specifying required clearances specifically from transformer pads or other utility equipment to the fire lanes or fire hydrants.\n\n**4. Proximity to transformers:**\nAs noted in your prompt, transformer pad locations are marked on Sheet 21. The document provided for analysis is Sheet 10. Because transformer pad locations are not visible on this sheet, I cannot visually estimate their distance to the fire hydrants or fire lanes. Additionally, there are no exterior features explicitly labeled as \"fire escape\" or \"stairwell\" on these building footprints to measure against."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94b43057-6c8d-4501-ab55-21f141703f72","uuid":"0ddac54e-aed6-4d3d-8679-086b12a3d9f6","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a visual analysis of the provided document, which is titled \"Fire Protection Plan\" (Sheet 10 of 39), here is the information requested:\n\n**1. Fire hydrant locations:**\nThere are three fire hydrants identified on this plan:\n*   **Existing Fire Hydrant:** Located in the top left corner of the drawing, outside the main