{"level":30,"time":1776980473002,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011DGxdzYkxDmFN6jrPj2JuD","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided Preliminary Electrical Design Plan, here are the observations regarding the westernmost Transformer Pad (located near the main entrance curve and the western property line, adjacent to Bldg 2) and the surrounding elements:\n\n**1. Tree locations relative to Pad 1:**\nLooking specifically at the rectangular box indicated by the leader line for \"Electrical Transformer Pad\" on the central-western edge (near Unit 201):\n*   There is a large dashed circular symbol representing a tree canopy that completely overlaps the drawn rectangular area of this transformer pad.\n*   Assuming the center point of the dashed circle represents the tree trunk, this center point is located just slightly to the west/northwest of the pad.\n*   Using the provided 1\" = 20' scale bar, the visual center of this overlapping tree canopy circle appears to be less than 5 feet from the edge of the transformer pad box.\n*   A second large tree canopy symbol is located immediately to the north, overlapping the entrance driveway curve. The southern edge of this canopy appears to touch or come within 1-2 feet of the northern edge of the transformer pad.\n\n**2. Tree symbols visible:**\n*   There are **two (2)** distinct, large dashed circular tree canopy symbols drawn in the immediate vicinity of this specific transformer pad (one overlapping the pad, one just to the north).\n*   Neither of these tree symbols has a specific numerical callout, tag, or species label attached to it on this sheet.\n*   In the bottom left corner of the drawing, there is a box labeled \"**Tree List**\" which states: \"Refer to landscape plan sheet 32 for the tree list.\"\n\n**3. Minimum cle