{"level":30,"time":1776980473013,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":8,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DJxjSjDShb3QFJPPhfeXzS","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 9 (Site Plan) of the provided real estate development submission, here are the locations and exact labeling of the requested features. \n\n### 1. Buildings\nThe site contains 8 primary buildings configured around a central drive loop. Building footprints are marked with a thick outline, and walls are indicated by the perimeter lines of these footprints.\n*   **Bldg. 1:** Northwest corner. Labeled `\"Bldg. 1\"`, `\"3,290 sf\"`, `\"FFE= 687.50\"`. Contains Units 101-104.\n*   **Bldg. 2:** West-central area, south of Bldg. 1. Labeled `\"Bldg. 2\"`, `\"4,930 sf\"`, `\"FFE= 686.50\"`. Contains Units 201-206.\n*   **Bldg. 3:** North-central area, east of Bldg. 1. Labeled `\"Bldg. 3\"`, `\"4,144 sf\"`, `\"FFE= 685.50\"`. Contains Units 301-305.\n*   **Bldg. 4:** Center of the site loop. Labeled `\"Bldg. 4\"`, `\"4,144 sf\"`, `\"FFE= 685.50\"`. Contains Units 401-405.\n*   **Bldg. 5:** Northeast corner. Labeled `\"Bldg. 5\"`, `\"3,290 sf\"`, `\"FFE= 683.0\"`. Contains Units 501-504.\n*   **Bldg. 6:** East-central area, south of Bldg. 5. Labeled `\"Bldg. 6\"`, `\"3,290 sf\"`, `\"FFE= 683.0\"`. Contains Units 601-604.\n*   **Bldg. 7:** Southeast area. Labeled `\"Bldg. 7\"`, `\"4,144 sf\"`, `\"FFE= 685.0\"`. Contains Units 701-705.\n*   **Bldg. 8:** Southwest area. Labeled `\"Bldg. 8\"`, `\"4,997 sf\"`, `\"FFE= 685.50\"`. Contains Units 801-806.\n\n### 2. Parking Areas\n*   **Garages / Driveways:** Individual driveways lead from the main drive aisles to each unit's garage. The \"Parking Data\" table notes `\"Parking Spaces Provided: 10 Surface/ 78 Garage\"`.\n*   **Surface Parking Stalls:** Standard striped perpendicular surface parking stalls are located directly off the main drive loop (e.g., a grouping of parallel/angled lines can be seen north of the drive aisle between Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 3). \n*   **Drive-Through Areas / Aisles:** A continuous loop driveway serves the site. The entrance off Valley View Road is labeled `\"Construct Type III Driveway\"`. The internal loop consists of a northern aisle serving Bldgs 1, 3, 5 and a southern aisle serving Bldgs 2, 8, 7, 6. The aisles are bordered by `\"Ribbon Curb\"` and `\"Curb & Gutter (Typ.)\"`.\n\n### 3. Fire Hydrants\n*   **On-Site:** A private fire hydrant is indicated by the symbol `\"FH\"` located on the eastern side of the property. It is situated on the water line loop just south of Unit 504 (Building 5) and north of Building 6.\n*   **Off-Site / Street:** An off-site hydrant is shown outside the western property boundary on the main street, labeled near an `\"Existing Water Manhole\"`.\n\n### 4. Dumpsters\n*   There is no explicit large \"Dumpster\" or \"Trash Enclosure\" footprint labeled on the plan. \n*   Instead, the **\"Trash Collection Notes\"** (bottom center) state: `\"1. Trash containers shall not be left at curb side unattended. Signs must be posted on the building or at a location that is publicly visible indicating that trash containers may not be left at curbside prior to report violations.\"` This indicates the use of individual rollout bins rather than a central dumpster pad.\n\n### 5. Retaining Walls\nRetaining walls are heavily utilized along the perimeter of the site due to grading:\n*   **North Perimeter:** Labeled `\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall\"`, `\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"`, and `\"End Concrete Retaining Wall\"` running eastward past Building 3 and along the northern edge of the `\"Detention Pond\"`.\n*   **East Perimeter:** Near Building 6, a wall is labeled `\"Existing Retaining Wall to be Replaced\"`.\n*   **South Perimeter:** Along the southern boundary, labels include `\"Begin Concrete Retaining Wall at Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\"`, `\"Tie to Existing Concrete Retaining Wall\"`, and several segments labeled `\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"`.\n*   **Detention Pond:** The pond area in the northeast includes a `\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"` alongside a `\"Concrete Retaining Wall\"`.\n\n### 6. Sidewalks\n*   **Public Frontage:** A `\"Construct 5' Concrete Sidewalk See Dtl 432S-1\"` runs continuously along the western property line outside the fence (Valley View Road frontage).\n*   **Internal Concrete Walks:** Labeled `\"Construct 4' Concrete Sidewalk (Typ.)\"` routes parallel to the drive aisles, connecting the driveways in front of the building units.\n*   **Granite Walkways:** Alternative paths are labeled `\"4' Wide Decomposed Granite Walkway\"`. One connects the area between Bldg. 1 and Bldg. 3; another is visible north of Building 4 near the `\"Detention Pond\"`.\n\n### 7. Fences\n*   A perimeter fence line is denoted by a dashed line with \"x\" symbols (`-x-x-x-`).\n*   On the eastern property boundary, this line is explicitly labeled `\"Wood Fence\"`.\n*   Around the detention pond, there is a `\"Pond Perimeter Fence\"`.\n*   The **\"Fence Note\"** (bottom right) states: `\"Post holes that are to be installed near a trees Critical Root Zone (CRZ) will be dug by hand...\"`.\n\n### 8. Bicycle Racks\n*   A bicycle parking pad is located just east of the main entrance, in the island between Building 1 and Building 2.\n*   It is labeled: `\"(2) Short Term Bicycle Parking Spaces See Site Details 719S-1\"`. \n\n### 9. Light Poles\n*   No standalone exterior parking lot light poles (or pole bases) are explicitly labeled on the plan view.\n*   The **\"Lighting Note\"** (bottom left) specifies: `\"All exterior lighting will be full cut-off and fully shielded... All site lighting to be located on the building will be in compliance with Subchapter E...\"` \n*   **\"Figure 34\"** provides `\"Examples of Fully-Shielded Light Fixtures\"` which appear to be wall-mounted sconces, supporting the note that lighting will be building-mounted.\n\n### 10. Fire Lanes\n*   The main internal loop functions as the emergency access route. The entrances are labeled `\"Construct Type III Driveway\"`.\n*   While there is no explicit `\"Fire Lane - No Parking\"` striping text painted directly onto the drive aisles in this specific view, the drive loop maintains an open width with an inside turning radius labeled `\"R25'\"` to accommodate emergency vehicles.\n\n### 11. Property Lines\n*   The property boundaries are indicated by thick, bold dashed lines (dash-dot-dot pattern) enclosing the site. \n*   The western line borders `\"Valley View Road\"`. The northern, eastern, and southern lines border adjacent parcels labeled `\"Existing Apartment Building\"` and `\"Clarion Ridge Condominiums\"`. Metes and bounds data (e.g., `\"N 62° 02' 28'' E\"`, `\"119.56'\"`) run continuously along these property lines.\n\n### 12. Easements\nSeveral easements are delineated with dashed boundary lines:\n*   **Western Frontage:** Includes a `\"Sidewalk Easement\"` and a `\"Wastewater Easement\"`.\n*   **Northern Boundary:** Includes a `\"5' P.U.E. Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"` (Public Utility Easement).\n*   **Eastern Boundary:** Includes a `\"15' Drainage Easement Vol. 73, Pg. 76 P.R.T.C.Tx.\"` and an adjacent `\"25' Drainage Easement\"`.\n*   **Southern Boundary:** Includes a broad `\"20' Drainage Easement\"`.\n*   **Internal Site:** An `\"Exclusive Water Line Vault Easement\"` is located in the southwestern quadrant, north of Building 8."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ccf6950-9428-47a1-a0e1-f1b6954e2e70","uuid":"9fc48b0c-145c-4610-9d4e-a8c86c9a1611","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of Sheet 9 (Site Plan) of the provided real estate development submission, here are the locations and exact labeling of the requested features. \n\n### 1. Buildings\nThe site contains 8 primary buildings configured around a central drive loop. Building