{"level":30,"time":1776980659765,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VSQqiLXqFX7knB98rQ47Hd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've provided the structured output with my findings. Let me verify I've covered all the major deficiencies:\n\n**DEFICIENCIES DOCUMENTED (FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE):**\n\n1. **EL-1.1** - Buildings 7.5-ft horizontal clearance - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no building elevations with surveyed conductor elevations)\n2. **EL-1.2** - 15-foot radial clearance from distribution conductors - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no radial clearance dimensions)\n3. **EL-1.3** - Building projections clearances - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no building elevations)\n4. **EL-1.6** - Buildings in ROW adjacent to site - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no building setback/conductor documentation)\n5. **EL-1.7** - Surveyed conductor elevations on building elevations - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no building elevation sheets)\n6. **EL-1.8** - Section/profile exhibits with clearance dimensions - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no section views)\n7. **EL-1.9** - Fences 7.5-ft sky-to-ground clearance - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no clearance dimensions)\n8. **EL-1.10** - Fence posts 10-ft from poles - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no dimensions)\n9. **EL-1.12** - Transmission line fencing (non-conductive, grounded) - NOT-VERIFIABLE (transmission easement not shown, no fence specs)\n10. **EL-1.14** - Retaining walls 7.5-ft clearance - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no clearance dimensions)\n11. **EL-1.17** - Retaining walls section exhibits - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no section views with dimensions)\n\n\n12. **EL-1.18** - Driveways 16-18-ft vertical clearance - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no vertical clearance dimensions, no surveyor data)\n13. **EL-1.19** - Vehicle parking vertical clearance - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no vertical clearance dimensions)\n14. **EL-1.20** - Roads/driveways 30-ft clearance from transmission - NOT-VERIFIABLE (transmission easement not shown, no clearance dimensions)\n15. **EL-1.23** - Clearance dimensions from conductor (not pole) - FAIL (no dimensions shown at all)\n16. **EL-1.26** - Trash areas - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no clearance documentation)\n17. **EL-1.27** - Facilities under/over distribution or within easements - NOT-VERIFIABLE (transmission easement boundary not shown, 7.5-ft clearance within easement not documented)\n18. **EL-1.31** - Survey data for marginal vertical clearances - FAIL (driveways/parking may have marginal clearances, no surveyor data provided)\n19. **EL-1.36** - Decorative lighting under overhead lines - NOT-VERIFIABLE (clearance dimensions not documented)\n20. **EL-1.37** - Trees within 10/50 lateral feet - NOT-VERIFIABLE (transmission easement not shown, tree distances not dimensioned, species not verified)\n21. **EL-1.40** - Down guy conflicts with paths/driveways - FAIL (down guy with potential path/driveway interference not resolved)\n22. **EL-1.41** - Guy easements for transmission - NOT-VERIFIABLE (transmission easement exhibit doesn't show guy easements)\n23. **EL-1.42** - Down guy anchor easements for distribution - NOT-VERIFIABLE (down guy anchors not shown despite power pole on site)\n24. **EL-1.43** - Transformers 7.5-ft vertical clearance - NOT-VERIFIABLE (no cross-section/elevation with clearance dimensions)\n25. **EL-1.46** - 48-hour notification note - FAIL (required note not included on plans)\n\nI've identified 25 separate deficiencies across the electrical clearance requirements. The fundamental problem is the absence of building elevations with actual conductor measurements, which cascades through the entire review—without surveyed heights and positions, I can't verify clearances for structures, equipment, vegetation, or easement compliance.\n\nThe plans lack any dimensional callouts showing vertical separations, the transmission easement boundary referenced in the code isn't depicted, there's no survey data documenting conductor locations, the mandatory notification language is missing, and down guy anchors remain undocumented despite visible infrastructure on site. These gaps represent a systematic failure to address the electrical clearance documentation requirements.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9052,"cache_read_input_tokens":75364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9052,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eda7f2a1-6294-41b6-8e72-831ed9038702","uuid":"1c571d55-277e-4550-8631-e2c824ee7b94"}
{"level":30,"time":1776980659765,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VSQqiLXqFX7knB98rQ47Hd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the site plan review for the Electric Line Clearances grouping (EL-MD-EXP 1.md). \n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nThis grouping is **applicable** to the Valley View Townhomes project, which includes:\n- Existing overhead electric distribution facilities (poles and conductors shown on site plan)\n- A transmission easement with specific requirements documented in Sheet 3 general notes\n- Proposed buildings, driveways, parking areas, detention pond, retaining walls, fences, and landscaping\n\n### Critical Systemic Issues Identified:\n\n1. **Missing Transmission Easement Depiction**: Sheet 3 contains extensive transmission easement requirements (25-foot no-dig/no-grade buffer, no permanent structures, no detention ponds, 20-foot clearance for staging, requirements for roads to support 46,000 lb. loads). However, **the transmission easement boundary is not shown on the site plan or grading plan** (Sheets 9 and 11).\n\n2. **No Building Elevation Documentation**: No building elevation sheets provided showing surveyed conductor elevations, clearance dimensions, or verification of required clearances from outside conductors to building faces, projections, or roof edges.\n\n3. **Missing Clearance Dimensions Everywhere**: Horizontal and vertical clearance dimensions from outer conductors to site features are not documented anywhere on the plans.\n\n4. **No Vertical Clearance Survey Data**: Driveways and parking areas lack registered surveyor mid-span clearance data to verify minimum 16-18 foot vertical clearances from overhead lines.\n\n5. **Down Guy Wires Not Depicted**: Despite Sheet 3 requirements for 25-foot buffers from down guy anchors, no down guy wire locations, anchor points, or easements are shown despite the presence of a power pole on the site.\n\n6. **48-Hour Notification Requirement Missing**: Required note for owner/contractor notification to Austin Energy before work near high-voltage lines is not included.\n\n### Findings Output\n\nI have documented **25 items as FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE**, including:\n- **4 FAIL findings** (clearance dimensions not measured from conductor; no surveyor data for marginal clearances; down guys not shown; 48-hour notification note missing)\n- **21 NOT-VERIFIABLE findings** (missing building elevations, clearance dimensions, vertical clearance survey data, transmission easement boundaries, and related documentation)\n\nThe structured output has been provided and includes specific references to applicable code sections, sheet numbers, and areas of non-compliance."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9052,"cache_read_input_tokens":75364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9052,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eda7f2a1-6294-41b6-8e72-831ed9038702","uuid":"2bfe0b6a-5c38-4cef-8578-d730a568b61d"}
{"level":30,"time":1776980659765,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":6,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":1736797,"duration_api_ms":195196,"num_turns":26,"result":"I have completed the site plan review for the Electric Line Clearances grouping (EL-MD-EXP 1.md). \n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nThis grouping is **applicable** to the Valley View Townhomes project, which includes:\n- Existing overhead electric distribution facilities (poles and conductors shown on site plan)\n- A transmission easement with specific requirements documented in Sheet 3 general notes\n- Proposed buildings, driveways, parking areas, detention pond, retaining walls, fences, and landscaping\n\n### Critical Systemic Issues Identified:\n\n1. **Missing Transmission Easement Depiction**: Sheet 3 contains extensive transmission easement requirements (25-foot no-dig/no-grade buffer, no permanent structures, no detention ponds, 20-foot clearance for staging, requirements for roads to support 46,000 lb. loads). However, **the transmission easement boundary is not shown on the site plan or grading plan** (Sheets 9 and 11).\n\n2. **No Building Elevation Documentation**: No building elevation sheets provided showing surveyed conductor elevations, clearance dimensions, or verification of required clearances from outside conductors to building faces, projections, or roof edges.\n\n3. **Missing Clearance Dimensions Everywhere**: Horizontal and vertical clearance dimensions from outer conductors to site features are not documented anywhere on the plans.\n\n4. **No Vertical Clearance Survey Data**: Driveways and parking areas lack registered surveyor mid-span clearance data to verify minimum 16-18 foot vertical clearances from overhead lines.\n\n5. **Down Guy Wires Not Depicted**: Despite Sheet 3 requirements for 25-foot buffers from down guy anchors, no down guy wire locations, anchor points, or easements are shown despite the presence of a power pole on the site.\n\n6. **48-Hour Notification Requirement Missing**: Required note for owner/contractor notification to Austin Energy before work near high-voltage lines is not included.\n\n### Findings Output\n\nI have documented **25 items as FAIL or NOT-VERIFIABLE**, including:\n- **4 FAIL findings** (clearance dimensions not measured from conductor; no surveyor data for marginal clearances; down guys not shown; 48-hour notification note missing)\n- **21 NOT-VERIFIABLE findings** (missing building elevations, clearance dimensions, vertical clearance survey data, transmission easement boundaries, and related documentation)\n\nThe structured output has been provided and includes specific references to applicable code sections, sheet numbers, and areas of non-compliance.","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"eda7f2a1-6294-41b6-8e72-831ed9038702","total_cost_usd":0.41871994999999995,"usage":{"input_tokens":9290,"cache_creation_input_tokens":186465,"cache_read_input_tokens":814937,"output_tokens":18971,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":186465},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":9290,"outputTokens":18971,"cacheReadInputTokens":814937,"cacheCreationInputTokens":186465,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.41871994999999995,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"grouping":"1","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.1","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows buildings and overhead distribution lines but does not include building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevations or horizontal clearance dimensions from the outside conductor to building faces, overhangs, or roof edges. Compliance with the 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance requirement cannot be verified without these documented clearances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.2","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows buildings and distribution lines but does not document radial clearance dimensions from the outside conductor of distribution primary and neutral conductors to building faces or structures. The required 15-foot radial clearance cannot be verified from available plan documentation."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.3","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"No building elevation sheets provided showing building projections (overhangs, awnings, balconies, decks, patios) with clearance dimensions from the outside conductor. Both 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances for building projections cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["buildings adjacent to western and southern property boundaries"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead distribution lines shown on site plan along western and southern property boundaries. Building setback distances from property lines and surveyed conductor elevations/locations are not documented. Compliance with 7.5-foot horizontal and 15-foot radial clearances from overhead facilities adjacent to site cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.7","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan does not include building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor elevation data and clearance dimension annotations from registered surveyor. Registered surveyor data required to verify clearances from overhead electric facilities is not provided."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.8","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all buildings"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan and grading plan do not include section or profile view exhibits showing dimension lines from outer electric conductor to outermost edges of buildings and building projections. Clearance verification cannot be completed without these cross-sectional exhibits."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["pond perimeter fence and property perimeter fences"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows fences (pond perimeter fence and landscape privacy fences) but does not document clearance dimensions from the outside conductor of overhead electric lines to fence faces. The required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.10","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["property perimeter and pond perimeter fences"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows a power pole near the northwest corner and fence locations but does not include dimension annotations verifying fence post locations maintain minimum 10-foot horizontal clearance from the electric pole."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["pond perimeter fence"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows a transmission easement on Sheet 3 with transmission line requirements stating fencing within the easement must be non-conductive and properly grounded. The transmission easement boundary is not shown on the site plan, and specifications for fence material, construction, and grounding details are not provided. Fencing materials and grounding compliance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.14","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["retaining walls on site perimeter and around detention pond"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan and grading plan show retaining walls around detention pond and site perimeter but do not document clearance dimensions from the outside conductor of overhead electric lines to wall surfaces. The required 7.5-foot horizontal sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.17","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["retaining walls on site perimeter and around detention pond"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Grading plan shows retaining wall locations but does not include cross-section exhibits with dimension lines showing clearances from the outer electric conductor to retaining wall faces. Clearance verification requires section views with documented dimensions."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.18","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["internal driveways"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan and grading plan show driveways but do not document vertical clearance dimensions from the lowest point of overhead electric facilities (including telecommunications attachments) to finished driveway grades. No registered surveyor mid-span clearance data provided to verify the minimum 16-foot vertical clearance requirement is maintained."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.6.2"],"applicableAreas":["surface parking areas and garage areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows 10 surface parking spaces and 78 garage parking spaces beneath buildings but does not document minimum vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric lines to finished grades. Vertical clearance requirements (16 feet for parking areas without truck traffic) cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.20","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.14.0"],"applicableAreas":["internal driveways, site grading areas adjacent to transmission easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 specifies requirements for roads and driveways within transmission easements, including 30-foot vertical clearance from transmission lines to ground surface and 46,000 lb. tandem axle structural requirements. The transmission easement boundary is not depicted on the grading plan, and no vertical clearance dimensions or structural capacity specifications are documented. Transmission structure locations are not shown, preventing verification of compliance."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.23","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all plan sheets with potential clearance dimensions"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan documentation provides no clearance dimensions annotated on any plans. Where clearances are depicted, dimension lines must originate from the outside conductor (not pole centerline or pole structure). Since no dimensions are shown, the requirement to measure from the outside conductor cannot be verified. All dimensions must be revised to originate from the actual conductor location."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.26","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["trash enclosure/receptacle locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan does not clearly identify trash enclosure locations relative to overhead electric facilities. Clearance verification for trash bin receptacles beneath overhead lines cannot be completed without documented clearance dimensions accounting for trash bin raised height during service collection."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.27","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all buildings, detention pond, driveways, parking, fences, structures within transmission easement"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 references a transmission easement with specific prohibitions on permanent structures, detention ponds, and facilities that would impair Austin Energy access. The transmission easement boundary is not depicted on the site plan or grading plan. Compliance with the prohibition against customer facilities under/over distribution lines and the 7.5-foot clearance requirement for items within electric easements cannot be verified without the easement boundary clearly shown."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.31","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["driveways, parking areas"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Driveways and parking areas appear to be located beneath or adjacent to overhead electric facilities with potentially marginal vertical clearances. No registered surveyor data showing pole locations and mid-span clearance measurements are provided. When overhead facilities may not meet minimum vertical clearance requirements, a registered surveyor survey is required to document clearances at midspan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["exterior lighting fixtures"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape and site plans show exterior lighting is required (Site Plan notes require full cut-off, fully shielded fixtures per Subchapter E 2.5) but do not document clearance verification dimensions showing the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground and 15-foot radial clearances from overhead electric lines to decorative lighting fixtures."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["landscape planting areas within transmission easement and adjacent to overhead conductors"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 transmission requirements specify no trees planted within 25 feet of transmission structures and within the transmission easement. The transmission easement boundary is not shown on the landscape plan, and tree locations are not dimensioned with lateral clearances from transmission structure bases or conductors. Landscape plan does not verify that proposed tree species are utility-compatible per ECM Appendix F, nor document distances from transmission and distribution conductors."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.40","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.17.0"],"applicableAreas":["site perimeter where down guy wires from distribution poles may exist"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Sheet 3 transmission notes explicitly reference down guy anchors from transmission and distribution poles, specifying 25-foot no-dig buffer and restrictions on structures/paths conflicting with down guys. Site plan does not show down guy wire locations, anchor points, or related easements despite the power pole visible at northwest corner. Down guy wire conflicts with proposed accessible paths and driveways cannot be resolved without these features depicted."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.41","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["transmission structure guy anchorages"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan references a transmission easement on Sheet 3, but the easement exhibit (Plat Sheet 2) does not show or describe guy easements for transmission down guys, which require 10-foot width either side of guy wire plus 50-foot extension beyond anchor point."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.42","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["distribution pole down guy anchor on site"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":2},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":9}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan shows power pole near northwest corner but does not depict down guy anchor locations or dedicated easements. Easement exhibit does not show down guy anchor easement boundaries (10-foot width extending 5 feet past anchor ground entry point) required for distribution poles."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.43","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["pole-mounted and pad-mounted transformers shown on electrical plan"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical design plan shows transformer locations but does not provide cross-section or elevation views with vertical clearance dimensions from overhead electric line conductors to the top of transformer equipment. The minimum 7.5-foot vertical sky-to-ground clearance cannot be verified."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["cover sheet and general notes"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Site plan set contains overhead electric lines on property and will involve construction activities. Plans do not include the required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. This notification requirement must be added to the cover sheet or general notes."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"d952f42b-4902-498f-94e4-dc2a8f43dd43"}
