{"level":30,"time":1776980659767,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SFZLZyozNn8DUH5w35dt9U","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 11 — Grading Plan\n     2→\n     3→This sheet displays the detailed grading plan for the development site.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet presents the Grading Plan for the Valley View Townhomes multi-family development located at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas. Its primary purpose is to detail existing and proposed topography, establish building finished floor elevations (FFEs), map storm drainage infrastructure, and indicate the location of retaining walls and utility easements across the site.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values**:\n    10→*   **Scale**: 1\" = 20'\n    11→*   **Benchmark 1**: Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n    12→*   **Benchmark 2**: Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n    13→*   **Bldg 1**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 687.50\n    14→*   **Bldg 2**: 4,830 sf | FFE = 685.50\n    15→*   **Bldg 3**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n    16→*   **Bldg 4**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n    17→*   **Bldg 5**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n    18→*   **Bldg 6**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n    19→*   **Bldg 7**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.00\n    20→*   **Bldg 8**: 4,997 sf | FFE = 685.50\n    21→*   **ADA Ramp Maximum Slope**: 8.33%\n    22→*   **Level Landing Maximum Slope**: 2%\n    23→\n    24→**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n    25→\n    26→*   **Block 2**: Main site grading drawing showing the layout of the 8 buildings, proposed/existing contours, retaining walls, storm drainage, and various utility easements. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, specific contour line variations, spot elevations, and the exact placement of infrastructure and adjacent property boundaries.\n    27→*   **Block 7**: Plan legend detailing line types and symbols for contours, limits of construction, storm drains, curb details, and ADA compliance parameters. READ for exact symbol definitions and maximum allowable slopes.\n    28→*   **Block 3**: Benchmark specifications detailing the exact vertical control points (Mag Nail in Asphalt) for the site. READ for exact baseline elevation data.\n    29→*   **Block 5**: Curb grading note detailing conditions for catch curbs vs. spill curbs. READ for grading flow instructions. \n    30→*   **Block 6**: Tree list reference directing the user to landscape plan sheet 32. READ for sheet reference.\n    31→*   **Block 4**: Legal description of the subject property (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision). READ to confirm property identity.\n    32→*   **Block 1**: Graphic scale bar. READ to confirm the 1\" = 20' measurement baseline.\n    33→*   **Blocks 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14**: Boilerplate & Administrative information, including the Texas 811 call warning, engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), project metadata (Sheet 11 of 39, Project No. RJ3 70496), title block, and standard utility and design disclaimers. READ for project details or administrative tracking; otherwise, these can be skipped during a technical review.\n    34→\n    35→---\n    36→\n    37→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    38→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8920d43-e944-47ba-ad17-2e6340f56c7c","uuid":"ee897ced-2081-494e-afbd-d1a826961541","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-11/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 11 — Grading Plan\n\nThis sheet displays the detailed grading plan for the development site.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet presents the Grading Plan for the Valley View Townhomes multi-family development located at 3759 Valley View Road, Austin, Texas. Its primary purpose is to detail existing and proposed topography, establish building finished floor elevations (FFEs), map storm drainage infrastructure, and indicate the location of retaining walls and utility easements across the site.\n\n**Key values**:\n*   **Scale**: 1\" = 20'\n*   **Benchmark 1**: Elevation = 678.52' NAVD 88\n*   **Benchmark 2**: Elevation = 681.08' NAVD 88\n*   **Bldg 1**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 687.50\n*   **Bldg 2**: 4,830 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 3**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 4**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **Bldg 5**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n*   **Bldg 6**: 3,290 sf | FFE = 683.00\n*   **Bldg 7**: 4,144 sf | FFE = 685.00\n*   **Bldg 8**: 4,997 sf | FFE = 685.50\n*   **ADA Ramp Maximum Slope**: 8.33%\n*   **Level Landing Maximum Slope**: 2%\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet**:\n\n*   **Block 2**: Main site grading drawing showing the layout of the 8 buildings, proposed/existing contours, retaining walls, storm drainage, and various utility easements. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, specific contour line variations, spot elevations, and the exact placement of infrastructure and adjacent property boundaries.\n*   **Block 7**: Plan legend detailing line types and symbols for contours, limits of construction, storm drains, curb details, and ADA compliance parameters. READ for exact symbol definitions and maximum allowable slopes.\n*   **Block 3**: Benchmark specifications detailing the exact vertical control points (Mag Nail in Asphalt) for the site. READ for exact baseline elevation data.\n*   **Block 5**: Curb grading note detailing conditions for catch curbs vs. spill curbs. READ for grading flow instructions. \n*   **Block 6**: Tree list reference directing the user to landscape plan sheet 32. READ for sheet reference.\n*   **Block 4**: Legal description of the subject property (Lot 1, Mecey Subdivision). READ to confirm property identity.\n*   **Block 1**: Graphic scale bar. READ to confirm the 1\" = 20' measurement baseline.\n*   **Blocks 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14**: Boilerplate & Administrative information, including the Texas 811 call warning, engineer's seal (Jason K. Rodgers), project metadata (Sheet 11 of 39, Project No. RJ3 70496), title block, and standard utility and design disclaimers. READ for project details or administrative tracking; otherwise, these can be skipped during a technical review.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":38,"startLine":1,"totalLines":38}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776980659767,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01JgJQTWsm5MYyAn9xYMmnNp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I now have enough information to start my review. Let me summarize what I've found:\n\n## KEY FINDINGS - RESEARCH PHASE:\n\n### EXISTING OVERHEAD UTILITIES:\n1. **Valley View Road (Western Boundary):** Overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) run parallel to Valley View Road along the western property boundary with multiple utility poles and guy wires\n2. **Northern/Eastern Boundary:** Additional overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) run along the northern boundary (adjacent property \"LOT A CORTEZ HEIGHTS\")\n\n### PROPOSED SITE FEATURES NEAR OVERHEAD LINES:\n1. **Driveways:** Two main driveway entrances from Valley View Road cross directly beneath/adjacent to the overhead lines\n2. **Sidewalk:** A public 5' concrete sidewalk is planned along Valley View Road, directly in the same corridor as the overhead utility lines\n3. **Trees:** Mitigation trees (marked \"M\") are proposed along the southern boundary directly under/adjacent to the overhead electric line\n\n### PROPOSED TREES:\n**Shade Trees (for mitigation):**\n- 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) - 100 gal., 4\" cal.\n- 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) - 100 gal., 4\" cal.\n\n**Ornamental Trees (NOT for mitigation):**\n- 6 Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana)\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora)\n\n### REGULATORY REQUIREMENTS ON COVER SHEET:\n1. Electric Transmission Notes (Block 13 on Sheet 3): 16 specific requirements for electric transmission facilities\n2. Austin Energy Notes (Blocks 17 & 19 on Sheet 3): Requirements for tree pruning, easement maintenance, clearance responsibility\n3. NO 48-hour notification requirement noted on cover sheet or general notes\n\n\n---\n\nSeveral critical details are missing from the plan documentation. There are no elevation surveys showing actual conductor heights or vertical clearances above the driveways, and no profile sections to illustrate the vertical relationships between driveway grades and the overhead conductors. The plan lacks documented mid-span clearance data from surveyor measurements, and I don't see any building elevation sheets that would show conductor clearances relative to structures. Additionally, the 48-hour notification requirement isn't documented on the cover sheet or general notes pages, and there are no clearance dimensions marked on the site plan itself showing distances from conductors to buildings or driveways.\n\nThe overhead lines are labeled as \"O.H.U.L.\" but the plan doesn't clarify whether these are distribution or transmission lines. However, the grading plan references electric transmission facilities with 25-foot clearance requirements and transmission easement compliance language, which suggests transmission structures could be involved.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1593,"cache_read_input_tokens":79391,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1593,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8920d43-e944-47ba-ad17-2e6340f56c7c","uuid":"712b4336-847c-48fe-a8bd-e7d506a9a9f9"}
