cumentation of conductor locations and mid-span clearances."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.37","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["ECM § 2.4.1.D","ECM § 2.4.2.C","UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary; areas within 10-50 feet of overhead electric lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Landscape plan Sheet 31 shows mitigation trees (marked 'M') planted along the southern boundary directly adjacent to or within close proximity to overhead electric line marked '- OHE -'. Proposed shade trees consist of Cedar Elm (10 trees) and Live Oak (2 trees). Plant schedule specifies minimum 4-caliper cedar elm and live oak trees. Cannot verify from submitted documents whether Cedar Elm and Live Oak are marked as utility-compatible (UC) in ECM Appendix F. Additionally, lateral distances from tree planting locations to the overhead conductor centerline are not dimensioned on the landscape plan; visual analysis suggests trees are within 10-15 feet of the overhead line. Provide: (1) verification that proposed tree species are ECM Appendix F trees marked as utility-compatible (UC), and (2) dimensioned clearance measurements on landscape plan showing lateral distance from each tree location to outside conductor of overhead electric line to confirm 10-foot minimum distance for distribution conductors or 50-foot minimum distance for transmission conductors per UCM § 1.10.10.4."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-1.46","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.2"],"applicableAreas":["Entire site; all areas where construction will occur"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":1},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":3}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Overhead electric lines are present on or adjacent to the site along Valley View Road and northern boundary. Construction activities are proposed including grading, utility installation, building construction, and landscaping. Cover sheet and general notes do not include required note that owner/contractor must notify Austin Energy at least 48 hours before work begins near high-voltage overhead lines per Texas Health & Safety Code Chapter 752, Section 752.003. Add mandatory 48-hour notification requirement note to cover sheet."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1593,"cache_read_input_tokens":79391,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1593,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8920d43-e944-47ba-ad17-2e6340f56c7c","uuid":"f1db1a47-2797-42d5-963f-902dc48adcc9"}
