{"level":30,"time":1776980659767,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BubuU7jvjFZdEMWTWg7NRU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've submitted the findings. Let me make sure I've covered all the checklist items in the grouping. Looking back at the checklist in the grouping file (1.md), I see there are 47 checklist items total (EL-1.1 through EL-1.47).\n\nI've identified:\n- EL-1.1: not-verifiable (no elevation sheets)\n- EL-1.7: not-verifiable (no building elevation sheets)\n- EL-1.8: not-verifiable (no section views with dimensions)\n- EL-1.18: not-verifiable (no vertical clearance data for driveways)\n- EL-1.23: fail (no clearance dimensions shown)\n- EL-1.31: not-verifiable (no surveyor data for mid-span clearances)\n- EL-1.37: not-verifiable (trees near overhead lines without clearance verification)\n- EL-1.46: fail (missing 48-hour notification note)\n\nNow I need to verify I haven't missed any other items that should be flagged. Let me review the other items to ensure I mark them correctly:\n\nItems that should NOT have findings (based on my research):\n- EL-1.2: Radial clearance from overhead distribution primary/neutral - not verifiable because no clearance dimensions shown, but the core issue is covered under EL-1.23\n- EL-1.3: Building projections - same as EL-1.1/1.8\n- EL-1.4: Gas pump canopies - not applicable (no gas pumps proposed)\n- EL-1.5: Stairs, elevated walkways - not specifically shown or proposed\n- EL-1.6: Buildings in ROW - not applicable (buildings not in ROW)\n- EL-1.9: Fences - fences are shown but need to check clearances\n\n\n- EL-1.10: Fence posts and poles - need to verify if they meet clearance requirements\n- EL-1.11: Substation fences - no substation on site\n- EL-1.12: Transmission fencing - need to check if transmission exists and fencing meets requirements\n- EL-1.13: Vehicle barriers - not shown\n- EL-1.14: Retaining walls - shown on plan, need to check clearances\n- EL-1.15: Retaining walls at substation - no substation\n- EL-1.16: Emergency access structures - not proposed\n- EL-1.17: Retaining wall sections - would be covered under EL-1.14 if clearances are an issue\n- EL-1.19: Vehicle parking on pads - parking exists but positioned away from overhead lines\n- EL-1.20: Transmission line clearances for roads - only relevant if transmission lines are present\n- EL-1.21: Highway/freeway clearances - not applicable to this site\n- EL-1.22: Pole conflicts with driveways - verify whether existing poles require relocation\n- EL-1.24: Streetlight poles - confirm whether new streetlights are proposed under overhead lines\n- EL-1.25: Sidewalk/poles at property ends - planned sidewalk but existing poles already in place\n- EL-1.26: Trash areas under lines - determine if trash collection areas are located beneath overhead lines\n- EL-1.27: Facilities under/over distribution lines - general prohibition applies\n- EL-1.28: Water meters - verify clearances from overhead lines\n- EL-1.29: Water lines - check routing and clearances\n- EL-1.30: Foundations within 5 feet of property line - need to verify locations. Electric line crossings should occur at 90 degrees, and secondary lines crossing over primary lines need to be checked. No marquee signs are proposed, and new power poles aren't applicable. Decorative lighting may be present on the site. Meter obstruction needs verification, and existing streetlights require clearance confirmation. Down guy wires should be verified, with guy easements applying if transmission poles are involved and anchor easements if distribution poles exist. Proposed transformers need clearance verification, transformer niches aren't applicable, and construction staging areas aren't shown on plans.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"in