{"level":30,"time":1776980659768,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01DHfnt9M6NwVZEBhKGPizFt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my research, let me now evaluate all the checklist items. I have gathered sufficient evidence to determine the status of each item. Let me create a comprehensive analysis:\n\n## Summary of Research Findings\n\n**EXISTING OVERHEAD ELECTRIC INFRASTRUCTURE (from Sheet 4 - Existing Conditions Survey):**\n- Overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) run along the southern property boundary within a 10' electric easement\n- Multiple utility poles exist along Valley View Road (western frontage) and southern boundary\n- Existing overhead lines pass through numerous tree canopies\n\n**PROPOSED SITE DEVELOPMENT:**\n- Sheet 9 (Site Plan): Shows proposed concrete retaining wall running exactly along the southern property line where the overhead electric line exists\n- Sheet 9 Vision analysis: **NO explicit clearance dimensions shown** between proposed structures and the overhead electric line\n- Buildings 6 and 8 are near the southern overhead infrastructure  \n- Proposed sidewalks run parallel to the OHE line\n- Sheet 21 (Electrical Design): Shows proposed underground electrical service; utilities notes mention contractor shall verify existing utility locations but does not address clearances to overhead lines\n\n**LANDSCAPE PLAN (Sheet 31):**\n- Trees shown with canopies overlapping the overhead electric line\n- No species information on Sheet 31 itself\n- Vision analysis shows trees planted 10-20 feet from the overhead line with canopies extending into the OHE alignment\n- Mitigation trees (\"M\" tagged) present along southern boundary\n\n**TREE LIST (Sheet 32):**\n- Multiple tree species shown, need to verify utility-compatibility of those near OHE line\n- Species include Live Oak, Hackberry, Cedar Elm, Pecan, China Berry, Poplar, American Elm, Arizona Ash, Pine, Bradford Pear\n- Appendix F designation noted for each tree\n\n**GENERAL NOTES (Sheet 3):**\n- Block 19 (Electric Notes): States owner responsible for maintaining clearances per NESC, OSHA, COA, and Texas law\n- Block 13 (Electric Transmission Notes): Addresses transmission lines (if applicable) but focuses on 25-foot clearances from transmission structures\n- **NO 48-hour notification requirement note visible** on reviewed sheets\n\n**CRITICAL GAP:**\n- No surveyed conductor elevations provided on building elevation sheets\n- No section views showing vertical clearances from overhead lines to buildings, retaining wall, or sidewalks\n- No profile plans showing mid-span clearances\n- No dimensions verifying the 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from the outside conductor to the proposed retaining wall\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1377,"cache_read_input_tokens":78483,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1377,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11ce902f-86c5-4003-b16c-9143da511761","uuid":"a6390aa8-ae27-4fb1-a7c0-1cd85655d848"}
