{"level":30,"time":1776980659768,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01M1U4cPzR4dNUVdiJ48pakv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Evaluation Complete\n\nI have completed the site plan review for the **EL-MD-EXP grouping (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines)** for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n### Key Findings Summary\n\n**Research Conducted:**\n1. **Existing Conditions (Sheet 4):** Identified overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) running along the entire southern property boundary within a 10' electric easement, plus utility poles along Valley View Road frontage\n2. **Proposed Development (Sheets 9, 21, 38-39):** Proposed concrete retaining wall positioned along the southern property line where the overhead lines exist; no surveyed conductor elevations or clearance verification exhibits provided\n3. **Landscape Plan (Sheets 31-32):** Mitigation trees proposed near overhead line with canopies overlapping the line; tree species on landscape plan not identified, making utility-compatibility verification impossible\n4. **Electrical & General Notes (Sheets 3, 21):** Contractor directed to verify existing utilities and maintain clearances, but no specific clearance dimensions or 48-hour notification note included\n\n**Critical Gaps Identified:**\n- No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor locations\n- No profile plans showing vertical clearances between overhead line and proposed structures\n- No dimensions verifying 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor\n- No section views for retaining wall showing clearance from conductor\n- No tree species identification on landscape plan near overhead facilities\n- Missing 48-hour notification to Austin Energy requirement note\n\n**Total Deficiencies Found:** 11\n- **Fail (definitive non-compliance):** 2 items\n- **Not-Verifiable (insufficient evidence):** 9 items\n\nThe most critical deficiencies involve the proposed concrete retaining wall running directly along the property line where the existing overhead electric line is located, with no clearance verification provided."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4422,"cache_read_input_tokens":82917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4422,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"11ce902f-86c5-4003-b16c-9143da511761","uuid":"d522bf1f-cf90-4f79-a5c3-5537746d2c1c"}
{"level":30,"time":1776980659768,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":9,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":1724330,"duration_api_ms":174102,"num_turns":33,"result":"## Evaluation Complete\n\nI have completed the site plan review for the **EL-MD-EXP grouping (Site Feature Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines)** for the Valley View Townhomes project.\n\n### Key Findings Summary\n\n**Research Conducted:**\n1. **Existing Conditions (Sheet 4):** Identified overhead utility lines (O.H.U.L.) running along the entire southern property boundary within a 10' electric easement, plus utility poles along Valley View Road frontage\n2. **Proposed Development (Sheets 9, 21, 38-39):** Proposed concrete retaining wall positioned along the southern property line where the overhead lines exist; no surveyed conductor elevations or clearance verification exhibits provided\n3. **Landscape Plan (Sheets 31-32):** Mitigation trees proposed near overhead line with canopies overlapping the line; tree species on landscape plan not identified, making utility-compatibility verification impossible\n4. **Electrical & General Notes (Sheets 3, 21):** Contractor directed to verify existing utilities and maintain clearances, but no specific clearance dimensions or 48-hour notification note included\n\n**Critical Gaps Identified:**\n- No building elevation sheets with surveyed conductor locations\n- No profile plans showing vertical clearances between overhead line and proposed structures\n- No dimensions verifying 7.5-foot sky-to-ground clearance from outside conductor\n- No section views for retaining wall showing clearance from conductor\n- No tree species identification on landscape plan near overhead facilities\n- Missing 48-hour notification to Austin Energy requirement note\n\n**Total Deficiencies Found:** 11\n- **Fail (definitive non-compliance):** 2 items\n- **Not-Verifiable (insufficient evidence):*