cific observations from the plan drawing.","msg":"Calling vision tool: 1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777 (21)"}
{"level":30,"time":1776980659772,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BrEr1rZKefTDsoXftNuUu5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have sufficient information to complete my evaluation. Let me compile my findings for all checklist items in this grouping.\n\n## Summary of Research Findings\n\n**Evidence gathered:**\n1. **Sheet 31 (Landscape Plan)**: Shows overhead electric line (OHE) along southern boundary with approximately 5-6 proposed mitigation trees immediately adjacent\n2. **Measured distances** (from measure-distance tool): Trees measured at 0 feet, 1.7 feet, and 2.2 feet from the outside OHE conductor (far less than the 15-foot minimum for any trees)\n3. **Sheet 21 (Electrical Design Plan)**: Confirms OHE lines on western and southern boundaries; shows no voltage classification; appears to be distribution infrastructure (typical for residential)\n4. **Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations)**: Lists 10 Cedar Elm (100 gal.), 2 Live Oak (100 gal.), 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (45 gal.), and 6 Mexican Redbud (45 gal.) trees\n5. **Sheet 31 Legend**: Identifies trees as \"M\" (mitigation trees) but provides no species identification\n6. **No root barrier details**: Sheet 37 provides general tree planting details but no root barriers are specified for trees near underground utilities\n7. **No Austin Energy approval**: No written approval from Austin Energy visible in supplementary documents for trees within restricted clearance zones\n8. **Transformer pad distances**: Trees are 54+ feet from transformer pads (EL-2.7 passes)\n9. **No transmission infrastructure** evident on plans; no transmission easement on site (EL-2.2, 2.4, 2.5 not applicable)\n\n**NOT FOUND / COULD NOT VERIFY:**\n- Species identification on landscape plan itself (only on Sheet 35)\n- Differentiation of large trees (40+ ft mature height) on landscape plan\n- Root barrier specifications for trees within 20 feet of underground electric equipment\n- Tree clearances dimensioned on landscape plan (suggesting EL-2.12 & 2.13 not applicable)\n- Voltage classification of overhead electric infrastructure (but appears to be distribution per standard practice)\n- Austin Energy written approval for tree placement variations\n\nNow I'll provide the structured findings:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":746,"cache_read_input_tokens":75246,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":746,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8f27eabf-4e7e-4d33-b3eb-83a00ab44689","uuid":"80c09324-45f2-4ed2-a699-2c615a19a79e"}
{"level":30,"time":1776980659772,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01BrEr1rZKefTDsoXftNuUu5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U2UKbQX1CN3C6c5T3BrtUn","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"2","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.1","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary near Buildings 7 and 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed mitigation trees along the southern boundary are located 0 to 2.2 feet from the overhead electric (OHE) conductor, far below the required minimum 15 lateral feet clearance for all trees from distribution conductors. This applies regardless of species utility-compatibility status. At least five trees have been measured with clearances of 0 feet (directly on the OHE line) or 1.7-2.2 feet."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.3","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary near Buildings 7 and 8"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":35}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) including Cedar Elm and Live Oak are specified in the plant schedule and are located 0 to 2.2 feet from the overhead distribution conductor, far below the required minimum 25 lateral feet clearance for large trees. Cedar Elm and Live Oak are standard Austin landscape species with mature heights of 40-60 feet and 40-80 feet respectively."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary near Buildings 7 and 8 where utility poles are located on the OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed mitigation trees planted 0 to 2.2 feet from the overhead electric line clearly violate the 10 lateral feet minimum clearance from utility poles, as the OHE line contains multiple poles marked along the southern boundary."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan Sheet 31"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan does not identify the species of trees proposed near the overhead electric facilities along the southern boundary. Trees are marked only with the letter 'M' (mitigation tree) designation. While species are listed on Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations), the landscape plan itself does not provide common or scientific names, making it impossible to verify utility-compatibility status or mature height clearance compliance from the landscape plan alone."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan Sheet 31, southern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) are not differentiated from smaller trees on the landscape plan. All proposed mitigation trees along the southern boundary near the overhead electric line are marked identically as 'M' with no indication of mature height. Cedar Elm and Live Oak, both large tree species in the plant schedule, cannot be distinguished from smaller species on the plan."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.15","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4