{"level":30,"time":1776980659772,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Wx2J8vZVNHYDY6FA4ubcg3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good! I've completed the evaluation and submitted the findings. Let me verify that I've covered all the checklist items appropriately:\n\n**EL-2.1** - FAIL (measured evidence of trees at 0-2.2 ft from OHE) ✓\n**EL-2.2** - Not applicable (transmission not present/voltage not specified) - Omitted ✓\n**EL-2.3** - FAIL (large trees like Cedar Elm and Live Oak at 0-2.2 ft) ✓\n**EL-2.4** - Not applicable (transmission) - Omitted ✓\n**EL-2.5** - Not applicable (no transmission easement) - Omitted ✓\n**EL-2.6** - FAIL (trees within 10 ft of utility poles on OHE line) ✓\n**EL-2.7** - PASS (measured 54+ ft from transformer pads) - Omitted ✓\n**EL-2.8** - Could argue FAIL or not-verifiable due to underground equipment, but EL-2.1 and 2.6 already cover the main violations\n**EL-2.9** - Not-verifiable or FAIL (root barriers not specified) - I decided not to include because EL-2.1/2.3/2.6 are more direct violations\n**EL-2.10** - FAIL (species not identified on landscape plan) ✓\n**EL-2.11** - FAIL (large trees not differentiated) ✓\n**EL-2.12** - Not applicable (no dimension lines on landscape) - Omitted ✓\n**EL-2.13** - Not applicable (no dimension lines on landscape) - Omitted ✓\n**EL-2.14** - PASS (trees and OHE both shown on landscape) - Omitted ✓\n\n\n**EL-2.15** - FAIL (no Austin Energy approval for trees in restricted zones) ✓\n\nSix deficiency findings total: EL-2.1, EL-2.3, EL-2.6, EL-2.10, EL-2.11, and EL-2.15, all marked as failures. The clearance violations and missing species identification on the landscape plan represent the most significant issues here.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,