{"level":30,"time":1776980659772,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":4,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01Wx2J8vZVNHYDY6FA4ubcg3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have completed the site plan review for grouping 2 (Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines). \n\n## Summary\n\nThe review identified **six failing items** across the Valley View Townhomes landscape and electrical design plans:\n\n**Critical Clearance Violations:**\n- **EL-2.1 & EL-2.3**: Proposed trees along the southern boundary (near Buildings 7-8) are planted 0 to 2.2 feet from the overhead electric conductor, violating the 15-foot minimum clearance for all trees and 25-foot minimum for large trees (40+ ft mature height)\n- **EL-2.6**: Same trees violate the 10-foot pole setback requirement\n\n**Documentation Deficiencies:**\n- **EL-2.10**: Tree species are not identified on the landscape plan itself (only on a separate calculation sheet), making compliance verification impossible from the landscape plan alone\n- **EL-2.11**: Large trees (Cedar Elm and Live Oak, both 40+ ft mature height) are not differentiated from smaller species on the landscape plan\n- **EL-2.15**: No Austin Energy written approval is documented for the trees proposed within restricted clearance zones\n\n**Items Passing/Not Applicable:**\n- Transformer pad distances are adequate (54+ feet)\n- Trees and overhead electric facilities are shown together on the landscape plan\n- No transmission infrastructure apparent; transmission-related items do not apply\n\nThe structured findings have been submitted with specific sheet references, code citations, and detailed comments for each deficiency."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2080,"cache_read_input_tokens":75992,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_token