pectively."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.6","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["Southern property boundary near Buildings 7 and 8 where utility poles are located on the OHE line"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Proposed mitigation trees planted 0 to 2.2 feet from the overhead electric line clearly violate the 10 lateral feet minimum clearance from utility poles, as the OHE line contains multiple poles marked along the southern boundary."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.10","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan Sheet 31"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"The landscape plan does not identify the species of trees proposed near the overhead electric facilities along the southern boundary. Trees are marked only with the letter 'M' (mitigation tree) designation. While species are listed on Sheet 35 (Landscape Calculations), the landscape plan itself does not provide common or scientific names, making it impossible to verify utility-compatibility status or mature height clearance compliance from the landscape plan alone."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-2.11","status":"fail","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["Landscape Plan Sheet 31, southern boundary"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":31}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Large trees (mature height 40+ feet per ECM Appendix F) are not differentiated from smaller trees on the landscape plan. All proposed mitigation trees along the southern boundary near the overhead electric line are marked identically as 'M' with no indication of mature height. Cedar Elm and Live Oak, both large tree species in the plant schedule, cannot be dis