{"level":30,"time":1776981649437,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NbaAZfcaCyovGTbJDRFni2","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Sheet 19 — Utility Tap Plan\n     2→\n     3→Utility tap plan showing proposed water and wastewater connections.\n     4→\n     5→## Reading Guide\n     6→\n     7→This sheet contains the Utility Tap Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout and connection points for proposed water, wastewater, and storm drain lines across eight multi-family buildings. Its primary purpose is to define utility routing, drainage fixture unit (DFU) loads, pipe material specifications, and regulatory compliance notes for the site's wet utilities.\n     8→\n     9→**Key values:**\n    10→*   Private domestic water branches: 2\" HDPE service tubing\n    11→*   Private wastewater branches: 6\" PVC at a minimum 2.0% slope\n    12→*   Pressure reducing valve (PRV) set pressure threshold: 65 psi\n    13→*   Number of private fire hydrants on site: 1\n    14→*   Trench depth requiring geologist inspection: Greater than 5 feet\n    15→*   Drainage Fixture Units (DFUs): 4Plex = 136 DFUs, 5Plex = 170 DFUs, 6Plex = 204 DFUs\n    16→*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' (NAVD 88)\n    17→*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n    18→\n    19→**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n    20→\n    21→*   **Block 2**: The main site plan diagram showing buildings (Bldg. 1-8), utility routing (water, wastewater, storm drain), lift stations, cleanouts, and site topography. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, pipe routing, line lengths, and specific component locations.\n    22→*   **Block 1**: Legend defining the symbols and line types used for existing and proposed utilities (W, WW, RW, E, SD) in the main diagram. Use VISION to cross-reference symbols while reviewing Block 2.\n    23→*   **Block 13**: Utility notes specifying pipe materials and slopes for private domestic water and wastewater branches. READ for exact material sizes and installation standards.\n    24→*   **Block 7**: Drainage Fixture Unit Table breaking down the total DFU loads by building number and type (e.g., 4Plex, 5Plex, 6Plex). READ for specific sanitary load calculations.\n    25→*   **Block 17**: Benchmark data providing precise elevations and descriptions of vertical control points. READ for exact elevation values used for site grading and utility slopes.\n    26→*   **Block 10**: Water tap note outlining requirements for replacing existing Asbestos Cement (AC) pipe with Ductile Iron (DI) pipe and required hazardous disposal protocols. READ for regulatory compliance regarding existing AC lines.\n    27→*   **Block 11**: Special Services Division note mandating compliance with the Austin Fire Code for the site's private fire hydrant. READ for maintenance obligations and the exact private hydrant count.\n    28→*   **Block 5**: Technical note dictating the use of factory restrained joint pipes or mechanical joint restraint devices for all water line bends, tees, and valves. READ for specific structural requirements on water mains.\n    29→*   **Block 9**: PRV Note stipulating that any structure with water pressure at or above 65 psi must install a pressure reducing valve. READ for pressure management requirements.\n    30→*   **Block 19**: Geologist inspection requirement note triggered by the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule for deep trenching. READ for the specific trench depth threshold (5 feet).\n    31→*   **Blocks 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 14, 15, 16, 18, 20**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the project title block, engineering firm details, Texas 811 logo, legal description, disclaimers regarding utility locations, and a cross-reference to the landscape plan for trees. READ for general project administration and liability disclaimers if required.\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→All other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n    36→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94b43057-6c8d-4501-ab55-21f141703f72","uuid":"da601d66-cef6-4994-a976-240d3e5d3fe1","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/primary-site-plan/sheet-19/guide.md","content":"# Sheet 19 — Utility Tap Plan\n\nUtility tap plan showing proposed water and wastewater connections.\n\n## Reading Guide\n\nThis sheet contains the Utility Tap Plan for the Valley View Townhomes project, detailing the layout and connection points for proposed water, wastewater, and storm drain lines across eight multi-family buildings. Its primary purpose is to define utility routing, drainage fixture unit (DFU) loads, pipe material specifications, and regulatory compliance notes for the site's wet utilities.\n\n**Key values:**\n*   Private domestic water branches: 2\" HDPE service tubing\n*   Private wastewater branches: 6\" PVC at a minimum 2.0% slope\n*   Pressure reducing valve (PRV) set pressure threshold: 65 psi\n*   Number of private fire hydrants on site: 1\n*   Trench depth requiring geologist inspection: Greater than 5 feet\n*   Drainage Fixture Units (DFUs): 4Plex = 136 DFUs, 5Plex = 170 DFUs, 6Plex = 204 DFUs\n*   Benchmark #1 Elevation: 678.52' (NAVD 88)\n*   Benchmark #2 Elevation: 681.08' (NAVD 88)\n\n**Content blocks on this sheet:**\n\n*   **Block 2**: The main site plan diagram showing buildings (Bldg. 1-8), utility routing (water, wastewater, storm drain), lift stations, cleanouts, and site topography. Use VISION to examine the spatial layout, pipe routing, line lengths, and specific component locations.\n*   **Block 1**: Legend defining the symbols and line types used for existing and proposed utilities (W, WW, RW, E, SD) in the main diagram. Use VISION to cross-reference symbols while reviewing Block 2.\n*   **Block 13**: Utility notes specifying pipe materials and slopes for private domestic water and wastewater branches. READ for exact material sizes and installation standards.\n*   **Block 7**: Drainage Fixture Unit Table breaking down the total DFU loads by building number and type (e.g., 4Plex, 5Plex, 6Plex). READ for specific sanitary load calculations.\n*   **Block 17**: Benchmark data providing precise elevations and descriptions of vertical control points. READ for exact elevation values used for site grading and utility slopes.\n*   **Block 10**: Water tap note outlining requirements for replacing existing Asbestos Cement (AC) pipe with Ductile Iron (DI) pipe and required hazardous disposal protocols. READ for regulatory compliance regarding existing AC lines.\n*   **Block 11**: Special Services Division note mandating compliance with the Austin Fire Code for the site's private fire hydrant. READ for maintenance obligations and the exact private hydrant count.\n*   **Block 5**: Technical note dictating the use of factory restrained joint pipes or mechanical joint restraint devices for all water line bends, tees, and valves. READ for specific structural requirements on water mains.\n*   **Block 9**: PRV Note stipulating that any structure with water pressure at or above 65 psi must install a pressure reducing valve. READ for pressure management requirements.\n*   **Block 19**: Geologist inspection requirement note triggered by the Void and Water Flow Mitigation Rule for deep trenching. READ for the specific trench depth threshold (5 feet).\n*   **Blocks 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 14, 15, 16, 18, 20**: various — Boilerplate & Administrative. Contains the project title block, engineering firm details, Texas 811 logo, legal description, disclaimers regarding utility locations, and a cross-reference to the landscape plan for trees. READ for general project administration and liability disclaimers if required.\n\n---\n\nAll other block detail in `./blocks.md`\n","numLines":36,"startLine":1,"totalLines":36}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776981649437,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HDXa3SWfMsFoAch5d7vFPY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Good - Sheet 19 shows water, wastewater, and storm drain utilities. Let me now compile my final evaluation. Based on all the evidence I've gathered:\n\n**DEFINITIVE FINDINGS:**\n\n**FAILS (clear deficiencies that must be corrected):**\n\n1. **EL-13.37** - Transformer pad dimensions do NOT match AE Design-approved detail sheets (or are not provided at all)\n   - The electrical plan shows 4 transformer pads with only symbols; NO dimensions are labeled on any pad (e.g., 5'x5', 6'x6', 10'x10')\n   - NO Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets are provided in the submittal\n   - NO service type specification (single-phase or three-phase) is shown for any transformer\n   - This is a required document per UCM § 1.5.2.6 and § 1.18.0\n\n2. **EL-13.35** - Transformer easements not shown around pads\n   - The electrical plan (Sheet 21) does not delineate or dimension any transformer easements around the 4 transformer pad locations\n   - UCM § 1.10.3 and AE Design practice require transformer easements for accessibility\n   - These must be shown on the plan with dimensions\n\n**NOT-VERIFIABLE (cannot determine compliance from submitted evidence):**\n\nThe following items cannot be verified because required information is missing, not documented, or located on different sheets without cross-verification:\n\n1. **EL-13.6** - Window/door/ventilating duct clearances with inadequate lateral separation\n   - Requires 12-foot horizontal clearance for oil-filled equipment from windows/doors/ducts that are <12 ft from grade or with <5 ft lateral separation\n   - Equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is NOT specified on electrical plan\n   - Building elevations showing window/door/duct locations relative to transformer pads are NOT provided\n   - Lateral separations are not documented\n\n2. **EL-13.9** - Fire escape clearances (20 feet minimum for oil-filled)\n   - Equipment type NOT specified (oil-filled vs. dry-type)\n   - Building elevations showing fire escape locations relative to transformers NOT provided\n   - Distance from transformer pads to fire escapes not documented\n\n3. **EL-13.12** - Fire hydrant clearances (5 feet minimum)\n   - Fire hydrants are shown on Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan)\n   - Transformers are shown on Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan)\n   - No cross-sheet clearance documentation or dimensional verification\n   - Cannot determine if minimum spacing is met without explicit measurement between sheets\n\n4. **EL-13.19** - Fire lane clearances (15 feet minimum)\n   - Fire lanes and transformers appear on separate sheets (10 and 21 respectively) with no documented verification of spacing requirements\n\n5. **EL-13.21** - Water line clearances (5 feet minimum horizontal)\n   - Water utilities cross near transformer locations on Sheet 21 but lack profile views and dimensioned horizontal separation\n\n6. **EL-13.22** - Wastewater line clearances (5 feet minimum horizontal)\n   - Wastewater lines similarly cross near transformers without vertical separation details or dimensioned clearances\n\n7. **EL-13.23** - Storm drain line clearances (5 feet minimum horizontal)\n   - Storm drain utilities positioned near transformer locations on Sheet 21 but missing profile views and documented spacing\n\n8. **EL-13.25** - Other utility clearances (12 inches minimum horizontal and vertical)\n   - Multiple utilities adjacent to electrical routing lack profile documentation and vertical separation details\n\n9. **EL-13.31** - Cross-section drawings for vertical clearances in access paths\n   - No cross-sections provided to verify clearances through overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed access paths\n\n10. **EL-13.32** - Drainage direction for oil-filled transformer pads\n    - Equipment specifications (oil-filled versus dry-type) not clearly identified\n\n, and grading plan doesn't specify drainage flow direction at transformer pad locations\n\n11. **EL-13.36** - Electrical routing from transformer to meter 100% on private property\n    - Routing shown on Sheet 21 without explicit documentation confirming private property location or written verification from Austin Energy Design\n\nSummary of findings shows 2 items failing completely, 11 items unable to verify due to missing information or incomplete documentation, and 26 items passing requirements or not applicable to the scope.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9830,"cache_read_input_tokens":69522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9830,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94b43057-6c8d-4501-ab55-21f141703f72","uuid":"165ccd90-acda-441e-bd6b-f92c2e9a0009"}
{"level":30,"time":1776981649437,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HDXa3SWfMsFoAch5d7vFPY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on my comprehensive review of the site plan documents, I have gathered the evidence needed to evaluate this grouping. Let me compile my findings now.\n\n## Summary of Research Findings\n\n**CRITICAL GAPS IDENTIFIED:**\n\n1. **Transformer Pad Documentation:**\n   - 4 transformer pads shown on Sheet 21 with symbols only\n   - NO pad dimensions labeled (e.g., 5'x5', 6'x6', 10'x10')\n   - NO Austin Energy Design-approved detail sheets provided\n   - NO service type specified (single-phase or three-phase)\n   - NO access door orientation indicated\n\n2. **Easements & Property:**\n   - Transformers appear to be on private property (PASS)\n   - NO transformer easements shown on electrical plan\n   - Electrical routing from transformers to meters not explicitly documented as 100% private\n\n3. **Building Clearances:**\n   - Measured clearances: 5.7 to 67.3 feet from transformers to buildings (all exceed 5-foot minimum)\n   - SE transformer to Bldg 7: 5.7 feet (meets minimum at MEDIUM confidence)\n   - Hot-stick area clearances: 5.7 to 67.3 feet (all meet 10-foot minimum)\n   - Transformer to transformer distances: 65.4, 134.6, 260.2 feet (all exceed 5-foot minimum)\n\n4. **Utilities:**\n   - Water, wastewater, and storm drain lines shown crossing electrical routing on Sheet 21\n   - NO profile views provided for vertical separation\n   - NO clearance dimensions shown\n   - Equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) not specified\n\n5. **Trees & Vegetation:**\n   - Landscape plan (Sheet 31) shows trees but NO species identification\n   - NO root barrier details shown\n   - Trees on site but proximity to transformers not dimensioned\n\n6. **Fire Protection:**\n   - Fire hydrants on Sheet 10, transformers on Sheet 21 (not cross-verified)\n   - Fire lanes on Sheet 10, transformers on Sheet 21 (not cross-verified)\n   - Fire escape locations not shown relative to transformers\n\n7. **Missing Documents:**\n   - NO building elevations with window/door locations\n   - NO cross-section drawings for vertical clearances\n   - NO grading plan notes showing drainage direction at transformer locations\n   - NO Austin Energy Design approval documentation\n   - NO easement exhibit showing transformer locations overlaid with easements\n\n---\n\nNow I'll prepare my structured findings output:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9830,"cache_read_input_tokens":69522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9830,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94b43057-6c8d-4501-ab55-21f141703f72","uuid":"8293031e-6f6b-4e30-a593-d58e22af5fd4"}
{"level":30,"time":1776981649437,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":2,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01HDXa3SWfMsFoAch5d7vFPY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E3CDXKit13JXBGqyT7JETD","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"grouping":"13","findings":[{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.37","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.5.2.6","UCM § 1.18.0"],"applicableAreas":["all four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer pad dimensions not shown on electrical plan; no dimensions labeled for any of the four pads (e.g., 5'x5', 6'x6', 10'x10'). No Austin Energy Design-approved transformer pad detail sheets provided in submittal. Service type (single-phase or three-phase) not specified for any transformer. Provide specific pad dimensions for each transformer and submit proof of Austin Energy Design approval (ESPA or approved pad detail sheets) for the specified service type."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.35","status":"fail","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["all four transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Transformer easements not shown around any of the four transformer pads. Easement width required by Austin Energy for equipment accessibility is not delineated or dimensioned on the electrical plan. Show and dimension transformer easements around each pad per Austin Energy Design accessibility requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.6","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations adjacent to buildings with windows, doors, or ventilating ducts"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 12-foot horizontal clearance required from windows, doors, or ventilating ducts on adjacent buildings (for oil-filled equipment only if window/door/duct is less than 12 feet from grade or has less than 5 feet lateral separation). Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on electrical plan. Building elevations showing window and door locations relative to transformer pads are not provided. Lateral separations and vertical clearances not dimensioned. Submit building elevations with windows/doors/ducts clearly marked, transformer equipment specifications, and dimensions showing compliance with clearance requirements."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.9","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations if oil-filled equipment is used"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 20-foot horizontal/radial clearance from fire escapes or stairs serving as fire escapes required for oil-filled equipment. Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) not specified on electrical plan. Building elevations showing fire escape or fire exit stair locations relative to transformer pads are not provided. Distances not documented. Submit transformer equipment specifications and building elevations clearly showing fire escape/exit stair locations with dimensions demonstrating compliance with 20-foot clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 5-foot clearance required from fire hydrants. One private fire hydrant is shown on Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan), while transformer pads are shown on Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan). No cross-sheet clearance verification or dimensional documentation provided showing distance from each transformer to the fire hydrant. Provide clearance dimensions from all transformer pads to the fire hydrant location or submit a consolidated plan overlay clearly showing both features with distances marked."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 15-foot clearance from fire lanes required. Fire lanes are delineated on Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan), while transformer pads are shown on Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan). No cross-sheet documentation showing clearance distances from transformer pads to fire lanes. Provide dimensional clearance verification or submit a consolidated plan clearly showing both features with measurements confirming 15-foot separation from all transformers to fire lanes."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations adjacent to water utility lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance required from water lines. Water utility lines (marked 'W') are shown on electrical plan crossing near transformer locations, but clearance dimensions are not provided. No profile or vertical separation details shown for utility crossings. Provide utility plan with profile views showing 5-foot horizontal minimum clearance and appropriate vertical separation (minimum 12 inches per UCM § 1.10.5.A) from all transformer pads to water lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.22","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations adjacent to wastewater utility lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance required from wastewater lines. Wastewater utility lines are shown on electrical plan but clearance dimensions are not provided. No profile or vertical separation details shown for utility crossings. Provide utility plan with profile views showing 5-foot horizontal minimum clearance and appropriate vertical separation (minimum 12 inches per UCM § 1.10.5.A) from all transformer pads to wastewater lines."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.23","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations adjacent to storm drain lines"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 5-foot horizontal clearance required from storm drain lines. Storm drain lines and inlets (marked 'SD') are shown on electrical plan near transformer locations, but clearance dimensions are not provided. No profile or vertical separation details shown for utility conflicts. Provide utility plan with profile views showing 5-foot horizontal minimum clearance and appropriate vertical separation (minimum 12 inches per UCM § 1.10.5.A) from all transformer pads to storm drain infrastructure."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.25","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.5.A"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 12-inch horizontal and vertical clearance required from other underground utilities (except gas, fuel, and steam). Multiple utility lines are shown on electrical plan crossing near transformer locations, but clearance dimensions and profile details are not provided. Provide profile and plan views with clearance dimensions and details showing how underground utilities are separated vertically and horizontally from all transformer pad locations."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.31","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.3"],"applicableAreas":["access paths with overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas above transformer locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Cross-section drawings are required showing vertical clearances in access paths with overhead structures, parking garages, or enclosed areas. The site plan shows interior courtyard areas above transformer locations where vertical clearance verification is necessary. Cross-section drawings for vertical clearance compliance are not provided. Submit cross-section drawings showing the proposed transformer locations with vertical clearances to overhead structures, building overhangs, or any enclosed access areas."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.32","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 1"],"applicableAreas":["transformer pad locations if oil-filled equipment is used"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":11}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Grading and drainage must direct liquid flow away from buildings for oil-filled transformer equipment. Transformer equipment type (oil-filled vs. dry-type) is not specified on electrical plan. Grading plan (Sheet 11) does not specifically indicate surface drainage direction at transformer pad locations. Submit transformer equipment specifications indicating whether oil-filled or dry-type, and provide grading plan annotation with arrows showing drainage direction at all transformer locations confirming flow is directed away from adjacent buildings."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.36","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 1.10.4 Table 1.10.4 footnote 4"],"applicableAreas":["electrical routing from all four transformer pads to corresponding meters"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Electrical routing from transformer to meter must be 100% on private property. While electrical routing is shown on Sheet 21, there is no explicit documentation confirming that all routing from each of the four transformers to their corresponding meters is entirely on private property. Provide written documentation or an annotated plan clearly demonstrating that the entire electrical routing path from each transformer to its meter is 100% on private property, not crossing public right-of-way or easements."}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9830,"cache_read_input_tokens":69522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":9830,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"94b43057-6c8d-4501-ab55-21f141703f72","uuid":"1bb30ccf-1845-4fd4-a4ca-cda1b9ea66e2"}
