ided. Distances not documented. Submit transformer equipment specifications and building elevations clearly showing fire escape/exit stair locations with dimensions demonstrating compliance with 20-foot clearance requirement."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.12","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 5-foot clearance required from fire hydrants. One private fire hydrant is shown on Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan), while transformer pads are shown on Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan). No cross-sheet clearance verification or dimensional documentation provided showing distance from each transformer to the fire hydrant. Provide clearance dimensions from all transformer pads to the fire hydrant location or submit a consolidated plan overlay clearly showing both features with distances marked."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.19","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["Reviewer Convention"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer pad locations"],"sheetReferences":[{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":21},{"documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNumber":10}],"documentReferences":[],"comment":"Minimum 15-foot clearance from fire lanes required. Fire lanes are delineated on Sheet 10 (Fire Protection Plan), while transformer pads are shown on Sheet 21 (Electrical Plan). No cross-sheet documentation showing clearance distances from transformer pads to fire lanes. Provide dimensional clearance verification or submit a consolidated plan clearly showing both features with measurements confirming 15-foot separation from all transformers to fire lanes."},{"deficiencyId":"EL-13.21","status":"not-verifiable","codeCitations":["UCM § 2.9.1.B.2"],"applicableAreas":["all transformer 