{"level":30,"time":1776981649447,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":35,"prompt":"Review the plant schedule and landscaping calculation tables. Specifically identify: 1) The complete list of proposed shade trees, ornamental trees, and shrubs with their quantities and species names; 2) Any notation or callout indicating which trees are designated as mitigation trees; 3) Which tree species are shade trees vs ornamental trees vs other categories; 4) The mature height specifications provided for each species listed. Pay particular attention to the symbol definitions (SY, PL, P, M) and see if the plant schedule clarifies which plant species correspond to each symbol.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a detailed visual analysis of the provided landscape plan (Sheet 32 of 35), here is the specific information extracted regarding your requests:\n\n### 1 & 3) Complete List and Categorization of Proposed Trees and Shrubs\nThe \"PLANT LIST\" table categorizes the proposed plant material precisely into \"SHADE TREES\", \"ORNAMENTAL TREES\", and \"SHRUBS\" (along with Groundcovers, which are omitted below per your prompt). \n\n**SHADE TREES**\n*   **Live Oak** (*Quercus virginiana*) \n    *   Quantity: 2 \n    *   Min. Spec.: 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM, CONTAINER GROWN\n*   **Cedar Elm** (*Ulmus crassifolia*)\n    *   Quantity: 10 \n    *   Min. Spec.: 100 GAL., 4\" CAL., 16' HT. MINIMUM, CONTAINER GROWN\n\n*(Note: There is an entry with a quantity blank for \"EXISTING TREE, TO BE PRESERVED\" under the Shade Trees section).*\n\n**ORNAMENTAL TREES**\n*   **Texas Mountain Laurel** (*Sophora secundiflora*)\n    *   Quantity: 2 \n    *   Min. Spec.: 45 GAL., 2.5\" CAL., 8' HT. MINIMUM, CONTAINER GROWN\n*   **Mexican Redbud** (*Cercis canadensis var. mexicana*)\n    *   Quantity: 6 \n    *   Min. Spec.: 45 GAL., 2.5\" CAL., 10' HT. MINIMUM, CONTAINER GROWN\n\n**SHRUBS**\n*   **Dwarf Palmetto** (*Sabal minor*)\n    *   Quantity: 12\n    *   Container: 5 GALLON | Max Spacing: 4' O.C.\n*   **Big Muhly (1 gal)** (*Muhlenbergia lindheimeri*)\n    *   Quantity: 24\n    *   Container: 1 GALLON | Max Spacing: SEE PLANS\n*   **Gulf Muhly (1 Gallon)** (*Muhlenbergia capillaris 'Regal Mist'*)\n    *   Quantity: 28\n    *   Container: 1 GALLON | Max Spacing: 3' O.C.\n*   **Texas Sage** (*Leucophyllum frutescens 'Green Cloud'*)\n    *   Quantity: 8\n    *   Container: 7 GALLON | Max Spacing: 3' O.C.\n*   **Dwarf Wax Myrtle** (*Myrica cerifera 'Don's Dwarf'*)\n    *   Quantity: 8\n    *   Container: 7 GALLON | Max Spacing: 3' O.C.\n\n### 2) Mitigation Tree Notations\nThere are **no specific notations or callouts on individual tree species** in the \"PLANT LIST\" designating them as mitigation trees. \n\nInstead, mitigation is calculated aggregately in the tables on the right side of the page:\n*   Under **CITY OF AUSTIN TREE PRESERVATION CALCULATIONS**, the form lists:\n    *   `TOTAL MITIGATION INCHES PLANTED ON SITE: 55 INCHES`\n    *   `REMAINING MITIGATION INCHES REQUIRED: 182 INCHES`\n    *   `MITIGATION DEFICIT (REPLACE REMAINING AT STANDARD $200 PER INCH): $36,400`\n*   In the **COA REQUIRED TREES CHART**, the table breaks down the formula:\n    *   `Total tree inches required: A = 13`\n    *   `PER PLANT LIST (PROPOSED): 12 @ 4\" \\ 8 @ 2.5\" | B = 68` (This correlates exactly to the 12 Shade Trees @ 4\" and 8 Ornamental Trees @ 2.5\" from the Plant List).\n    *   `PROPOSED TREE INCHES THAT MAY BE COUNTED FOR MITIGATION: C = 55` (Which is B minus A).\n\n### 4) Mature Height Specifications\n**Mature height specifications are NOT provided** for any species on this document. \n\nThe \"MIN. SPEC.\" column in the Plant List only provides the **minimum installation height** required at the time of planting:\n*   Live Oak: `16' HT. MINIMUM`\n*   Cedar Elm: `16' HT. MINIMUM`\n*   Texas Mountain Laurel: `8' HT. MINIMUM`\n*   Mexican Redbud: `10' HT. MINIMUM`\n\n### 5) Symbol Definitions (SY, PL, P, M)\nThe text symbols **SY, PL, P, and M do not appear anywhere on this page.** \n\nInstead of alphanumeric codes, the \"PLANT LIST\" utilizes **graphic icons** (located in the \"SYM.\" column) to correspond plant species to the site plan map. These symbols include:\n*   A circle with a plus sign (`+`) for Live Oak.\n*   A circle with a cross/dot pattern for Cedar Elm.\n*   A scalloped circle shape for Texas Mountain Laurel.\n*   A multi-circle cluster/blob shape for Mexican Redbud.\n*   Various smaller circle patterns (hatched, dots, lines) for the shrubs.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1423,"outputTokens":1151,"totalTokens":6150,"reasoningTokens":3576},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 2584864]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Review the plant schedule and landscaping calculation tables. Specifically identify: 1) The complete list of proposed shade trees, ornamental trees, and shrubs with their quantities and species names; 2) Any notation or callout indicating which trees are designated as mitigation trees; 3) Which tree species are shade trees vs ornamental trees vs other categories; 4) The mature height specifications provided for each species listed. Pay particular attention to the symbol definitions (SY, PL, P, M) and see if the plant schedule clarifies which plant species correspond to each symbol."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-QX1SVA9fXH9HqYdi8plq7vN9","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-headers":"Content-Type, Authorization, ai-gateway-auth-method, ai-gateway-protocol-version, ai-model-id, ai-language-model-id, ai-language-model-specification-version, ai-image-model-specification-version, ai-embedding-model-specification-version, ai-language-model-streaming, ai-reporting-tags, ai-reporting-user, http-referer, x-title, anthropic-beta","access-control-allow-methods":"GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE, OPTIONS","access-control-allow-origin":"*","cache-control":"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate","content-encoding":"br","content-type":"application/json","date":"Thu, 23 Apr 2026 21:42:20 GMT","server":"Vercel","strict-transport-security":"max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload","transfer-encoding":"chunked","vary":"rsc, next-router-state-tree, next-router-prefetch, next-router-segment-prefetch","x-matched-path":"/v1/ai/language-model","x-vercel-cache":"MISS","x-vercel-id":"iad1::iad1::5rbpm-1776980473680-726c17401200"},"body":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based o