c Line\"** enters the site from the West (Valley View Road), connects to an \"Electrical Pull Box,\" and then routes to the Northwest transformer pad. From there, the main line routes East (along the north side of the buildings) to serve the Eastern transformer pad, and South (along the west side) to serve the Southwest transformer pad. Dashed blue lines route from the pads/pull boxes to \"Electrical Meters\" at the various buildings.\n*   **Proximity to other utilities:** Yes, other underground utilities are shown in proximity.\n    *   Lines labeled **\"W\"** (Water), **\"WW\"** (Wastewater), and **\"SD\"** (Storm Drain) are visible across the site.\n    *   The blue \"Underground Electric Line\" visibly crosses over/under \"W\", \"WW\", and \"SD\" lines at various points to reach the pads.\n*   **Separation:** While the utilities are shown in proximity and crossing each other, **there are no dimensioned labels indicating specific minimum separation distances** (e.g., \"5' min. separation\") between the electrical lines/pads and the water, wastewater, or storm drain lines on this specific sheet.\n\n**6. Access Door Orientation and Hot-Stick Clearance Area**\n*   **No, there is no indication of access door orientation or hot-stick clearance areas.**\n*   The transformer pads are drawn as simple, empty geometric rectangles. There are no distinct lines indicating a door side, nor are there any dashed lines, arcs, or text notes defining a required clear zone or hot-stick clearance area in front of any of the three pads.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1673,"outputTokens":1105,"totalTokens":5219,"reasoningTokens":2441},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","resolvedProvider":"vertex","resolvedProviderApiModelId"