{"level":30,"time":1776981694764,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KXqvNq5gDR3sb1cNcLexdY","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Electric Review\n     2→\n     3→*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n     4→\n     5→Electric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n     6→\n     7→See Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\n     8→Link: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\n     9→Applicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n    10→\n    11→Site Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\n    12→Austin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n    13→* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n    14→* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n    15→* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n    16→* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n    17→* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n    18→* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n    19→* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n    20→* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n    21→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f2d0cbc-d0ea-481e-8f7b-51f5d8083c45","uuid":"63232803-3be3-4080-8b10-176d9e5e9d59","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/vercel/sandbox/workspace/projects/63cead15-41f8-418c-b0ef-bd5c2b44719a/supplementary-docs/master-comment-report/02-electric-review.md","content":"# Electric Review\n\n*Lists the preliminary design requirements and links for Austin Energy review comments.*\n\nElectric Review – Rosemary Avila (512) 972-8488 - rosemary.avila@austinenergy.com\n\nSee Bluebeam link below to download AE site comments:\nLink: https://studio.bluebeam.com/share/epcafnizivuefw\nApplicant, for your comment responses use the color BLUE.\n\nSite Plan Preliminary Design Requirements\nAustin Energy Design Criteria Effective December 12th, 2023\n* UCM § 1.3.8 - Customer Electrical Facilities that Cross Property Lines\n* UCM § 1.3.12 - AE Line Extension Policy\n* UCM § 1.3.16- Truck Access to AE Construction and Existing Facility Sites\n* UCM § 1.9.3 - Installation of Metering Equipment\n* UCM § 1.10.3 - Permanent Clearances from AE Overhead Lines and Facilities\n* UCM § 1.10.4 - Clearances from AE Padmount Equipment and Distribution Vaults\n* UCM § 1.10.10.3 & 4 - Customer Activity in Utility Easements - Landscaping & Trees\n* Appendix F of the Environmental Criteria Manual\n","numLines":21,"startLine":1,"totalLines":21}}}
{"level":30,"time":1776981698864,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"1.md","index":3,"runIndex":"run-1","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01VzCuKEQdUVNVDBLDvMFEFg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The wall plan detail sheet doesn't show the overall site location of walls relative to property boundaries or overhead lines. I need to check the grading plan which showed the overall site layout with walls. Let me verify whether retaining walls are near the overhead lines by going back to the grading plan or site plan.\n\nFrom my earlier review of the site plan (Sheet 9), I saw \"Concrete Retaining Wall\" structures along various property boundaries. Let me check if any of these are near the overhead lines on the western (Valley View Road) or southern boundaries.\n\nBased on my earlier vision analysis of Sheet 9, I noted that retaining walls are mapped \"internally and along the rear/side boundaries\" but there was no specific detail about whether they are near the overhead lines.\n\nSince I cannot definitively determine from the plans whether retaining walls are located in proximity to the overhead electric lines that would trigger EL-1.14 or EL-1.17 compliance requirements, I should mark those as \"not-verifiable\" if there's ambiguity, but actually looking back at the application grouping, those items are only applicable \"when retaining walls are proposed adjacent to or within clearance distance of overhead electric facilities.\"\n\nSince the retaining walls shown are located internally or along boundaries, and the overhead lines are specifically on the western boundary and southern boundary, I need to verify the exact locations from the grading or site plan.\n\nActually, from the landscape plan vision, I saw \"Existing Stone Retaining Wall\" mentioned as a feature on the property. And from the wall plan, I see both existing walls and new pond walls referenced.\n\nThe issue is: are any of these walls within the clearance distance of the overhead electric lines? For EL-1.14 and EL-1.17, I would need to confirm that retaining walls are specifically proposed near the overhead lines to trigger those items.\n\nLet me reconsider: The overhead lines are on Valley View Road (western boundary) and on the northern boundary. The site plan shows buildings and parking set back from these boundaries. \n\nRetaining walls would typically be positioned along drainage features or property lines rather than directly beneath overhead lines. Since I can't clearly establish that any walls conflict with the electric lines, EL-1.14 and EL-1.17 don't appear applicable. For EL-1.45 regarding construction staging areas, the plans don't show a dedicated staging area layout, making this item not-verifiable unless one is specifically depicted.\n\nLooking at the evaluation criteria, items only count as failures or not-verifiable when they're actually applicable based on what's proposed. Features that aren't part of the project get marked as n/a and excluded from findings. I've narrowed down to 8 items that are either failing or cannot be verified. Everything else either doesn't apply because those elements aren't being constructed, or it passes review.\n\nWait—I should double-check EL-1.2 since the sheet analysis indicated transformers are planned. I need to confirm whether those transformers maintain the required 15-foot radial clearance from distribution lines.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":68125,"cache_read_input_tokens":19314,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":68125,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8920d43-e944-47ba-ad17-2e6340f56c7c","uuid":"be8e5340-72bd-4c9d-87ae-9eabe0a3811a"}
