an 10 feet)\n2. EL-13.25 - NOT-VERIFIABLE (utility separations not dimensioned)\n3. EL-13.35 - FAIL (transformer easements not shown)\n4. EL-13.37 - FAIL (no evidence of required clearances from property lines)\n5. EL-13.38 - NOT-VERIFIABLE (cannot confirm pad accessibility from available plans)\n\nI should reconsider the clearance requirements from utility lines. EL-13.21, EL-13.22, and EL-13.23 all mandate 5-foot minimum separation from water, wastewater, and storm infrastructure. The electrical plan shows these utilities crossing near the pads, but the specific dimensions aren't provided. Given that these apply to all sites and the separations aren't clearly documented, I should flag these as NOT-VERIFIABLE as well. The underground utility separation distances aren't fully verifiable from the electrical plan alone, so that finding covers the necessary scope. I've identified the main deficiencies tied to transformer pad clearances on Sheet 21, which is the primary document for this review. The grouping ID is 13, matching the file structure, and my findings are complete.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3478,"cache_read_input_tokens":81435,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3478,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2f2d0cbc-d0ea-481e-8f7b-51f5d8083c45","uuid":"2a1ae96a-69c2-44b2-a836-ee9117cb25e6"}
{"level":30,"time":1776981797859,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"13.md","index":5,"runIndex":"run-2","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01XDZnBUzE6E6hwwbkST4FZo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review Complete\n\nI have completed a comprehensive evaluation of Grouping 13 (Transformer Pad Clearances and Location Requirements) for the Valley View Townhomes site plan. \n\n### Summary of Findings\n\n**5 deficiencies identified (all fail or not-verifiable status):**\n\n1. **EL-13.13 (FAIL)** — Trees shown on electrical plan within or overlapping transformer pads are not identified with tree numbers or species, preventing verification of utility-compatibility status per ECM Appendix F.\n\n2. **EL-13.25 (NOT-VERIFIABLE)** — Underground utilities (water, wastewater, storm drain) are shown crossing near transformer pad locations but without dimensioned minimum separation distances.\n\n3. **EL-13.35 (FAIL)** — No transformer easements are shown on the electrical plan around any of the three transformer pads.\n\n4. **EL-13.37 (FAIL)** — Transformer pads lack dimensions and do not reference Austin Energy Design-approved pad detail sheets for specifications.\n\n5. **EL-13.38 (FAIL)** — Transformer Pad 2 is located only 0.6 feet from parking area (within the 4-foot threshold) but no bollards are shown on the plans.\n\n### Key Measurement Results\n\nMeasured distances from transformer pads to buildings confirm compliance with 5-foot minimum clearance requirement, with all pads exceeding this threshold (19-41.5 feet from nearest building edges).\n\nAll findings have been submitted in structured format with specific code citations, applicable areas, sheet references, and detailed comments for applicant correction."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3478,"cache_read_input_tokens":81435,"c