{"level":30,"time":1776981798784,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","documentId":"1144b126-1216-4dee-a89c-178950fa7777","sheetNum":31,"prompt":"On Sheet 31, examine the key notes legend (Block 5) that defines the tree symbols. Specifically, identify: 1) The symbols for SY (Street Yard tree), PL (Parking Lot tree), P (point tree), and M (Mitigation tree); 2) Any other tree symbols visible on the map; 3) Whether there is a clear visual legend that connects these letter abbreviations to the circular symbols shown on the main drawing; 4) For the trees positioned along the southern OHE line that you identified earlier (the ones marked with \"M\"), cross-reference their symbol appearance with the legend to confirm they are truly mitigation trees. The legend should clarify which symbol type corresponds to which tree category.","res":{"steps":[{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on a careful visual analysis of the provided image (noting that the title block indicates this is sheet \"28 of 35\", not Sheet 31 as mentioned in the prompt), here are the findings regarding the Key Notes legend and tree symbols:\n\n**1) Identification of symbols for SY, PL, P, and M:**\nUnder the \"KEY NOTES:\" section on the right side of the document, below the numbered graphics (H-1 through H-7), there is a text-only list defining these abbreviations. **There are no graphical tree symbols (e.g., circles with specific patterns) provided next to these definitions in the legend.** The text reads exactly as follows:\n\n*   \"SY - STREET YARD TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"PL - PARKING LOT TREE (EXCESS OF 1.5 CAL. INCH COUNTING TOWARDS MITIGATION)\"\n*   \"P - PARKING BUFFER POINT TREE\"\n*   \"M - MITIGATION TREE\"\n\n**2) Any other tree symbols visible on the map:**\nThe main drawing utilizes generic circular graphics to represent trees. These vary slightly in size and style (mostly open circles with a center crosshair or '+' mark, some with smaller inner circles, and a few with shaded inner circles located in the grey H-2 area on the left). To differentiate tree types, the plan relies on placing text tags directly next to or inside these generic circular symbols on the map itself (e.g., a circle with an \"M\", \"SY\", \"PL\", or a combination like \"SY+M\" next to its center point).\n\n**3) Presence of a clear visual legend connecting abbreviations to circular symbols:**\n**No.** There is no clear visual legend that links specific, distinct circular graphic symbols to these letter abbreviations. The \"legend\" provided for trees is strictly an abbreviation glossary. The reader must look for the text tags attached to the generic tree graphics on the plan to determine the tree's classification.\n\n**4) Cross-referencing \"M\" trees along the southern OHE line:**\nLocating the southern property boundary line marked with \"OHE\" and \"LOC\", there are tree symbols situated near the bottom right area along this line. These generic tree circles are explicitly labeled on the plan with the letter \"M\" near their center marks. Because there are no distinct graphical symbols in the legend to cross-reference their *appearance* against, you cannot confirm they are mitigation trees by their visual shape/pattern. However, you *can* confirm they are intended to be mitigation trees because the explicit text tag \"M\" applied to them on the drawing corresponds directly to the definition \"M - MITIGATION TREE\" in the Key Notes text list.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1459,"outputTokens":579,"totalTokens":3669,"reasoningTokens":1631},"warnings":[],"request":{"body":{"prompt":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"file","mediaType":"image/jpeg","data":"[BINARY_DATA_REMOVED - length: 1755680]"},{"type":"text","text":"# Your task\n\nYou are analyzing a subset of a real estate development site plan submission document.\n\nVisually analyze the binary file provided with extreme accuracy. Pay close attention to tables, reproducing them EXACTLY as they appear, character-by-character.\n\nCRITICAL: Do not paraphrase, interpret, or \"fill in\" text. If you cannot read something clearly, state \"text unclear\" rather than guessing. Transcribe field labels and values exactly as written.\n\nIf the requirements being validated require certain content to be present, look closely for it and provide all relevant information that pertains to the broader request. Remember that you are only looking at a single supplementary document, or a single page from the primary site plan. Just because you do not find evidence for a requirement on this page does not mean it will not be present on another page.\n\nReport back precisely on what you see, using exact quotes for any text you transcribe from forms, tables, or labels.\n\nThe final review agent will not be able to look at this document directly, so you must be their eyes. Ensure you describe everything relevant in full detail with perfect accuracy.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"On Sheet 31, examine the key notes legend (Block 5) that defines the tree symbols. Specifically, identify: 1) The symbols for SY (Street Yard tree), PL (Parking Lot tree), P (point tree), and M (Mitigation tree); 2) Any other tree symbols visible on the map; 3) Whether there is a clear visual legend that connects these letter abbreviations to the circular symbols shown on the main drawing; 4) For the trees positioned along the southern OHE line that you identified earlier (the ones marked with \"M\"), cross-reference their symbol appearance with the legend to confirm they are truly mitigation trees. The legend should clarify which symbol type corresponds to which tree category."}]}],"headers":{"user-agent":"ai/5.0.152"}}},"response":{"id":"aitxt-dKQdgngQpWlUTujkRqBfpmYf","timestamp":{},"modelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","headers":{"access-control-allow-heade