ly in size and style (mostly open circles with a center crosshair or '+' mark, some with smaller inner circles, and a few with shaded inner circles located in the grey H-2 area on the left). To differentiate tree types, the plan relies on placing text tags directly next to or inside these generic circular symbols on the map itself (e.g., a circle with an \"M\", \"SY\", \"PL\", or a combination like \"SY+M\" next to its center point).\n\n**3) Presence of a clear visual legend connecting abbreviations to circular symbols:**\n**No.** There is no clear visual legend that links specific, distinct circular graphic symbols to these letter abbreviations. The \"legend\" provided for trees is strictly an abbreviation glossary. The reader must look for the text tags attached to the generic tree graphics on the plan to determine the tree's classification.\n\n**4) Cross-referencing \"M\" trees along the southern OHE line:**\nLocating the southern property boundary line marked with \"OHE\" and \"LOC\", there are tree symbols situated near the bottom right area along this line. These generic tree circles are explicitly labeled on the plan with the letter \"M\" near their center marks. Because there are no distinct graphical symbols in the legend to cross-reference their *appearance* against, you cannot confirm they are mitigation trees by their visual shape/pattern. However, you *can* confirm they are intended to be mitigation trees because the explicit text tag \"M\" applied to them on the drawing corresponds directly to the definition \"M - MITIGATION TREE\" in the Key Notes text list.","providerMetadata":{"google":{"thoughtSignature":""}}}],"finishReason":"stop","usage":{"inputTokens":1459,"outputTokens":579,"totalTokens":3669,"reasoningTokens":1631},"warnings":[],"providerMetadata":{"google":{"promptFeedback":null,"groundingMetadata":null,"urlContextMetadata":null,"safetyRatings":null,"serviceTier":null},"gateway":{"routing":{"originalModelId":"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview","