{"level":30,"time":1776981835080,"pid":122,"hostname":"0067a724-a36","step":"review-runs","item":"2.md","index":7,"runIndex":"run-3","type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01GxKU5FEvDB2kcorJWhYqCd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Let me now compile my research findings and evaluate each checklist item. Let me create a summary of my research before I determine the final status for each item.\n\n## Research Summary - Tree Clearances from Overhead Electric Lines\n\n**Key Finding - Critical Distance Measurements:**\nUsing the measure-distance tool on the Landscape Plan (Sheet 31), I measured the distances from four mitigation trees (\"M\" designated) along the southern boundary to the overhead electric (OHE) line:\n- Tree 1 (southeast cluster, first): 1.3 feet from OHE\n- Tree 2 (southeast cluster, second): 3 feet from OHE  \n- Tree 3 (southeast cluster, third): 0 feet from OHE (ON the line)\n- Tree 4 (southeast corner): 0.5 feet from OHE\n\nPer UCM § 1.10.10.4, overhead distribution line clearances require:\n- **< 15 feet lateral**: Only utility-compatible (UC) trees permitted\n- **15-25 feet**: UC trees OR trees with mature height < 40 feet\n- **> 25 feet**: All trees permitted\n\n**Tree Species Information:**\nThe Landscape Calculations sheet (Sheet 35) lists proposed species:\n- 10 Cedar Elm (Ulmus crassifolia) @ 4\" caliper, 100 gal., 16' minimum height\n- 2 Live Oak (Quercus virginiana) @ 4\" caliper, 100 gal., 16' minimum height  \n- 6 Mexican Redbud (Cercis canadensis var. mexicana) @ 2.5\" caliper, 45 gal., 10' minimum\n- 2 Texas Mountain Laurel (Sophora secundiflora) @ 2.5\" caliper, 45 gal., 8' minimum\n\n**Critical Deficiencies Identified:**\n1. The landscape plan shows mitigation trees (\"M\" designations) at 0-3 feet from the southern OHE line\n2. The landscape plan does NOT identify the species of individual tree symbols - only generic \"M\" labels  \n3. No UC (utility-compatible) designations are provided for any proposed species on the landscape plan\n4. No mature height information is provided on the landscape plan (only installation minimum heights)\n5. No documented Austin Energy approval found for trees in restricted zones\n6. Large trees (40+ feet mature height per ECM Appendix F) are not differentiated on the landscape plan\n\nNow let me evaluate each checklist item:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1226,"cache_read_input_tokens":65732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1226,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b4bf1903-670d-4b71-b534-95d04a5dca76","uuid":"ea0829fd-1eb7-4631-be9e-bd39e1b5c749"}
